var e={tone:5,_encoded:`core,little_vespers,great_vespers,nocturns,matins,liturgy,vespers_weekday.sun,vespers_weekday.mon,vespers_weekday.tue,vespers_weekday.wed,vespers_weekday.thu,vespers_weekday.fri,compline.sun,compline.mon,compline.tue,compline.wed,compline.thu,compline.fri,compline.sat,matins_weekday.mon,matins_weekday.tue,matins_weekday.wed,matins_weekday.thu,matins_weekday.fri,matins_weekday.sat,liturgy_weekday.mon,liturgy_weekday.tue,liturgy_weekday.wed,liturgy_weekday.thu,liturgy_weekday.fri,liturgy_weekday.sat`.split(`,`),troparion:{text:`Let us, O faithful, praise and worship the Word * Who is co-beginningless with the Father and the Spirit, * and Who was born of the Virgin for our salvation; * for He was pleased to ascend the Cross in the flesh * and to endure death, ** and to raise the dead by His glorious Resurrection.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, if-no-Vigil (CANONICAL print, §9.5 convention)`},provenance_note:`Verified word- and pointing-identical at all four print sites (LV dismissal, GV no-vigil, Matins God-is-the-Lord, Liturgy); quotation-mark variance at: none. Canonical field stores the GV print per the §9.5 ruling.`},dismissal_theotokion:{text:`Rejoice, impassible portal of the Lord! * Rejoice, rampart and protection of those who have recourse unto thee! * Rejoice, haven untouched by storms, * and who knowing not wedlock, * didst bear in the flesh thy Creator and God. * Cease not to intercede for those ** who praise and worship thine Offspring.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, if-no-Vigil (verified identical at the Matins God-is-the-Lord site)`}},kontakion:{text:`Thou didst descend into Hades, O my Savior, * and having shattered its gates, as All-powerful, * Thou didst raise the dead with Thyself, as Creator, * and didst deliver Adam from the curse, * O Lover of mankind. ** Therefore, we all cry to Thee: “Save us, O Lord!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins after Ode VI (verified identical at the Liturgy site)`}},ikos:{text:`When the women heard the angel’s words, they cast away their lamentation and became radiantly joyful, trembling as they beheld the Resurrection. Christ drew near to them saying “Come and see, Rejoice! take courage, I have overcome the world and set free the prisoners held in the bondage of Hades. Hurry then to the disciples, and take unto them this message: Lo, I go before you to preach in the cities of Galilee.” Wherefore we all cry unto Thee: Save us, O Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, after Ode VI`},sourceLabel:`Ikos`},little_vespers:{rubric:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 4 Stichera:`,lic:[{text:`By Thy precious Cross, O Christ, * Thou hast shamed the devil, * and by Thy Resurrection Thou hast blunted the sting of sin, * and saved us from the gates of death: ** we glorify Thee, the only-begotten One.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Little Vespers, LIC sticheron position 1`}},{text:`By Thy precious Cross, O Christ ...,`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Little Vespers, LIC sticheron position 2 (incipit repeat of position 1, §2.7, printed with an explicit "Repeat:" label)`},incipit_ref:`tone5.little_vespers.lic[0]`,sourceLabel:`Repeat:`},{text:`He Who hath granted Resurrection to mankind, * was led as a sheep to the slaughter; * the princes of Hades trembled before Him * and the gates of lamentations were lifted up; * for Christ the King of glory entered therein, * saying to those in bondage: “Come forth!” ** and to those in darkness: “Reveal yourselves!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Little Vespers, LIC sticheron position 3`}},{text:`O great wonder! * Having suffered in the flesh through His love for mankind, * the Creator of all things visible and invisible, * hath arisen as immortal. * Come O ye descendents of the nations, * let us worship Him; * for delivered from deception by His compassion, ** we have learned to hymn one God in three Hypostases.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Little Vespers, LIC sticheron position 4`}}],lic_verses:[{text:`From the morning watch until night, from the morning watch * let Israel hope in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Little Vespers, LIC verse 1`}},{text:`For with the Lord there is mercy, and with Him is plenteous redemption; * and He shall redeem Israel out of all his iniquities.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Little Vespers, LIC verse 2`}},{text:`O praise the Lord, all ye nations; * praise Him, all ye peoples`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Little Vespers, LIC verse 3`}},{text:`For He hath made His mercy to prevail over us, * and the truth of the Lord abideth forever.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Little Vespers, LIC verse 4`}}],lic_theotokion:{text:`Let us honor the God-worthy and honorable maiden, * more honorable than the cherubim. * For the Creator of all things, having deigned to become a man * ineffably made His abode within her. * O strangest of deeds and wondrous mysteries! * Who would not be amazed upon hearing that God hath become a man? * Yet there was no change in Him, * having passed through the gates of virginity without diminishing it, * as the prophet hath said; * No man shall ever pass through this gate, ** except the Lord, the God of Israel, who hath great mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Little Vespers, LIC Glory/Both-now Theotokion`}},prokeimenon:{ref:`shared.saturday_vespers_prokeimenon`,rubric:`The Prokeimenon: “The Lord is King ...,” with its verses.`},aposticha:{resurrection:[{text:`With voices of song we magnify Thee, O Christ, * the Savior incarnate, * yet not separated from heaven, * for as the Lord who lovest mankind * Thou hast suffered the Cross and death for the sake of our race, * overthrowing the gates of Hades, * and rising on the third day, ** saving our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Little Vespers, aposticha Resurrection sticheron (as printed here — differs from the GV print, §2.2)`}}],theotokos:[{text:`My hands I stretch out towards thee, * my unclean lips I open in supplication, * I bend the knee of my heart and in spirit I now touch thy most pure feet, O pure Virgin, * falling down before thee. * Heal my pains and, in thy loving- kindness, * treat my many and incurable wounds. * Deliver me from adversaries visible and invisible. * Lighten the burden of my sloth, * that I may praise and glorify thee ** through whom the world hath found God’s great mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Little Vespers, aposticha Theotokos sticheron 1`}},{text:`Rejoice, O all-immaculate Virgin, * beyond telling thou didst conceive and give birth in the flesh * to the Son of God, * who from thy blood truly took that which is ours, * with a soul that was rational and possessing free will. * For having put on the cloth of Adam yet without defect, * He refashioned and saved mankind. * Therefore Christ is proclaimed to us as being in two natures, * showing in Himself the characteristics of them both. ** Implore Him that His great mercy be granted unto our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Little Vespers, aposticha Theotokos sticheron 2`}},{text:`Rejoice!, thou beauty of Jacob, * whom God hath chosen and loved; * door of the saved, flame-bearing tongs, * abolition of the curse, O most blessed maiden. * Thou art the womb that hath contained God, * the righting of the fallen, holier than the cherubim, * higher than all creation, * a sight hard to look upon, * strangest report, inexpressible sayings. * Thou hast shown thyself to be the chariot of the Word, * the cloud from which dawned the Sun that doth shed His light even upon me ** and granteth unto those in darkness His great mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Little Vespers, aposticha Theotokos sticheron 3`}}],theotokos_verses:{ref:`shared.lv_theotokos_aposticha_verses`}},aposticha_theotokion:{text:`The prophecies concerning thee have been fulfilled, O pure Virgin; * for one of the prophets foretold thee as the Gate in Eden * facing towards the east through which none had passed, * except the Creator of thee and all the world. * Another saw thee as a bush aflame with fire, * because in thee there dwelt the fire of the Godhead * and yet thou hast remained unburned. * Another saw thee as a holy mountain * from which was hewn without the hand of man a cornerstone * and with it the image of the noetic Nebuchadnezzar hath been crushed. * Truly great and wondrous is the mystery that hath been manifest in thee, * wherefore we glorify thee, ** for through thee Salvation hath come to our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Little Vespers, aposticha Theotokion`}},closing_rubric:`“Now lettest Thou Thy servant depart ...,” Trisagion. Then:`,dismissal_rubric:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion: [marked WITHOUT a printed text — §9.6: resolution is an assembly question (Fekula/Theotokia tables), not a data gap]`},great_vespers:{rubric:`On “Lord I have cried ...,” 10 Stichera: 7 Resurrection Stichera and 3 of the saint of the day, or 4 and 6 if the Menaion service is of Polyeleos rank.`,lic:[{text:`By Thy precious Cross, O Christ, * Thou hast shamed the devil, * and by Thy Resurrection Thou hast blunted the sting of sin, * and saved us from the gates of death: ** we glorify Thee, the only-begotten One.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, LIC sticheron 1`}},{text:`He who hath granted Resurrection to mankind, * was led as a sheep to the slaughter; * the princes of Hades trembled before Him * and the gates of lamentations were lifted up; * for Christ the King of glory entered therein, * saying to those in bondage: “Come forth!” ** and to those in darkness: “Reveal yourselves!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, LIC sticheron 2`}},{text:`O great wonder! * Having suffered in the flesh through His love for mankind, * the Creator of all things visible and invisible, * hath arisen as immortal. * Come O ye descendents of the nations, * let us worship Him; * for delivered from deception by His compassion, ** we have learned to hymn one God in three Hypostases.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, LIC sticheron 3`}},{text:`We offer unto Thee our evening worship, * O never-setting Light, * who in the flesh at the end of the ages, * as in a mirror, shone through upon the world, * and descended even into Hades, * dispersing the darkness therein * and showing unto the nations the light of the Resurrection. ** O Lord, Giver of light, glory be to Thee!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, LIC sticheron 4`},provenance_note:`sub-group "Other Stichera, by Anatolius" (§4.3)`},{text:`Let us glorify Christ the Author of our salvation; * for by His arising from the dead, * the world hath been saved from delusion; * the choir of angels rejoiceth, * the deception of demons fleeth, * fallen Adam hath arisen, ** and the devil hath been overthrown.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, LIC sticheron 5`},provenance_note:`sub-group "Other Stichera, by Anatolius" (§4.3)`},{text:`The watchmen were instructed by the lawless ones * to conceal Christ’s Resurrection, * taking money to say that “while we slept * the corpse was stolen from the grave.” * Who ever saw, or who ever heard of a corpse being stolen? * Especially one anointed yet naked, * and with its grave-clothes left in the tomb? * Be not deceived, O ye Jews, * learn from the sayings of the prophets, * and know that He is truly the Redeemer of the world ** and All-powerful.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, LIC sticheron 6`},provenance_note:`sub-group "Other Stichera, by Anatolius" (§4.3)`},{text:`O Lord, our Savior, * Thou hast despoiled Hades and trampled upon death; * enlightening the world by the precious Cross, ** have mercy upon us.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, LIC sticheron 7`},provenance_note:`sub-group "Other Stichera, by Anatolius" (§4.3)`}],lic_verses:[{text:`Bring my soul out of prison * that I may confess Thy name.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, LIC ladder verse 1`}},{text:`The righteous shall wait patiently for me * until Thou shalt reward me.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, LIC ladder verse 2`}},{text:`Out of the depths have I cried unto Thee, O Lord; * O Lord, hear my voice.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, LIC ladder verse 3`}},{text:`Let Thine ears be attentive * to the voice of my supplication.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, LIC ladder verse 4`}},{text:`If Thou shouldest mark iniquities, O Lord, O Lord, who shall stand? * For with Thee there is forgiveness.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, LIC ladder verse 5`}},{text:`For Thy name’s sake have I patiently waited for Thee, O Lord; my soul hath patiently waited for Thy word, * my soul hath hoped in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, LIC ladder verse 6`}},{text:`From the morning watch until night, from the morning watch * let Israel hope in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, LIC ladder verse 7`}}],lic_menaion_rubric:`Then the Stichera from the Menaion, with the following Verses:`,lic_menaion_verses:[{text:`For with the Lord there is mercy, and with Him is plenteous redemption; * and He shall redeem Israel out of all his iniquities.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, Menaion-stichera verse 1`}},{text:`O praise the Lord, all ye nations; * praise Him, all ye peoples.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, Menaion-stichera verse 2`}},{text:`For He hath made His mercy to prevail over us, * and the truth of the Lord abideth forever.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, Menaion-stichera verse 3`}}],dogmatikon_rubric:`Glory from the Menaion, if appointed. Otherwise: Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion Dogmatic:`,dogmatikon:{text:`In the Red Sea of old * an image of the Bride who knew not wedlock was depicted. * There Moses was the one who parted the sea, * here Gabriel is the minister of the miracle. * At that time Israel marched dry-shod through the deep, * now the Virgin doth seedlessly give birth to Christ. * The sea after Israel’s passage remained impassable; * the immaculate one after bearing Emmanuel remained incorrupt. * O God, Who doth exist and is pre-eternal, * and hath appeared as man, ** have mercy upon us.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, Glory/Both-now — Theotokion Dogmatic`},sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion Dogmatic`},prokeimenon:{ref:`shared.saturday_vespers_prokeimenon`},aposticha:[{text:`With voices of song we magnify Thee, O Christ, * the Savior incarnate, * yet not separated from heaven, * for as the Lord who lovest mankind * Thou hast suffered the Cross and death for the sake of our race, * overthrowing the gates of Hades, * and rising on the third day, ** thus saving our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, aposticha sticheron 1 (unversed)`}},{text:`When Thy side was pierced, O Giver of life, * Thou didst pour forth streams of forgiveness, * of life and salvation for all; * Thou didst suffer death in the flesh, * granting unto us immortality, * and by dwelling in a grave Thou hast freed us, * gloriously raising us up with Thyself as God; * wherefore we cry out to Thee: ** “O Lord, Lover of mankind, glory be to Thee!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, aposticha sticheron 2`}},{text:`Wonderful is Thy crucifixion * and Thy descent into Hades, O Lover of mankind, * for having despoiled it and as God gloriously raising with Thyself * those who were captive therein, * Thou hast opened paradise and bidden them welcome. * So too grant unto us who glorify Thine arising on the third day, * the forgiveness of our sins, * making us worthy to be inhabitants of paradise, ** as Thou alone art compassionate.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, aposticha sticheron 3`}},{text:`O Lover of mankind, * Who for our sake didst accept to suffer the Passion in the flesh, * and arise from the dead on the third day, * heal the passions of our flesh, * and raise us up from our grievous transgressions, ** and save us.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, aposticha sticheron 4`}}],aposticha_verses:{ref:`shared.saturday_gv_aposticha_verses`},aposticha_glory_rubric:`Glory from the Menaion, if appointed, otherwise:`,aposticha_theotokion:{text:`Thou art the temple and portal, * the palace and throne of the King, * O most honored Virgin, * through whom Christ the Lord, my Redeemer, * Who is the Sun of righteousness, * hath revealed Himself unto those who sleep in darkness, * deigning to enlighten those * whom He hath fashioned in His image by His own hand. * Wherefore, O all-hymned one, * as thou hast acquired a mother’s boldness before Him, ** entreat Him without ceasing, that our souls be saved.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Great Vespers, aposticha Theotokion — the REAL Saturday fallback (§4.3/§8)`}},vigil_rubric:{tone:4,text:{text:`O Theotokos and Virgin, rejoice, * O Mary, Full of grace; the Lord is with thee; * blessed art thou among women, * and blessed is the Fruit of thy womb, * for thou hast borne the Savior of our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Great Vespers, after the aposticha (vigil) — "* for thou hast borne" single asterisk (shared/2-1: **; §5 pointing divergence)`}},provenance_note:`Printed with "(Thrice)"; stored WITHOUT a repeat field per the §9.4-adjacent ruling — the vigil rubric governs the count. §5: pointing diverges from shared (single * at the final line).`},no_vigil_rubric:`If a Vigil is not served, we chant (Once):`},nocturns:{frame_rubric:`The priest saith: “Blessed is our God ...,” and we say: Amen. Glory to Thee, our God, glory to Thee. O heavenly King ..., Trisagion through Our Father ..., Priest: For Thine is the kingdom ..., And we say: Amen. Lord, have mercy (12 times), Glory..., Both now ..., O come, let us worship (Thrice). Psalm 50 (Have mercy on me, O God...)`,canon:{title:`Canon to the Holy & Life-creating Trinity`,composer:`Metrophanes`,acrostic:`The fifth rule to the three-sunned Light`,heading_rubric:`And then, the Canon to the Holy & Life-creating Trinity, the acrostic whereof is “The fifth rule to the three-sunned Light,” the composition of Metrophanes, in Tone V:`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Christ, who with an upraised arm * bringeth wars to naught, * hath shaken horse and rider in the Red Sea; * but Israel hath He saved * as they chanted a song of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Refrain: O Most Holy Trinity, our God, glory be to Thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 1, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Hymning the might of the single countenance of the triple Sun, we cry out: Illumine our mind, O almighty God, and raise it up to Thine ineffable glory, O Master!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 1, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`On high the noetic rings of the angels with thrice-holy voices continually hymn the threefold Unity, the Trinity sharing the same essence, transcendent and omnipotent.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 1, item 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Give unto my soul the divine, most sweet and light-giving food of Thy love and divine and cleansing compunction, O Trinity, Unity, Origin of light, greatly merciful Master of all creation`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 1, item 4`},label:`glory`},{text:`Theotokion: Without thunder, like the dew upon the fleece, the divine Rain descended from heaven into thy womb, O Virgin; and He hath saved all human nature, which had dried up, O all-pure one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 1, item 5`},label:`both_now`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`By Thy command Thou didst establish the earth upon nothing * and suspended it unsupported; * do Thou establish Thy Church on the unshakeable rock of Thy commandments, O Christ, * Who alone art good * and the Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Having conceived in thought the noetic beings, Thou didst make them constant singers of Thy divinity, O thrice-radiant and almighty God. Yet, as Thou art compassionate, accept also the entreaty and supplication of mortals made of clay.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 3, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`As Thou art compassionate, O Thou Who by essence art immune to change, grant forgiveness offenses and salvation unto us who are changeable, and hymn the unfathomable wellspring of Thy goodness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 3, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`As the prophets and the apostles manifestly learned from Thee, we glorify Thee - the Father, the Son and the Spirit - in the immutable aspect of the one and thrice-radiant Godhead of the Lord of all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 3, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`Theotokion: Thou didst appear unto Moses in the bush as the angel of great Counsel of the Almighty, revealing Thine incarnation from the Virgin, O Word of God, whereby Thou hast transformed us and raised us up to the heavens.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 3, item 4`},label:`both_now`},{text:`Lord, have mercy! (Thrice)`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 3, item 5`},label:`plain`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Habbakuk, prophetically apprehending * Thy divine self-emptying, O Christ, * cried out to Thee with trembling: * Thou hast come for the salvation of Thy people; * to save Thine anointed ones.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Beholding Christ the Judge going to the Father and revealing a vision of the Spirit, Daniel mystically learned of the threefold radiance of the one Dominion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 4, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Grant the glory of the angels unto those who with lips of clay hymn Thee, the transcendent God, the trinity of Hypostases, one in essence.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 4, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let us glorify the one Authority, the one Dominion indivisible in three characters. O Father, Son and Spirit, enlighten us, Thy servants!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 4, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`Theotokion: The mountain densely wooded and overshadowed, which Habbakuk beheld of old, and from whence the Holy One came forth, revealed the invisible Offspring Whom thou didst conceive, O Virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 4, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Thou Who hast clothed Thyself in light as with a garment, * I rise early unto Thee and cry out to Thee: * Enlighten my darkened soul, O Christ, * in that Thou alone art compassionate!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O my God, Thou threefold Light, Who in Thy goodness fashioned man and made him according to Thine image, abide in me, in that Thou art Good and compassionate.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 5, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O three-sunned Unity, guide me to the divine paths of salvation, and fill me with Thine effulgence, in that Thou art in essence God infinite in power.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 5, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O indivisible Light of the one Essence, thrice-radiant, never-waning, distinguished in characteristics: with Thy rays illumine my heart.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 5, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`Theotokion: When the prophet of old beheld thee, O most immaculate and pure one, as the gate facing the never-waning Light, he straightway recognized thee as the dwelling-place of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 5, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Calm the raging sea of the passions, * O Master Christ, * with its soul-destroying tempest, * and lead me up from corruption * in that Thou art compassionate.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`As the thrice-radiant Godhead of Hypostases, Thou art One, sharing the same form and equal in activity, essence and will.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 6, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The prophet clearly revealed Thee when he chanted to the Father, Thy Light: In the Spirit shall we behold the light of the Son, the one three-sunned God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 6, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The immaterial Being in three Hypostases hath sole authority and might; for through It every creature doth receive its existence and is renewed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 6, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`Through the supplications of the Mother of God, O God, our sole, thrice-radiant Master, send down deliverance from transgressions and misfortunes upon those who hymn Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 6, item 4`},label:`both_now`},{text:`Lord, have mercy! (Thrice)`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 6, item 5`},label:`plain`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The supremely exalted Lord of our fathers * quenched the flame, * and bedewed the youths * as they chanted in harmony: * O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`As Thou dost possess an abyss of mercy and an unfathomable depth of compassions, O Lord, have mercy upon those who hymn Thee, the one, thrice- radiant God of all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 7, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Hymning Thee, the incomprehensible, single and thrice-radiant God and Lord, we cry out to Thee: Grant cleansing of sins unto Thy servants.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 7, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Equally honoring the Hypostases in the single Dominion, we distinguish the indivisible Essence of God the Father, and the Son, and the most holy Spirit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 7, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`Theotokion: Thou didst bud forth the Flower of the Godhead, the Offshoot of the beginningless Father, O Virgin, the co-eternal Scion which imparteth life to all mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 7, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Unto Thee the Fashioner of all, * the children in the furnace chanted a hymn: * All ye works of the Lord, * supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`That Thou mightest reveal one of the three Hypostases of the Dominion, of old Thou didst manifestly appear unto Abraham in the guise of a man; and he hymned Thy sole might.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 8, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O unapproachable Light - compassionate Father, Word and Spirit - grant that I may behold Thy beneficent radiance, and may ever be well-pleasing unto Thee, O Lord of all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 8, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Holy is God the pre-eternal Father; holy is the Son Who is begotten of the Father; and holy is the life-creating Spirit, Who proceedeth from the Father and is revealed by the Son.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 8, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`Theotokion: O all-hymned one, from the glory of the threefold Sun thou hast shone forth for us the one Christ and Lord, Who mystically teaches all to chant unto the one Godhead in three Hypostases throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 8, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`O Isaiah, rejoice and be glad! * The Virgin hath conceived in her womb, * and hath borne a Son, Emmanuel, * Who is both God and man; * and Orient is His name; * Him we magnify, and the Virgin we call blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Human words are unable to hymn Thee as is meet, O beginningless Unity; yet deriving boldness from our faith, as far as possible we offer glory and praise to Thy might, O divine co-enthroned Trinity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 9, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`With most pure mouths the cherubim and seraphim glorify Thee, the one thrice-radiant God Who dost reign in equal glory; and with them accept also us sinners, who magnify Thy might.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 9, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Isaiah beheld Thee on the throne of the cherubim, with the seraphim standing round about Thee, covering their faces with their wings, and crying aloud: Holy, Holy, Holy art Thou, O thrice-holy God, Who art glorified in three Hypostases!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 9, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`Theotokion: In that thou art the pure and immaculate Virgin, thou hast given birth to the Son, the immutable God Who delivereth us from temptations. Him do thou now entreat, that He grant us remission of sins.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, Ode 9, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]}}},after_ode3:{sessional:{text:`Merciful art Thou, O indivisible Trinity, for Thou hast mercy on all, in that Thou art almighty and most compassionate, full of pity and greatly merciful. Wherefore, we who are weighed down with many sins flee unto Thee, crying aloud: Cleanse Thou Thy servants, and deliver all from every torment!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, sessional after Ode III`},spec_mel:`The co-beginningless Word`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn`},theotokion:{text:`O all-holy Virgin, have mercy on us who with faith have recourse to thee, the compassionate one, and now ask thy fervent aid; for as thou art good, thou art able to save us, in that thou art the Mother of God Most High, ever employing thy maternal supplications, O thou who art full of the grace of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, sessional theotokion after Ode III`},type:`theotokion`}},after_ode6:{sessional:{text:`Let us now glorify the three-sunned Light, and let us worship the simple Trinity, for It hath enlightened and had mercy upon us, and hath freed from corruption the whole race of mankind, delivering the whole world from the deceit of idolatry, and hath given us the kingdom.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, sessional after Ode VI`},spec_mel:`The co-beginningless Word`,sourceLabel:`Sessional Hymn`},theotokion:{text:`Perplexed by all things, I have fled to thee, the help of all and refuge of the sinful and lowly, crying aloud: I have sinned and insensibly abide in evils, wretch that I am! Have mercy on me and, before the end, turn me back, and deliver me from all torment, unworthy though I be.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, Trinity canon, sessional theotokion after Ode VI`},type:`theotokion`}},gregory_rubric:{rubric:`Then, the hymn of Gregory the Sinaite: (which, is chanted every Sunday after the canon)`,stanzas:[{text:`It is truly meet to glorify Thee, the Word of God, before Whom the cherubim tremble and quake, and Whom the hosts of heaven glorify. And with fear we glorify Christ, the Bestower of life, Who rose from the tomb on the third day.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, hymn of Gregory the Sinaite, stanza 1`}},{text:`With divine songs let us all in godly manner hymn the Father, the Son and the Spirit divine, the Might in three Hypostases, the one Sovereignty and Dominion,`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, hymn of Gregory the Sinaite, stanza 2 — "in godly manner" (no article) + comma stanza end (§5 per-tone)`}},{text:`Whom all mortals hymn and the hosts of heaven glorify, the essential Unity in three Hypostases, Who is worshipped with faith by all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, hymn of Gregory the Sinaite, stanza 3`}},{text:`We magnify Thee, the Godhead, the Lord of the cherubim, the incomparable divine Origin of the seraphim, the indivisible Trinity in Unity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, hymn of Gregory the Sinaite, stanza 4`}},{text:`I worship God: the beginningless Father, the Son Who is equally without beginning, and the Spirit. With hymns let us honor the one indivisible and unified Essence, the threefold Unity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, hymn of Gregory the Sinaite, stanza 5`}},{text:`Shine forth Thy dazzling lightning flashes upon me, O my God in three Hypostases, Creator of all, and show me to be a splendid, luminous and unshakable habitation of Thine unapproachable glory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, hymn of Gregory the Sinaite, stanza 6 — "unshakable" (shared: "immutable"; §5 per-tone)`}},{text:`With fear let us glorify Christ the Bestower of life, Who ineffably became incarnate from the Virgin, for the cherubim tremble and quake before Him, and the angelic armies glorify Him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Nocturns, hymn of Gregory the Sinaite, stanza 7 — "incarnate from the Virgin" (shared: "of the Virgin"; §5 per-tone)`}}],provenance_note:`RULED (Bill, July 8 2026): the Gregory hymn is stored PER-TONE in every tone — four prints (2-1/3-1/4-1/5-1) yield three distinct byte-states with no majority reading, falsifying the §5 shared hypothesis for this hymn. 5-1 divergences at stanzas 2, 6, 7 (see per-stanza loci). The shared table remains the 2-1 print.`},closing_rubric:`The rest of Nocturns, and the Dismissal.`},matins:{god_is_lord_rubric:`On “God is The Lord ...,” the Resurrection Troparion, in Tone V: [troparion printed "(Twice)"] Glory ..., the Troparion from the Menaion, otherwise Glory ..., Both now ..., The Theotokion, in Tone V, (or in the Tone of that from the Menaion):`,sessionals:[{rubric:`After the 1st chanting of the Psalter (Kathisma II), the Sessional Hymns of the Resurrection, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`Let us celebrate the Cross of the Lord, * let us honor His holy burial with hymns, * and let us exulting, glorify His Resurrection. * For with Himself He hath raised the dead from their graves, * and as God having despoiled the dominion of death * and the might of the devil, ** He hath shone forth light upon those in Hades.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Kathisma II, sessional 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Lord, Thou who hast put death to death, * was called dead; * Thou who hast emptied the tombs was placed in a tomb; * above, the soldiers stood guarding the grave, * below, Thou didst raise the dead from all ages. * O all-powerful and incomprehensible Lord, ** glory be to Thee!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Kathisma II, sessional 2`},label:`plain`}],verses:[{text:`Arise, O Lord my God, let Thy hands be lifted on high; * forget not Thy paupers to the end.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Kathisma II, sessional verse`}}],closer:{text:`Rejoice holy mountain upon which God hath walked; * Rejoice! living bush unconsumed by fire; * Rejoice! O only bridge of creation to God, * who leadeth mortals to eternal life; * Rejoice! maiden undefiled, * who hath born without wedlock the salvation of our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Kathisma II, Glory/Both-now closer`},type:`theotokion`}},{rubric:`After the 2nd chanting of the Psalter (Kathisma III), the Sessional Hymns of the Resurrection, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`O Lord, after Thy Resurrection on the third day, * and after the worship of the apostles, Peter cried unto Thee; * “The women had courage, and I was afraid; * the thief confessed Thee as God, and I denied Thee: * wilt Thou no longer call me a disciple, * or wilt Thou once again declare me a fisher of the deep? ** Receive me in my penitence, O God, and save me!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Kathisma III, sessional 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O merciful Lord, the lawless ones * nailed Thee between two condemned thieves * and pierced Thy side with a lance, * but Thou, Who didst destroy the gates of Hades, * didst suffer burial and arise on the third day; * The women ran to see Thee * and announced the Resurrection to Thine apostles. * O supremely exalted Savior whom the angels hymn, ** O blessed Lord, glory be to Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Kathisma III, sessional 2`},label:`plain`}],verses:[{text:`I will confess Thee, O Lord, with my whole heart, * I will tell of all Thy wonders.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Kathisma III, sessional verse`}}],closer:{text:`The Bride who knew not wedlock, the Birthgiver of God, * who turned Eve’s grief to joy, * do we the faithful hymn and worship, * for thou hast redeemed us from the ancient curse. * And now, O all-hymned most holy one, ** cease not to make intercession for the salvation of our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Kathisma III, Glory/Both-now closer`},type:`theotokion`}}],polyeleos_rubric:{verses:[{text:`Praise ye the name of the Lord; O ye servants, * praise the Lord. Alleluia, alleluia, alleluia.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Polyeleos select verse 1 (with Alleluia refrain) — pointed print (§5 per-tone; shared/2-1 prints unpointed)`}},{text:`Blessed is the Lord out of Zion, * who dwelleth in Jerusalem. Alleluia, alleluia, alleluia.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Polyeleos select verse 2 (with Alleluia refrain) — pointed print (§5 per-tone; shared/2-1 prints unpointed)`}},{text:`O give thanks unto the Lord, for He is good; * for His mercy endureth forever. Alleluia, alleluia, alleluia.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Polyeleos select verse 3 (with Alleluia refrain) — pointed print (§5 per-tone; shared/2-1 prints unpointed)`}},{text:`O give thanks unto the God of Heaven; * for His mercy endureth forever. Alleluia, alleluia, alleluia.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Polyeleos select verse 4 (with Alleluia refrain) — pointed print (§5 per-tone; shared/2-1 prints unpointed) — "God of Heaven" (shared: "of heaven")`}}],provenance_note:`§5: the 5-1 Polyeleos prints every select verse WITH a * pointing mark, and verse 4 reads "God of Heaven" — the whole set stored per-tone; the shared (2-1) table stands for the tones that match it. Frame rubrics unchanged (shared.polyeleos.rubric/prelent_note/megalynarion_rubric still govern assembly).`},evlogitaria_rubric:{ref:`shared.evlogitaria`},hypakoe:{text:`The myrrh-bearing women, amazed in their minds by the vision of the angel * yet enlightened in their souls by the divine Resurrection, * announced the glad tidings to the apostles: * “Proclaim ye among the nations the Resurrection of the Lord, * Who worketh in us through wonders, ** and Who granteth us great mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, after the Evlogitaria`},sourceLabel:`The Sessional Hymn`},anabathmoi:[{troparia:[{text:`When I am troubled I sing to Thee like David, * O my Savior: ** Deliver my soul from a deceitful tongue.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Anabathmoi antiphon 1, troparion 1`}},{text:`Blessed is the life of those * who dwell in the desert places, ** divine love giveth them wings.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Anabathmoi antiphon 1, troparion 2`}}],gloria:{text:`By the Holy Spirit all things are unshaken, * both visible and invisible; * for He hath sovereign power, ** being undeniably one of the Trinity.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Anabathmoi antiphon 1, Glory/Both-now`}}},{troparia:[{text:`Lift up thyself to the mountains, * O my soul; ** go thither from whence cometh our help.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Anabathmoi antiphon 2, troparion 1`}},{text:`Let Thy right hand hover over me, * O Christ, ** and guard me from every misfortune.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Anabathmoi antiphon 2, troparion 2`}}],gloria:{text:`Let us sing to the Holy Spirit, * as we contemplate God: * Thou art God, Life, Love, Light, and Intellect, * Thou art Goodness, ** and Thou reignest unto the ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Anabathmoi antiphon 2, Glory/Both-now`}}},{troparia:[{text:`Filled with great joy * at the words of those who say unto me: * “Let us go into the courts of the Lord,” ** I offer up my prayers.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Anabathmoi antiphon 3, troparion 1`}},{text:`Fearful things are accomplished in the house of David; * for a fire is found there, ** burning every shameful thought.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Anabathmoi antiphon 3, troparion 2`}}],gloria:{text:`To the Holy Spirit belongeth the lordship of life, * for from Him every living being hath its breath, * as also from the Father ** together with the Son.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Anabathmoi antiphon 3, Glory/Both-now`}}}],prokeimenon:{tone:5,text:{text:`Arise, O Lord my God, let Thy hand be lifted high; * for Thou art King unto the ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins prokeimenon`}},verse:{text:`I will confess Thee, O Lord, with my whole heart, I will tell of all Thy wonders.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins prokeimenon verse`}}},canon:{title:`Resurrection Canon Tone V`,heading_rubric:`After which: “O God, save Thy people ...,” Then the Canons: Resurrection Canon Tone V.`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Christ, who with an upraised arm * bringeth wars to naught, * hath shaken horse and rider in the Red Sea; * but Israel hath He saved * as they chanted a song of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 1 irmos`}},resurrection:{refrain:`Glory to Thy holy Resurrection O Lord.`,troparia:[{text:`O Benefactor Christ, the assembly of the Jews showed no beneficent love for Thee, but bearing thorns they crowned Thee, the Author of our race, who hath abolished the punishment of tares.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 1, resurrection troparion 1`}},{text:`O Giver of life, without falling Thou, O sinless One, didst descend into the pit and raise me up who had fallen. Thou didst endure the stench of my corruption unsullied, and hath made me sweet-smelling with the myrrh of Thy divine nature.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 1, resurrection troparion 2`}}],closer:{text:`The curse hath been abolished, and sorrow hath ceased, for the blessed one, Full of grace, hath made joy dawn upon the faithful, bringing forth a flower, Christ, as a blessing unto all the ends of the earth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 1, resurrection closer`},type:`theotokion`,refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`}},cross_resurrection:{refrain:`Glory to Thy precious Cross and Resurrection O Lord.`,troparia:[{text:`Unto Him who hath been willingly nailed upon the Cross, and through the Cross freed the fallen one from the ancient curse, to Him alone let us sing, for He is glorified.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 1, cross_resurrection troparion 1`}},{text:`Unto Christ, the dead One, who hath risen from the tomb and raised together with Himself the fallen one and adorned him by seating him with the Father, to Him alone let us sing, for He is glorified.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 1, cross_resurrection troparion 2`}}],closer:{text:`O Immaculate Mother of God, we beseech thee to unceasingly implore God who was incarnate from thee, yet never absent from His Father’s bosom, to save those whom He hath fashioned from every besetting calamity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 1, cross_resurrection closer`},type:`theotokion`,refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`}},theotokos:{refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,troparia:[{text:`O all-immaculate one, implore Christ, the light who dwelt within thee and Who hath enlightened the world with the rays of His Godhead, to enlighten all those who hymn thee, O Virgin Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 1, theotokos troparion 1`}},{text:`O thou who art Full of grace, and art made fair by the beauty of the virtues, thou hast received by the overshadowing of the Spirit the comeliness that bestoweth beauty, O most pure one, and which maketh the universe radiant.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 1, theotokos troparion 2`}},{text:`O Virgin, the bush on Sinai foreshadowing thee of old, was not consumed though mingled with fire; for beyond understanding as a Virgin thou didst bear a Child and yet remain a virgin, O Virgin Mother.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 1, theotokos troparion 3`}}]},menaion_rubric:`The Troparia from the Menaion, then the appointed Katavasia.`},3:{irmos:{text:`By Thy command Thou didst establish the earth upon nothing * and suspended it unsupported; * do Thou establish Thy Church on the unshakeable rock of Thy commandments, O Christ, * Who alone art good * and the Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 3 irmos`}},resurrection:{refrain:`Glory to Thy holy Resurrection O Lord.`,troparia:[{text:`Unto Thee O Christ, Who didst work the wondrous miracle in the wilderness, did the ungrateful children of Israel, who had suckled honey from the rocks, offer gall, and in exchange for Thy deeds of goodness they offered Thee vinegar instead of manna.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 3, resurrection troparion 1`}},{text:`They who of old were protected by a cloud of light, laid Christ, who is Life, in a tomb; but by Thine own power Thou didst arise and grant unto all the faithful the effulgence of the Spirit, which doth mystically overshadow them from above.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 3, resurrection troparion 2`}}],closer:{text:`Without wedlock and without the pain of childbirth thou hast become the Mother of Him Who shone forth from the incorrupt Father through thee; Since thou didst bear the Word made flesh, with Orthodox belief we proclaim thee to be the Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 3, resurrection closer`},type:`theotokion`,refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`}},cross_resurrection:{refrain:`Glory to Thy precious Cross and Resurrection O Lord.`,troparia:[{text:`Thou hast arisen from the tomb, O Christ, giver of life, delivering from the corruption of death those who hymn Thy voluntary crucifixion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 3, cross_resurrection troparion 1`}},{text:`The myrrh-bearing women were hastening to anoint Thy body, O Christ, and not finding it they returned hymning Thine arising.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 3, cross_resurrection troparion 2`}}],closer:{text:`O pure one, without ceasing implore the One who became incarnate from thy loins that those who hymn thee, O pure Virgin, may be delivered from the snares of the devil.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 3, cross_resurrection closer`},type:`theotokion`,refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`}},theotokos:{refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,troparia:[{text:`Thou hast now most clearly been revealed, O honored Virgin, to be the ladder by which the Most High came down to restore corrupted nature. For through thee the supremely good One was well-pleased to be joined to the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 3, theotokos troparion 1`}},{text:`God, Who of old prefigured the mystery of the Virgin, and Who knoweth all things, even from before the ages, hath in these last days sent His Offspring and revealed Him taking His dwelling within thy womb, O all-immaculate one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 3, theotokos troparion 2`}},{text:`The condemnation of the ancient curse hath been absolved through thee, O most pure Virgin, for in His exceeding goodness the Lord, having come forth from thee, hath poured forth His blessings upon all, O praise-worthy one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 3, theotokos troparion 3`}}]},menaion_rubric:`The Troparia from the Menaion, then the appointed Katavasia.`},4:{irmos:{text:`Habbakuk, prophetically apprehending * Thy divine self-emptying, O Christ, * cried out to Thee with trembling: * Thou hast come for the salvation of Thy people; * to save Thine anointed ones.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 4 irmos`}},resurrection:{refrain:`Glory to Thy holy Resurrection O Lord.`,troparia:[{text:`O good One, Through wood Thou didst sweeten the bitter waters of Mara as if in an icon prefiguring Thine immaculate Cross, the wood which doth rectify the bitter taste of sin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 4, resurrection troparion 1`}},{text:`Thou didst accept, O my Savior, a Cross in place of the tree of knowledge of good and evil, and gall for sweet provender; while for the corruption of death Thou didst shed Thy divine blood.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 4, resurrection troparion 2`}}],closer:{text:`Without wedlock and without corruption didst thou conceive in thy womb, and in giving birth without the pangs of labor, thou didst bare God in the flesh, and after giving birth remained a virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 4, resurrection closer`},type:`theotokion`,refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`}},cross_resurrection:{refrain:`Glory to Thy precious Cross and Resurrection O Lord.`,troparia:[{text:`When the Cross was fixed upon the earth on Golgotha, the bars of Hades were smashed and the eternal gate-keepers cried aloud: “Glory to Thy power, O Lord!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 4, cross_resurrection troparion 1`}},{text:`When the Savior descended to those in bonds as one dead, the dead from all ages arose with Him and cried aloud: “Glory to Thy power, O Lord!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 4, cross_resurrection troparion 2`}}],closer:{text:`The Virgin hath given birth without knowing the birth-pangs of a mother, but a mother hath she been shown to be and a virgin hath she remained; wherefore hymning her we cry: “Rejoice!, O Theotokos!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 4, cross_resurrection closer`},type:`theotokion`,refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`}},theotokos:{refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,troparia:[{text:`Devoutly confessing thee with heart, mind, soul and voice, as truly the Theotokos, O pure Virgin, I thereby gather the fruit of salvation and am saved by thine intercessions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 4, theotokos troparion 1`}},{text:`He that created the universe from nothing, hath been well-pleased as a Benefactor to be fashioned from thee, O pure one, for the salvation of those who with faith and love hymn thee, O all-immaculate one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 4, theotokos troparion 2`}},{text:`The choirs beyond this world hymn thine Offspring, O all-immaculate One, rejoicing at the salvation of those who believe thee to be the true Theotokos, O Virgin undefiled.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 4, theotokos troparion 3`}},{text:`Isaiah named thee the staff from which, for our sakes, hath sprung forth a fair Flower, Christ God, for the salvation of those who with faith and love have recourse unto thy protection.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 4, theotokos troparion 4`}}]},menaion_rubric:`The Troparia from the Menaion, then the appointed Katavasia.`},5:{irmos:{text:`O Thou Who hast clothed Thyself in light as with a garment, * I rise early unto Thee and cry out to Thee: * Enlighten my darkened soul, O Christ, * in that Thou alone art compassionate!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 5 irmos`}},resurrection:{refrain:`Glory to Thy holy Resurrection O Lord.`,troparia:[{text:`The Lord of glory in a form without glory, hath been voluntarily hung dishonored upon the Tree, and thus hath ineffably procured for me divine glory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 5, resurrection troparion 1`}},{text:`Thou, O Christ, hast clothed me with incorruption, having incorruptibly tasted the corruption of death in the flesh, and didst dawn forth from the grave on the third day.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 5, resurrection troparion 2`}}],closer:{text:`Having given birth without seed to Christ, who is our justice and redemption, O Theotokos, thou hast freed our forefather’s nature from the curse.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 5, resurrection closer`},type:`theotokion`,refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`}},cross_resurrection:{refrain:`Glory to Thy precious Cross and Resurrection O Lord.`,troparia:[{text:`Thine hands outstretched upon the Tree, O our Savior, Thou didst call all to Thyself as Thou art the Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 5, cross_resurrection troparion 1`}},{text:`Thou hast despoiled Hades, O my Savior, and by Thy burial and Thy Resurrection, Thou hast filled all things with joy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 5, cross_resurrection troparion 2`}},{text:`Having arisen from tomb on the third day, Thou hast rendered all immortal and incorrupt.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 5, cross_resurrection troparion 3`}}],closer:{text:`We sing thy praises as a Virgin after child-birth, O Theotokos; for thou hast borne unto all the world, God the Word in the flesh.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 5, cross_resurrection closer`},type:`theotokion`,refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`}},theotokos:{refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,troparia:[{text:`All the prophets clearly announced thee beforehand, O all-honored Theotokos; for thou alone, O pure one, wast found to be wholly immaculate.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 5, theotokos troparion 1`}},{text:`O most pure one, we acknowledge thee to be the illumined cloud of living Water which hath rained down upon us, thy despairing people, Christ the Shower of incorruption.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 5, theotokos troparion 2`}},{text:`God, Who alone is compassionate dwelt within thee, and loved thee as one close to Him. O thou wholly good and immaculate one, sealing thy purity with virginity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 5, theotokos troparion 3`}}]},menaion_rubric:`The Troparia from the Menaion, then the appointed Katavasia.`},6:{irmos:{text:`Calm the raging sea of the passions, * O Master Christ, * with its soul-destroying tempest, * and lead me up from corruption * in that Thou art compassionate.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 6 irmos`}},resurrection:{refrain:`Glory to Thy holy Resurrection O Lord.`,troparia:[{text:`The ancestor of mankind, O Master Christ, descended into corruption through tasting of the forbidden fruit, but was restored to life through Thy Passion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 6, resurrection troparion 1`}},{text:`Thou, who art Life, didst descend into Hades, O Master Christ, and by becoming corruption to the corrupter, through death Thou hast become the Source of the resurrection.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 6, resurrection troparion 2`}}],closer:{text:`The Virgin hath given birth to a Child and after child-birth remained pure, and as a truly virgin Mother, cradled Him Who holdeth all things in His hands.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 6, resurrection closer`},type:`theotokion`,refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`}},cross_resurrection:{refrain:`Glory to Thy precious Cross and Resurrection O Lord.`,troparia:[{text:`Thou hast stretched out Thy hands, gathering together the nations, separated far from Thee, O Christ our God, by Thy life-bearing Cross, for Thou art the Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 6, cross_resurrection troparion 1`}},{text:`Thou hast despoiled death and shattered the gates of Hades; while Adam, released from his chains, crieth out to Thee: “Thy right hand hath saved me, O Lord!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 6, cross_resurrection troparion 2`}}],closer:{text:`O Mary, thou praise of the Orthodox, we fittingly glorify thee as the bush that remained unburnt, the mountain and the living ladder, and the gate of heaven.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 6, cross_resurrection closer`},type:`theotokion`,refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`}},theotokos:{refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,troparia:[{text:`When He who is the cause of all, by giving existence to all, took flesh like unto our flesh, He had thee as the cause of this wonder, O all-immaculate Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 6, theotokos troparion 1`}},{text:`We know thee, O all-immaculate one, to be a source brimming with life-giving healing for those who with faith have recourse to thy far-famed protection, O Sovereign Lady.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 6, theotokos troparion 2`}},{text:`For us thou didst bring forth the Giver of life, the Source of our salvation, Who bestoweth eternal redemption upon those who proclaim thee to be the true Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 6, theotokos troparion 3`}}]},menaion_rubric:`The Troparia from the Menaion, then the appointed Katavasia.`},7:{irmos:{text:`The supremely exalted Lord of our fathers * quenched the flame, * and bedewed the youths * as they chanted in harmony: * O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 7 irmos`}},resurrection:{refrain:`Glory to Thy holy Resurrection O Lord.`,troparia:[{text:`Wrapped in flesh, like unto bait draping a hook, Thou didst hurl down the serpent by Thy divine power raising up those who cry: “O God, blessed art Thou!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 7, resurrection troparion 1`}},{text:`The uncircumscribed One, who hath brought into being the boundless creation of the universe, is hidden in the flesh in a tomb. To Him we all sing: “O God, blessed art Thou!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 7, resurrection troparion 2`}}],closer:{text:`O all-immaculate one, thou hast borne in one Hypostasis two natures, God incarnate. To Him we all sing: “O God, blessed art Thou!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 7, resurrection closer`},type:`theotokion`,refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`}},cross_resurrection:{refrain:`Glory to Thy precious Cross and Resurrection O Lord.`,troparia:[{text:`Thou hast destroyed the deception of idols through the tree of the Cross; O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 7, cross_resurrection troparion 1`}},{text:`Thou didst arise from the dead, and with Thee, Thou hast raised those in Hades; O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 7, cross_resurrection troparion 2`}}],closer:{text:`Thou wast born of a Virgin, and revealed her to be the Theotokos; O God of our fathers, blessed art Thou.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 7, cross_resurrection closer`},type:`theotokion`,refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`}},theotokos:{refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,troparia:[{text:`The uncircumscribed One, who remaineth unchanged, was, since He is compassionate, hypostatically united to flesh within thee the most holy one. He Who is the only blessed God of our fathers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 7, theotokos troparion 1`}},{text:`O Sovereign Lady, Theotokos, with one voice we glorify thee, the all- immaculate Bride and throne of thy Creator; to Him we all sing: “Blessed art Thou, O God.”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 7, theotokos troparion 2`}},{text:`Made pure by the Spirit, O Virgin, thou didst become the Mother of the King of all, who hath fashioned thee; to Him we all sing: “Blessed art Thou, O God.”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 7, theotokos troparion 3`}},{text:`The Lord saved me, O all-immaculate Theotokos, having clothed Himself in the garment of the flesh He took from thee; to Him do we all chant: “Blessed art Thou, O God.”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 7, theotokos troparion 4`}}]},menaion_rubric:`The Troparia from the Menaion, then the appointed Katavasia.`},8:{irmos:{text:`Unto Thee the Fashioner of all, * the children in the furnace chanted a hymn: * All ye works of the Lord, * supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 8 irmos`}},resurrection:{refrain:`Glory to Thy holy Resurrection O Lord.`,troparia:[{text:`As if it was not willed by Thee, Thou didst pray that the cup of Thy saving Passion might pass; revealing thereby that Thou dost bear two wills, O Christ, corresponding to Thy two natures, throughout the ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 8, resurrection troparion 1`}},{text:`At Thy descent, O Christ, Hades became an object of derision disgorging all those who of old had been slain by the devil’s deception and who now supremely exalt Thee throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 8, resurrection troparion 2`}}],closer:{text:`O Virgin, who beyond all understanding hath, by the Word, given birth to the Lord as both God and man, and yet remained a virgin, all we His works bless thee and supremely exalt thee throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 8, resurrection closer`},type:`theotokion`,refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`}},cross_resurrection:{refrain:`Glory to Thy precious Cross and Resurrection O Lord.`,troparia:[{text:`Christ God, who willingly stretched forth His hands upon the Cross and thereby hath broken open the bonds of death; praise Him, ye priests, and ye peoples supremely exalt Him, throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 8, cross_resurrection troparion 1`}},{text:`Christ God, who didst dawn from the tomb like a bridegroom, appearing to the myrrh-bearing women and proclaiming unto them the tidings of great joy; praise Him, ye priests, and ye peoples supremely exalt Him, throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 8, cross_resurrection troparion 2`}}],closer:{text:`Thou hast been revealed, O pure Theotokos, as higher than the cherubim, for within thy womb thou didst carry Him who rideth upon them. With the bodiless powers we mortals glorify Him, throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 8, cross_resurrection closer`},type:`theotokion`,refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`}},theotokos:{refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,troparia:[{text:`The grief of the first-parents hath now ceased, since thou, God’s Mother, hast given birth to joy; wherefore we unceasingly hymn thee, O Virgin, and supremely exalt thee throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 8, theotokos troparion 1`}},{text:`The hosts of the bodiless powers sing the praises of thine incomprehensible child-bearing with us, O Virgin; with one voice and with love we, with them, supremely exalt thy child-bearing throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 8, theotokos troparion 2`}},{text:`A translucent stream of immortality hath issued forth from thee, O maiden, the Lord of all, Who cleanseth away the filth of sin from those who hymn thee with faith, and who supremely exalt thee throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 8, theotokos troparion 3`}},{text:`We confess thee, O Virgin, to be in truth, a divine and radiant throne, and a tabernacle of grace, for thou didst receive the Word of the Father; whom we supremely exalt throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 8, theotokos troparion 4`}}]},menaion_rubric:`After the Troparia from the Menaion for ODE VIII, we chant:`},9:{irmos:{text:`O Isaiah, rejoice and be glad! * The Virgin hath conceived in her womb, * and hath borne a Son, Emmanuel, * Who is both God and man; * and Orient is His name; * Him we magnify, and the Virgin we call blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 9 irmos`}},resurrection:{refrain:`Glory to Thy holy Resurrection O Lord.`,troparia:[{text:`O Master Christ, Thou hast assumed the nature of fallen mankind, and become wholly joined to him from a virgin womb, but alone not sharing in sin, and Thou hast freed the whole of him from corruption by Thine undefiled Passion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 9, resurrection troparion 1`}},{text:`O Master Christ God, by the blood which flowed from Thine immaculate and life-giving side, sacrifice to idols hath ceased, and all the earth doth offer Thee the sacrifice of praise.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 9, resurrection troparion 2`}}],closer:{text:`The pure and holy maiden did not reveal God without a body, nor yet a mere man, but both a perfect man and in truth perfect God, Whom we magnify together with the Father and the Spirit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 9, resurrection closer`},type:`theotokion`,refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`}},cross_resurrection:{refrain:`Glory to Thy precious Cross and Resurrection O Lord.`,troparia:[{text:`Thou didst endure sufferings on the Cross and by Thy death Thou didst destroy the power of Hades; with Orthodox belief we the faithful magnify Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 9, cross_resurrection troparion 1`}},{text:`Thou didst arise from the tomb on the third day, despoiling Hades and enlightening the world; we the faithful with one mind magnify Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 9, cross_resurrection troparion 2`}}],closer:{text:`Rejoice!, O God-bearer, Mother of Christ God; beseech Him Whom thou didst bear to grant remission of sins unto those who hymn thee with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 9, cross_resurrection closer`},type:`theotokion`,refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`}},theotokos:{refrain:`Most holy Theotokos save us.`,troparia:[{text:`O Ever-virgin Theotokos, from thy pure blood the flesh of the Creator and only-begotten Son of the Father was nurtured in a manner beyond nature, not from a man, and without seed, yet possessing both a mind and a soul.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 9, theotokos troparion 1`}},{text:`Thou didst halt the unrestrained stream of death, when beyond telling, thou didst in truth give birth in the flesh to life eternal; for Hades, consuming it with its bitter mouth, hath been destroyed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 9, theotokos troparion 2`}},{text:`Seated on His royal throne as Lord, thy Son hath placed thee on His right hand, shining radiantly in tasseled gold, and in divine virtues, bestowing upon thee the honor due His Mother, O all-immaculate one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 9, theotokos troparion 3`}},{text:`Thy childbirth is beyond telling, O Mother of God, for without a man hast thou conceived, and in a virginal manner hast thou delivered God; wherefore magnifying Him, we glorify thee, O Theotokos`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins canon, Ode 9, theotokos troparion 4`}}]},menaion_rubric:`The Troparia from the Menaion, then the appointed Katavasia.`}}},exapostilarion_rubric:`Exapostilarion (Svetilen). Note: The Exapostilarion is taken from the prescribed Eothinon according to the Resurrection Gospel, however, If the Menaion service is ‘feasted’ the Exapostilarion, with the appointed Theotokion, are taken from the Menaion.`,praises:{rubric:`On the Praises: “Let every breath ...,” 8 Stichera of the Resurrection, however, if the service from the Menaion is ‘feasted’ sing the first 4 Stichera from the Resurrection, and the last 4 from the Menaion, with the appointed verses.`,stichera:[{text:`O Lord, while the grave was sealed by lawless men, * Thou didst come forth from the tomb * in a manner similar to Thy birth from the Theotokos. * Thy bodiless angels could not fathom the event of Thine incarnation, * likewise the soldiers guarding Thee could not know when Thou didst arise. * For the full knowledge of both events hath been sealed from those who would inquire, * but the wonder of these events hath been revealed to those who with faith * worship the mystery which we hymn; ** grant unto us joy and great mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Praises sticheron 1`}},{text:`O Lord, having smashed the eternal bars and burst asunder the bonds of Hades, * Thou didst arise from the tomb, * leaving Thy grave clothes behind in testimony of Thy three day burial. * Whereupon Thou didst go forth into Galilee, * while yet being guarded in a cave. * Great is Thy mercy, O Savior, and beyond understanding; ** have mercy upon us.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Praises sticheron 2`}},{text:`O Lord, the women ran unto Thy tomb to see Thee, * the Christ who had suffered for our sakes. * Approaching the tomb they found an angel seated upon the stone, which had rolled back from fear, * and he cried unto them saying. * “The Lord hath arisen; go tell His disciples that He is risen, saving your souls.”`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Praises sticheron 3`}},{text:`O Lord, in a manner similar to that * by which Thou didst come forth from the sealed tomb, * Thou didst enter in unto Thy disciples when the doors were shut, * showing them Thy body’s sufferings, * O long-suffering Savior, * which Thou didst willingly endure. * As One who hath sprung forth from the seed of David, * Thou didst endure wounds, * but as One who didst spring forth from God, * even the Son of God * Thou hast delivered the world. * Incomprehensible and great is Thy mercy, ** O Savior, have mercy on us.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Praises sticheron 4`}},{text:`O Lord, and King of the ages, * Creator of all things, * Who for our sake willingly endured crucifixion and burial in the flesh, * in order to free us all from Hades, * Thou art our God and we know no other besides Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Praises sticheron 5`},provenance_note:`sub-group "Other Stichera of Anatolius"`},{text:`O Lord, who will recount Thine awe-inspiring wonders? * Who will confess Thy dread mysteries? * For, becoming incarnate for us, as Thou Thyself didst will, * Thou hast manifest the might of Thy power; * For on Thy Cross Thou didst open paradise to the thief, * and in Thy burial Thou didst smash the bars of Hades, * and with Thy Resurrection Thou hast enriched all things. * O compassionate Lord, glory be to Thee!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Praises sticheron 6`},provenance_note:`sub-group "Other Stichera of Anatolius"`},{text:`The myrrh-bearing women coming to Thy tomb in the deep of morning * seeking to anoint with spices the Immortal Word and God; * and being informed by the words of the angel * returned with joy to tell the apostles * that Thou O Lord, the Life of all, hast arisen, ** granting the world forgiveness and great mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Praises sticheron 7`},provenance_note:`sub-group "Other Stichera of Anatolius"`},{text:`The guards of the tomb which received God said unto the Jews: * “O the folly of your plan! * In vain did ye labor when you thought to guard Him who cannot be circumscribed.” * “Openly you appeared wishing to hide the Resurrection of the crucified One. * O the folly of your assembly!” * “Why do ye again wish to hide that which cannot be hidden?” * “Rather listen to us, * and be willing to believe the truth of what hath taken place.” * “A radiant angel came down from heaven and rolled away the stone;” * from fear of Him ye became as dead men,” * and calling out to the brave myrrh-bearing women the angel said: * “Do ye not see the death of the guards, * the breaking of the seals and the emptying of Hades?” * “Why seek ye as a mortal man, * the One who hath destroyed Hades’ victory * and smashed death’s sting?” * “Go quickly and proclaim to the apostles * the good tidings of the Resurrection, crying fearlessly:” * “He hath risen indeed, ** the Lord who hath great mercy!”`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Praises sticheron 8`},provenance_note:`sub-group "Other Stichera of Anatolius"`}],verses:{ref:`shared.praises_verse_ladder`},gloria_rubric:`Glory ..., The Eothinon of the Resurrection Gospel Note: If the service from the Menaion is “feasted” the Eothinon is taken from the Menaion, and the Eothinon of the Gospel is read at the end of Matins.`,theotokion:{text:`Thou art most blessed, O Virgin Theotokos, * for through Him who took flesh from thee, Hades hath been captured, * Adam recalled, the curse slain, Eve set free, * death put to death, and we have been given life. * Therefore in praise we cry: ** Blessed art Thou, O Christ our God, who hast been thus well-pleased, glory be to Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, Praises Both-now Theotokion`}}},doxology_troparion:{text:`Today is salvation come unto the world; * let us sing praises to Him that arose from the tomb, * and is the Author of our life. * For, having destroyed death by death, ** He hath given us the victory and great mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Matins, troparion after the Great Doxology`}}},liturgy:{beatitudes:{rubric:`Typika and Beatitudes.`,troparia:[{text:`Believing Thee to be God, O Christ, the thief on the cross confessed Thee in a pure manner, crying out from the depths of his heart: Remember me in Thy kingdom, O Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Liturgy, Beatitude troparion 1`}},{text:`Together let us hymn as Savior and Creator, Him Who on the Cross budded forth life for our race and caused the curse which originated from the tree to wither up.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Liturgy, Beatitude troparion 2`}},{text:`By Thy death hast Thou destroyed the power of death, O Christ, and Thou didst raise up with Thyself the dead of ages past, who now hymn Thee as our true God and Savior.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Liturgy, Beatitude troparion 3`}},{text:`Arriving at Thy tomb, O Christ, the honorable women sought to anoint Thee with myrrh, O Bestower of life; but an angel appeared to them, crying out: The Lord is risen!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Liturgy, Beatitude troparion 4`}},{text:`When Thou wast crucified between two condemned thieves, O Christ, one of them blasphemed Thee and was justly damned, while the other confessed Thee and dwelleth now in paradise.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Liturgy, Beatitude troparion 5`}},{text:`When they had come to the choir of the apostles, the honorable women cried out: Christ is risen! Let us worship Him as Master and Creator.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Liturgy, Beatitude troparion 6`}}],gloria:{text:`O indivisible Trinity, all-effecting and all-powerful Unity: Father, Son, and Holy Spirit: Thee do we hymn as our true God and Savior!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Liturgy, Beatitudes Gloria (Triadicon — final pre-Theotokion item)`}},theotokion:{text:`Rejoice, O animate temple of God and impassible gate! Rejoice, O fiery throne which burneth yet is not consumed! Rejoice, O Mother of Emmanuel, Christ our God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Liturgy, Beatitudes Theotokion`},sourceLabel:`Theotokion`}},prokeimenon:{tone:5,text:{text:`Thou, O Lord, shalt keep us and shalt preserve us from this generation and forevermore.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Liturgy prokeimenon`}},verse:{text:`Save me, O Lord, for a righteous man there is no more.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Liturgy prokeimenon verse`}}},alleluia:{tone:5,verses:[{text:`Thy mercies, O Lord, will I sing forever; unto generation to generation will I declare Thy truth with my mouth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Liturgy Alleluia`}},{text:`For Thou hast said, mercy shall be built up forever; in the heavens shall Thy truth be established.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Sunday Liturgy Alleluia verse 2`}}]}},vespers_weekday:{sun:{rubric:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 3 Stichera of repentance, in Tone V: Spec. Mel.: “Rejoice ...”:`,lic:{octoechos:[{text:`I weep and am downcast, envisioning the dread sentence of the Word, for which I, a wretch, have not the least reply for my guilt. Wherefore, I pray: Before the unseemliness of mine end overtaketh me, before I am mowed down by death, before I must needs be condemned to the place where the fire is unquenchable and the darkness is absolute, where are the worm and gnashing of teeth, and sinners are consumed, O my Christ, grant me great mercy and deliverance from mine offenses.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers, LIC Octoechos sticheron 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice`},{text:`Disdaining Thy laws and the Scriptures, wretch that I am, I have rejected Thy commandments, O God my Creator. How will I ever avoid the torment which is to come, O Savior! Wherefore, before mine end grant me forgiveness and a shower of tears, imparting true compunction to me, O Savior. As Thou art the supremely good God, drive far from me the hordes of the demons who seek to drag me down into the abyss of Hades, for I entreat Thee: Take not Thine almighty hand from me!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers, LIC Octoechos sticheron 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:3}],label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice`},{text:`Woe is me! How have I been darkened in mind? How have I withdrawn from Thee and, wretch that I am, enslaved myself to sin; and, enslaved to the passions, given myself wholly over to carnal pleasure which liveth within me, who am passion-fraught? Now I await my departure from this life and the coming reckoning. O supremely good Lord, grant me tearful repentance and release from my countless transgressions, for with faith I beseech Thee Who grantest the world great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers, LIC Octoechos sticheron 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice`}],octoechos_verses:[{text:`If Thou shouldest mark iniquities, O Lord, O Lord, who shall stand? * For with Thee there is forgiveness.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}]},{text:`For Thy name’s sake have I patiently waited for Thee, O Lord; my soul hath waited patiently for Thy word, * my soul hath hoped in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]},{text:`From the morning watch until night, from the morning watch * let Israel hope in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 3`}}],menaion_rubric:`Then the Stichera from the Menaion; or if there is no Menaion, these Stichera of the incorporeal ones, in Tone V:`,menaion_fallback:[{text:`O honorable initiates of the mysteries of the Godhead, the thrice-radiant and consubstantial Divinity, who, unceasingly offering up hymnody with incorporeal mouths and fiery tongues, bear our supplications and prayers, which we utter with defiled lips, and who ask for remission of sins: He. Who assumed our nature and is merciful by nature doth accept your pleas on behalf of His sinful servants, granting great mercy to the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers, Menaion-fallback sticheron 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O ye whole multitude of the angels, who draw nigh to my Master and stand with fear before His divine throne, full of ineffable light; guide me to the light of salvation for I have gone astray in the darkness of sin, and at the command of our compassionate God dispel the dark and alien gloom of the crafty demons with your help and grace; for they cannot endure, and are driven away, by the coming of light.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers, Menaion-fallback sticheron 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O radiant angels of God, standing before the divine throne of grace, receiving humility and true enlightenment from the divine light: Look down on us from the heavens, O ye who love mankind, for we are beset by the storm of evils, and are afflicted and sleep in darkness. Wherefore, come to our aid, O archangels, and deliver us from the snares of the enemy, the author of evil; for we all flee to your protection, O all-famed ones.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers, Menaion-fallback sticheron 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:4}],label:`plain`}],menaion_verses:[{text:`For with the Lord there is mercy, and with Him there is plenteous redemption; * and He shall redeem Israel out of all his iniquities.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers, ladder tail verse 1`}},{text:`O praise the Lord, all ye nations; * praise Him, all ye peoples.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers, ladder tail verse 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]},{text:`For He hath made His mercy to prevail over us, * and the truth of the Lord abideth forever.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers, ladder tail verse 3`}}]},lic_theotokion:{text:`Thou art truly higher than the throne of the cherubim, for the divine Word made His abode within thee, O pure one, desiring to restore our image; and issuing forth from thee as mortal, in that He is full of tender compassion, He endured the Cross and suffering for our sake, and as God hath given us the resurrection. Wherefore, giving thanks to the Creator with faith, we beseech thee as the one who transformed our condemned nature, that we may receive forgive- ness of transgressions and great mercy by your prayers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers, LIC Glory/Both-now closer`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],type:`theotokion`},prokeimenon:{ref:`shared.daily_vespers_prokeimena.sun`,rubric:`Then, “O Joyous Light ...,” the Prokeimenon, in Tone VIII:`},aposticha:{rubric:`Vouchsafe, O Lord ..., Litany: Let us complete ..., Then: On the Aposticha, these Stichera of repentance, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`O Lord, I cease not to sin, nor do I perceive Thy love for mankind which Thou hast granted me. Vanquish my lack of discernment, O Thou Who alone art good, and have mercy on me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Lord, from reverent fear of Thee I tremble, yet I cease not from committing sins. Who, when called to trial, doth not fear the judge? Or who, desiring to be healed, angereth the physician, as I do? O longsuffering Lord, have compassion upon my weakness, and have mercy on me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Not caring for all earthly things, and manfully braving tortures, ye were not disappointed in your goodly hopes, but became inheritors of the kingdom, of heaven, O all-famed martyrs. Having boldness before God the Lover of mankind, ask peace for the world and great mercy for our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`}],verses:[{text:`Unto Thee have I lifted up mine eyes, unto Thee that dwellest in heaven. Behold, as the eyes of servants look unto the hands of their masters, as the eyes of the handmaid look unto the hands of her mistress, so do our eyes look unto the Lord our God, * until He take pity on us.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers aposticha verse 1 — "her mistress" lowercase (shared/2-2: "Mistress"; §5 per-tone)`}},{text:`Have mercy on us, O Lord, have mercy on us, for greatly are we filled with abasement. Greatly hath our soul been filled therewith; let reproach come upon them that prosper, * and abasement on the proud.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers aposticha verse 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]}]},aposticha_theotokion:{text:`O strange, awesome and great mystery! * The Un-circumscribable One hath made His abode within a womb, * and a Mother remaineth a Virgin even after birthgiving, * for from her she gave birth to God Incarnate. * To Him, then, let us cry aloud, * to Him let us raise a hymn, * chanting with the angels: * Holy art Thou, O Christ God, * Who wast incarnate for our sake! ** Glory be to Thee!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-evening Vespers, aposticha Glory/Both-now closer`},type:`theotokion`},closing_rubric:`Then, “Now lettest Thou Thy servant depart ...,” Trisagion through Our`},mon:{rubric:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 3 Stichera of repentance, in Tone V: Spec. Mel.: “Rejoice ...”:`,lic:{octoechos:[{text:`Woe unto me who have angered Thee, my merciful God and Lord! How many times have I promised to repent, O Christ, and have been found to be a senseless liar? I have soiled my first baptismal raiment, and have forsaken my covenant with Thee, and this second commandment, which I confessed before Thee in the presence of men and angels, have I also abandoned, clad in a lamentable form. Setting this aside, O Savior, leave me not to perish utterly.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-evening Vespers, LIC Octoechos sticheron 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice`},{text:`What answer shalt thou find on the day of judgment, O wretched soul? Who will deliver thee from condemnation to everlasting fire and other torments? No- one, if thou thyself dost not placate the Compassionate One, forsaking thine evil deeds and acquiring a right pleasing life, every day weeping over thy countless transgressions, which thou committest at every hour in deed, word and thought, and beseeching Christ to grant thee the complete forgiveness of them.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-evening Vespers, LIC Octoechos sticheron 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice`},{text:`Let sinful habit not seize me, dragging me down, O Savior, nor let the demon, which ever wageth war on me and subjecteth me to his will, gain dominance over me; but rescue me from his dominion with Thy mighty hand, O Almighty One Who lovest mankind, and reign Thou within me. Grant that I may be wholly Thine, and living according to Thy will, O Word, may find rest in Thee, and cleansing, salvation and great mercy for myself.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-evening Vespers, LIC Octoechos sticheron 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:3}],label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice`}],octoechos_verses:[{text:`If Thou shouldest mark iniquities, O Lord, O Lord, who shall stand? * For with Thee there is forgiveness.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]},{text:`For Thy name’s sake have I patiently waited for Thee, O Lord; my soul hath, waited patiently for Thy word, * my soul hath hoped in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]},{text:`From the morning watch until night, from the morning watch * let Israel hope in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 3`}}],menaion_rubric:`Then the Stichera from the Menaion; or if there is no Menaion, these Stichera of the holy forerunner, in the same melody:`,menaion_fallback:[{text:`O blessed Forerunner and martyr of Christ, heal me who am wholly bowed down to the earth and am incurably broken, yet I flee with faith to thy godly protection. And rescue me, I pray thee, on the dread day, when I shall come to stand before His judgment-seat, and shall be given over to torments; and as thou hast unashamed boldness, O wise one, deliver me from standing on the left hand of Christ, entreating Him Who granteth great mercy to the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-evening Vespers, Menaion-fallback sticheron 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`As a most radiant luminary of the Sun, O wise Forerunner of Christ, shine thou a ray of light upon me who have fallen down into the darkness of countless evils, I pray thee. Raise me up out of the pit of sin, guiding me by thy sweet voice. O thou who of old loosed the voice of thy father by thy birth, direct now my voice, I pray thee, that with faith and love I may glorify God the Savior, the Lover of mankind, Who grants the world great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-evening Vespers, Menaion-fallback sticheron 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast the divine temple of God, the Bestower of life upon all, O blessed prophet, Forerunner and herald, and didst have Him living in thy heart. Him do thou ever entreat, O most noetically rich John, that those who have recourse to thy holy temple and honor thee may become temples of the Spirit and draw nigh unto God, that in hymns we may honor thy help and fervent prayer, for He bore witness that thou art the greatest from all mankind, O right wondrous one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-evening Vespers, Menaion-fallback sticheron 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:3}],label:`plain`}],menaion_verses:[{text:`For with the Lord there is mercy, and with Him there is plenteous redemption; * and He shall redeem Israel out of all his iniquities.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-evening Vespers, ladder tail verse 1`}},{text:`O praise the Lord, all ye nations; * praise Him, all ye peoples.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-evening Vespers, ladder tail verse 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]},{text:`For He hath made His mercy to prevail over us, * and the truth of the Lord abideth forever.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-evening Vespers, ladder tail verse 3`}}]},lic_theotokion:{text:`From my childhood I have been revealed to be a tireless committer of sins, having been grievously wounded in mind and lovingly remained such by my many evil habits. Downcast, I now weep over my cruel deception, mine evil habits and mindlessness, and the destruction of my soul. O Lady, disdain me not who am perishing in evil, but, taking pity, deliver me from every assault of the passions by thine aid, that if only in old age I may repent before God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-evening Vespers, LIC Glory/Both-now closer`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],type:`theotokion`},prokeimenon:{ref:`shared.daily_vespers_prokeimena.mon`,rubric:`Then, “O Joyous Light ...,” the Prokeimenon, in Tone IV:`},aposticha:{rubric:`Vouchsafe, O Lord ..., Litany: Let us complete ..., Then: On the Aposticha, these Stichera of repentance, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`O Lord, I cease not to sin, nor do I perceive Thy love for mankind which Thou hast granted me. Vanquish my lack of discernment, O Thou Who alone art good, and have mercy upon me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Lord, from reverent fear of Thee I tremble, yet I cease not from committing sins. Who, when called to trial, doth not fear the judge? Or who, desiring to be healed, angereth the physician, as I do? O longsuffering Lord, have compassion upon my weakness, and have mercy upon me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having put on the breastplate of faith and armed themselves with the image of the Cross, Thy saints, O Lord, manfully gave themselves over to torments and cast down the pride and deception of the devil. As God almighty, send down peace upon the world through their entreaties, and great mercy upon our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`}],verses:{ref:`shared.weekday_aposticha_verses.sets.standard_vespers`}},aposticha_theotokion:{text:`Assuage the sufferings of my much-sighing soul, * O thou that wipest every tear from the face of the earth; * for thou dost banish the sufferings of mankind, * and dispel the sorrows of the sinful. * For in thee do we all have our hope and confirmation, ** O most holy Virgin Mother.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-evening Vespers, aposticha Glory/Both-now closer`},type:`theotokion`},closing_rubric:`Then, “Now lettest Thou Thy servant depart ...,” Trisagion through Our`},tue:{rubric:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 3 Stichera of the precious Cross, in Tone V: Spec. Mel.: “Rejoice ...”:`,lic:{octoechos:[{text:`Thou wast lifted up like a lamb upon the Cross, and didst lay low the uprisings of the deceiver; and when Thou wast slaughtered Thou didst sanctify the whole earth with Thy blood. Pierced by the spear, Thou didst command the flaming sword to turn away from me, that I might dwell in paradise and partake without fear of the tree of life. Wherefore, saved by Thy sufferings, I cry out, rejoicing: Glory be to Thy divine Cross, whereby we have been delivered from the ancient curse and receive from the Tree blessing and great mercy!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-evening Vespers, LIC Octoechos sticheron 1`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice`},{text:`Desiring to bring an end to the pain and afflictions of all, O supremely good Lord my Savior, Thou didst endure vile crucifixion; Thou didst taste of gall, O Innocent One, removing the bitter taste of evil; and wounded, O Word, by the thrust of the spear, Thou healest our wounds, in that Thou art Master. Wherefore, we hymn Thy glorious will, and bowing down, we honor the spear, the sponge and the reed, whereby Thou hast imparted to Thy world peace and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-evening Vespers, LIC Octoechos sticheron 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:3}],label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice`},{text:`“How did the iniquitous multitude of the Jews condemn Thee to be crucified on the Cross, O Jesus, taking no pity on Thee, the Compassionate One?”, exclaimed the Virgin, weeping, when she beheld lifted up upon the Cross Him Who was born from her womb without suffering; “and what hath the iniquitous council done to Thee, O my Child most desired, my most beloved Son? Haste Thou, and save those who glorify Thy crucifixion with faith, and those who magnify me, as Thou didst promise, in that Thou alone art supremely good!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-evening Vespers, LIC Octoechos sticheron 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice`}],octoechos_verses:[{text:`If Thou shouldest mark iniquities, O Lord, O Lord, who shall stand? * For with Thee there is forgiveness.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}]},{text:`For Thy name’s sake have I patiently waited for Thee, O Lord; my soul hath waited patiently for Thy word, * my soul hath hoped in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]},{text:`From the morning watch until night, from the morning watch * let Israel hope in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 3`}}],menaion_rubric:`Then the Stichera from the Menaion; or if there is no Menaion, these Stichera of the most holy Theotokos, in the same tone:`,menaion_fallback:[{text:`Desiring to utterly lift from the first-formed Adam the most painful sentence, O sinless Christ Who lovest mankind, as the Creator of Adam Thou wast pierced with nails; and Thy divine side wounded for our sake with a spear, Thou dost turn away the flaming sword, O Word, that it might no longer deny entry to us, Thy servants. Wherefore, glorifying Thee, we hymn Thy might, and honor and praise Thy Cross, whereby all nature hath found great mercy and an inheritance without pain, O Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-evening Vespers, Menaion-fallback sticheron 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:3}],label:`plain`},{text:`Once beholding her Lamb hastening to the slaughter, the Ewe-lamb followed ardently, crying out to Him these things: “Whither goest Thou, O Christ, my Child most sweet? Wherefore dost Thou run this course with haste, O long- suffering and most desired Jesus? O sinless and greatly merciful Lord, my most beloved Son, grant discourse unto me, Thy handmaid. Spurn not in silence me who gave birth to Thee in a strange manner, O God, Bestower of life, Who grantest the world great mercy!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-evening Vespers, Menaion-fallback sticheron 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:4}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast truly the throne of the cherubim, in that thou art more exalted than all creatures: for the divine Word, desiring to restore our form, made His abode within thee, O pure one; and having issued forth from thee as a mortal man, He accepted the Cross and suffering for our sake, in that He is compassionate, and as God hath bestowed resurrection. Wherefore, giving thanks to thee who hast reconciled our condemned nature with the Creator, we cry out to Him and thee: By thy prayers grant us remission of transgressions and mercy!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-evening Vespers, Menaion-fallback sticheron 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}],menaion_verses:[{text:`For with the Lord there is mercy, and with Him there is plenteous redemption; * and He shall redeem Israel out of all his iniquities.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-evening Vespers, ladder tail verse 1`}},{text:`O praise the Lord, all ye nations; * praise Him, all ye peoples.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-evening Vespers, ladder tail verse 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]},{text:`For He hath made His mercy to prevail over us, * and the truth of the Lord abideth forever.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-evening Vespers, ladder tail verse 3`}}]},lic_theotokion:{text:`Desiring that all receive salvation, O my sinless Christ, Thou wast pleased to pay a great price, Thy precious blood, for our deliverance. Wherefore, beholding Thee nailed, Thy Mother, lamenting, rent her hair, saying: “O Child, mine all-immaculate Lamb, Who desirest to deliver the world by Thy precious blood, how hast Thou set to whence I cannot see, O never-setting Sun, Who grantest unto all enlightenment, peace and great mercy?”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-evening Vespers, LIC Glory/Both-now closer`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`},prokeimenon:{ref:`shared.daily_vespers_prokeimena.tue`,rubric:`Then, “O Joyous Light ...,” the Prokeimenon, in Tone I:`},aposticha:{rubric:`Vouchsafe, O Lord ..., Litany: Let us complete ..., Then: On the Aposticha, these Stichera of the precious Cross, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`O Lord, of old, in the time of Moses the prophet, the image of Thy Cross, having been precisely revealed, vanquished Thine enemies; and now, possessed of that same Cross, we ask Thy help: Strengthen Thy Church, for the sake of Thy great mercy, O Lover of mankind!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Though a tree visible by nature, Thy Cross, O Christ, is invested with divine power; and being tangibly revealed to the world, it wondrously and noetically worketh our salvation. Bowing down before it, we glorify Thee, O Savior. Have mercy on us!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Pray for us, O holy martyrs, that we may be delivered from our iniquities; for unto you hath been given the grace to make supplication on our behalf.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`}],verses:{ref:`shared.weekday_aposticha_verses.sets.standard_vespers`}},aposticha_theotokion:{text:`Taking upon Himself my whole form, God the Creator clad himself therein, desiring to refashion the fallen form of Adam; and was willingly lifted up upon the Cross as one guilty. But now stretching forth His hands, He healeth our hands, which of old were rendered weak by stretching forth to pluck the fruit of the tree. And the all-pure one, beholding Him, exclaimed: “What is this Thine ineffable long-suffering, O my Son? I cannot bear to see Thee Who holdeth the ends of the whole earth in the palm of Thy hand, lifted up upon the Cross!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-evening Vespers, aposticha Glory/Both-now closer`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],type:`stavrotheotokion`,spec_mel:`O venerable father`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`},closing_rubric:`Then, “Now lettest Thou Thy servant depart ...,” Trisagion through Our`},wed:{rubric:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 3 Stichera of the holy apostles, in Tone V: Spec. Mel.: “Rejoice ...”:`,lic:{octoechos:[{text:`Traversing all the earth, ye sowed divine teachings, bearing the Word alone as a lamp and all riches, O disciples of the Lord; and thereby ye put emperors and torturers to shame, and rent asunder the vain arguments of the philosophers and rhetors as though they were spiders’ webs, calling all to recognize the Creator, and abolishing the vain worship of demons. Wherefore, I pray that, by your prayers, ye deliver me from those who are irrational.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-evening Vespers, LIC Octoechos sticheron 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice`},{text:`By your supplications unto God, deliver us all from the turmoil of temptations, the cruel deception of shameful heresies, the evil counsel of the demons, the fire which burneth in the absence of light, the everlasting worm, the gnashing of teeth, and all other torments; and beseech Him that, for the sake of your temperance and toils, we may receive the reward of the virtues, the inheritance of the kingdom of heaven, and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-evening Vespers, LIC Octoechos sticheron 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice`},{text:`Clearly receiving all the effulgence, and the reflected light of the ineffable dispensation of the Trinity, insofar as human nature can so do, the all-praised twelve perfectly manifested themselves, bringing with them the seventy-two, and enlightening the ends of the world, darkened by the darkness of wicked heresy, pray ye unto Christ that He grant the world great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-evening Vespers, LIC Octoechos sticheron 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice`}],octoechos_verses:[{text:`If Thou shouldest mark iniquities, O Lord, O Lord, who shall stand? * For with Thee there is forgiveness.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]},{text:`For Thy name’s sake have I patiently waited for Thee, O Lord; my soul hath waited patiently for Thy word, * my soul hath hoped in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 2`}},{text:`From the morning watch until night, from the morning watch * let Israel hope in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 3`}}],menaion_rubric:`Then the Stichera from the Menaion; or if there is no Menaion, these Stichera of the holy hierarch Nicholas, the wonderworker, in the same Melody:`,menaion_fallback:[{text:`Rejoice, O sacred one, pure habitation of the virtues, godly standard of a blameless priesthood, great and manifest pastor, whose radiant name signifies victory, who mercifully heeds those who make supplication, inclining thine ear to the pleas of the infirm, ready deliverer, saving refuge for all who with faith ever honor thy glorious memory! Entreat Christ, that He send down upon us great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-evening Vespers, Menaion-fallback sticheron 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoice, O holy hierarch Nicholas, most sacred mind, pure abode of the Trinity, pillar of the Church, confirmation of the faithful, helper of the afflicted, star who with the brilliant rays of thy right acceptable prayers dost ever dispel the darkness of trial and tribulation, calm haven whereto the imperiled who flee are saved from the threefold waves of life! Entreat Christ God, that He send down upon our souls great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-evening Vespers, Menaion-fallback sticheron 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoice, standard for hierarchs, inexhaustible depths of divine wonders, beauty of the Church, brilliant star who with thy sacred effulgence dost shed light upon each of us, O blessed and most holy one who art illumined with most radiant flashes of lightning, unshakable tower, stairway of faith for those who with love keep thine honored memory: Entreat Christ, that He grant our souls great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-evening Vespers, Menaion-fallback sticheron 3`},label:`plain`}],menaion_verses:[{text:`For with the Lord there is plenteous redemption, * and He shall redeem Israel out of all his iniquities.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-evening Vespers, ladder tail verse 1`}},{text:`O praise the Lord, all ye nations; * praise Him, all ye peoples.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-evening Vespers, ladder tail verse 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]},{text:`For He hath made His mercy to prevail over us, * and the truth of the Lord abideth forever.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-evening Vespers, ladder tail verse 3`}}]},lic_theotokion:{text:`O strange, awesome and great mystery! * The Un-circumscribable One hath made His abode within a womb, * and a Mother remaineth a Virgin even after birthgiving, * for from her she gave birth to God Incarnate. * To Him, then, let us cry aloud, * to Him let us raise a hymn, * chanting with the angels: * Holy art Thou, O Christ God, * Who wast incarnate for our sake! ** Glory be to Thee!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-evening Vespers, LIC Glory/Both-now closer`},type:`theotokion`},prokeimenon:{ref:`shared.daily_vespers_prokeimena.wed`,rubric:`Then, “O Joyous Light ...,” the Prokeimenon, in Tone V:`},aposticha:{rubric:`Vouchsafe, O Lord ..., Litany: Let us complete ..., Then: On the Aposticha, these Stichera of the holy apostles, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`As eye-witnesses to the mysteries of the Savior, O disciples, ye preached the Invisible One Who hath no beginning, saying: In the beginning was the Word. Ye were not created before the angels, nor were ye taught of men, but by the wisdom of the Most High. Wherefore, as ye have boldness, pray ye on behalf of our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Together let us praise the apostles of the Lord with hymns, for, having arrayed themselves in the armor of the Cross, they abolished the delusion of the demons and were revealed to be crowned victors. By the supplications of them and all the saints, O God, have mercy on us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Your souls filled with insatiable love, O holy martyrs, ye did not deny Christ; and enduring the divers wounds of sufferings, ye cast down the audacity of the tormentors; and having preserved the Faith intact and unharmed, ye were translated to the heavens. Wherefore, as ye have boldness before Him, ask that He grant us great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`}],verses:{ref:`shared.weekday_aposticha_verses.sets.standard_vespers`}},aposticha_theotokion:{text:`We bless thee, O Virgin Theotokos, * and we, the faithful, glorify thee as is meet, * thou unassailable city, * impregnable rampart, ** and steadfast intercession and refuge of our souls.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-evening Vespers, aposticha Glory/Both-now closer`},type:`theotokion`},closing_rubric:`Then, “Now lettest Thou Thy servant depart ...,” Trisagion through Our`},thu:{rubric:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” 3 Stichera of the precious Cross, in Tone V: Spec. Mel.: “O venerable father ...”:`,lic:{octoechos:[{text:`Let all the groves of trees rejoice, beholding the most precious Tree which was made joyous by the suffering of the Master, shining forth grace like a flame of fire, pouring forth gifts upon all like water, and enlightening the thoughts of our souls, washing away infirmities and driving away invisible passions, and manifestly vanquishing foreign nations, ever granting to the faithful victories, blessing and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, LIC Octoechos sticheron 1`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O venerable father`},{text:`Worshipping with faith the place where the feet of the Lord stood, as the prophet said, let us glorify Christ Who was crucified, and with Himself crucified our transgressions, Who abolished the curse which originated with a tree, and reconciled with the Father those who had withdrawn far from Him through evil thoughts; and venerating the nails of his hands and feet, the spear and the reed, the sponge and the crown of thorns, and the insults and mockery, and all else He endured, let us venerate them with honor, for by them we are saved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, LIC Octoechos sticheron 2`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O venerable father`},{text:`Let us crucify all our members with Christ, and let us die unto the world; and desiring to walk in the footsteps of Christ, the Ruler of this world, let us take His divine Cross upon our shoulder by rejecting the uprisings of the flesh and the evil lusts which draw our souls into sin, thinking to stand before Him and to behold Him nailed to the Cross, breathing His last and surrendering His soul into the hands of the Father, that we may never be separated from Him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, LIC Octoechos sticheron 3`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`O venerable father`}],octoechos_verses:[{text:`If Thou shouldest mark iniquities, O Lord, O Lord, who shall stand? * For with Thee there is forgiveness.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}]},{text:`For Thy name’s sake have I patiently waited for Thee, O Lord; my soul hath waited patiently for Thy word, * my soul hath hoped in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]},{text:`From the morning watch until night, from the morning watch * let Israel hope in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 3`}}],menaion_rubric:`Then the Stichera from the Menaion; or if there is no Menaion, these Stichera of the most holy Theotokos, in the same melody:`,menaion_fallback:[{text:`When thou didst behold hanging upon the Tree, the planted Cluster of grapes Whom, like a vine, thou didst bring forth, with His divine side pierced by a spear, thou didst exclaim crying aloud O most pure one: “What is this, O my Son and God? How is it that Thou Who dost heal all infirmities and sufferings, hath undergone suffering, though Thou art dispassionate according to Thy divine nature? How have the thankless people thus rewarded Thee for Thy benefactions, O Benefactor?”. By His sufferings pray thou that I may ever be free from sufferings, that I may glorify thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, Menaion-fallback sticheron 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let us all weep and lift up our hands, beating our breast, shedding fervent tears, bending our knees, earnestly smiting our foreheads on the ground; and let us who have angered God by unseemly deeds and the rejection of His com- mandments send sighs on high, crying out: By the supplications of Thy Mother, deliver from all torment at the coming judgment those who have grieved Thee but have converted, for whom, incarnate, Thou didst endure the Cross; and grant them a share in Thy kingdom.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, Menaion-fallback sticheron 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Unto whom hast thou likened thyself, O my soul, ever prospering in bitter works, and mindlessly adding so many stripes to thy wounds that thou art covered with sores, giving no thought to the approach of the Judge, before Whom thou must needs stand to receive retribution for thy guilt according to thy deeds? But turning, fall down before the Virgin, crying out: O Lady, O Lady, disdain me not who have angered the right merciful God Who was born from thee for the salvation of all, and was crucified in the flesh!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, Menaion-fallback sticheron 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:3}],label:`plain`}],menaion_verses:[{text:`For with the Lord there is mercy, and with Him there is plenteous redemption; * and He shall redeem Israel out of all his iniquities.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, ladder tail verse 1`}},{text:`O praise the Lord, all ye nations; * praise Him, all ye peoples.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, ladder tail verse 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]},{text:`For He hath made His mercy to prevail over us, * and the truth of the Lord abideth forever.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, ladder tail verse 3`}}]},lic_theotokion:{text:`Desiring that all receive salvation, O my sinless Christ, Thou wast pleased to pay a great price, Thy precious blood, for our deliverance. Wherefore, beholding Thee nailed, Thy Mother, lamenting, rent her hair, saying: “O Child, mine all-immaculate Lamb, Who desirest to deliver the world by Thy precious blood, how hast Thou set to whence I cannot see, O never-setting Sun, Who grantest unto all enlightenment, peace and great mercy?”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, LIC Glory/Both-now closer`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`},prokeimenon:{ref:`shared.daily_vespers_prokeimena.thu`,rubric:`Then, “O Joyous Light ...,” the Prokeimenon, in Tone VI:`},aposticha:{rubric:`Vouchsafe, O Lord ..., Litany: Let us complete ..., Then: On the Aposticha, these Stichera of the precious Cross, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`Spec. Mel.: “Rejoice ...”:`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Lord, of old, in the time of Moses the prophet, the image of Thy Cross, having been precisely revealed, vanquished Thine enemies; and now, possessed of that same Cross, we ask Thy help: Strengthen Thy Church, for the sake of Thy great mercy, O Lover of mankind!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Though a tree visible by nature, Thy Cross, O Christ, is invested with divine power; and being tangibly revealed to the world, it wondrously and noetically worketh our salvation. Bowing down before it, we glorify Thee, O Savior. Have mercy on us!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Despising all the things of earth, and manfully braving tortures, ye did not fail to attain your divine hopes, but became heirs to the kingdom of heaven, O all-famed martyrs. And as ye have boldness before God Who is the Lover of mankind, ask peace for the world and great mercy for our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`}],verses:{ref:`shared.weekday_aposticha_verses.sets.standard_vespers`}},aposticha_theotokion:{text:`Of old, the Virgin Mother, the all-blessed maiden, beholding the Lamb, her Son, lifted up upon the Cross, cried out, weeping: ''Woe is me, O my Son! How is it that Thou diest Who art in essence God immortal?”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-evening Vespers, aposticha Glory/Both-now closer`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`},closing_rubric:`Then, “Now lettest Thou Thy servant depart ...,” Trisagion through Our`},fri:{rubric:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” these Stichera of the righteous ones, in Tone V: Spec. Mel.: “Rejoice ...”:`,lic:{octoechos:[{text:`With the streams of their blood the passion-bearers quenched the flame of grievous ungodliness; and enkindling the radiance of piety throughout the whole world, they utterly consumed the false gods and their fetid stench. They have shone forth the most pure light upon those on earth, and enlightened thereby, we elude the darkness of ungodliness and evade the delusion of idols, worshipping Christ, Who granteth the world great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers, LIC sticheron 1`},label:`plain`,provenance_note:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” these Stichera of the righteous ones, in Tone V: Spec. Mel.: “Rejoice ...”:`},{text:`Easily setting at naught the words of the ungodly heretics and their pursuit, ye became warriors of the beginningless Father, the Son Who is equally without beginning, and the Holy Spirit, the Unity of Divinity in three Hypostases, teaching the faithful with piety of mind and confirming the preaching of Orthodoxy. Wherefore, ye are called blessed, O most sacred pastors, for in life-bearing pastures ye tended the flock of Christ, for Whom ye endured all manner of pangs and many and varied trials.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers, LIC sticheron 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,provenance_note:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” these Stichera of the righteous ones, in Tone V: Spec. Mel.: “Rejoice ...”:`},{text:`Receiving mastery of mind through the doing of virtuous deeds, the company of the venerable, who struggled, with ease utterly trampled the carnal passions underfoot. Thereby they valiantly overcame all the wiles of the demons and were revealed to be conversers with the angels, since they lived as ones incorporeal. And they now rejoice in the mansions on high, living in splendor, and standing before Christ, beseech Him to grant our souls great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers, LIC sticheron 3`},label:`plain`,provenance_note:`On “Lord, I have cried ...,” these Stichera of the righteous ones, in Tone V: Spec. Mel.: “Rejoice ...”:`},{text:`Girding themselves with the shield of faith, and arming themselves with the sign of the Cross, Thy saints O Lord, bravely gave themselves over to torments, casting down the pride and delusion of the devil. By their supplications, O God almighty, send down peace upon the world, and great mercy upon our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers, LIC sticheron 4`},label:`plain`,provenance_note:`These Stichera of the holy martyrs, in the same tone:`},{text:`Girding themselves with the shield of faith ...,`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers, LIC sticheron 5 (incipit repeat of sticheron 4, §2.7, printed with an explicit "Repeat:" label)`},label:`plain`,incipit_ref:`tone5.vespers_weekday.fri.lic.octoechos[3]`,sourceLabel:`Repeat:`,provenance_note:`These Stichera of the holy martyrs, in the same tone:`},{text:`Despising all things earthly, and bravely withstanding torture, ye were not deprived of your goodly hope, but became heirs of the Kingdom of heaven. O ye all-famed martyrs, since ye have boldness before God the Lover of mankind, ask that peace be granted to the world, and great mercy to our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers, LIC sticheron 6`},label:`plain`,provenance_note:`These Stichera of the holy martyrs, in the same tone:`}],octoechos_verses:[{text:`If Thou shouldest mark iniquities, O Lord, O Lord, who shall stand? * For with Thee there is forgiveness.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}]},{text:`For Thy name’s sake have I patiently waited for Thee, O Lord; my soul hath waited patiently for Thy word, * my soul hath hoped in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]},{text:`From the morning watch until night, from the morning watch * let Israel hope in the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 3`}},{text:`For with the Lord there is mercy, and with Him there is plenteous redemption; * and He shall redeem Israel out of all his iniquities.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 4`}},{text:`O praise the Lord, all ye nations; * praise Him, all ye peoples.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]},{text:`For He hath made His mercy to prevail over us, * and the truth of the Lord abideth forever.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers, LIC ladder verse 6`}}]},lic_theotokion:{text:`In the Red Sea of old * an image of the Bride who knew not wedlock was depicted. * There Moses was the one who parted the sea, * here Gabriel is the minister of the miracle. * At that time Israel marched dry-shod through the deep, * now the Virgin doth seedlessly give birth to Christ. * The sea after Israel's passage remained impassable; * the immaculate one after bearing Emmanuel remained incorrupt. * O God, Who doth exist and is pre-eternal, * and hath appeared as man, ** have mercy upon us.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers, LIC Glory/Both-now closer — the dogmatikon printed IN FULL as its own site (§9.2)`},type:`dogmatic_theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Dogmatic Theotokion:`},prokeimenon:{ref:`shared.daily_vespers_prokeimena.fri`,rubric:`Then, “O Joyous Light ...,” the Prokeimenon, in Tone VII:`},aposticha:{rubric:`Vouchsafe, O Lord ..., Litany: Let us complete ..., Then: On the Aposticha, these Stichera, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`Intercede on our behalf, O holy martyrs, that we may be delivered from our iniquities: for unto you hath been given the grace to pray for us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`With your souls filled with insatiable love, O holy martyrs, ye did not deny Christ; and enduring divers wounds in sufferings, ye cast down the audacity of the tyrants, and keeping the faith unaltered and unharmed, ye were translated to the heavens. Wherefore, since ye have boldness before Him, ask that He grant us great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`I called to mind the words of the prophet, ‘I am but dust and ashes.’ I went also to the tombs, and beheld the bones laid bare, and I said: ‘Which is the king or which the warrior, which the rich man or which the beggar, which the righteous or which the sinner?’ But grant rest with the righteous, O Lord, to Thy servants, as the Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers, aposticha item 3`},label:`for_the_reposed`}],verses:[{text:`Blessed are they whom Thou hast chosen * and taken to Thyself, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers aposticha, departed verse 1 (final period present, unlike the 2-7 print — §5 per-tone; 3-7 and 4-7 diverged the same way)`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]},{text:`Their souls * shall dwell among good things.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers aposticha, departed verse 2`}}]},aposticha_theotokion:{text:`O thou who art full of joy, intercede by thy supplications, and beg that a multitude of compassions, and the cleansing of our many sins, be granted to our souls, we entreat thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-evening Vespers, aposticha Glory/Both-now closer`},type:`theotokion`},closing_rubric:`Then, “Now lettest Thou Thy servant depart ...,” Trisagion through Our`}},compline:{sun:{canon:{title:`Canon of supplication to the most holy Theotokos`,heading_rubric:`Canon of supplication to the most holy Theotokos`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Christ, who with an upraised arm * bringeth wars to naught, * hath shaken horse and rider in the Red Sea; * but Israel hath He saved * as they chanted a song of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`A truly awesome miracle was wrought within thee, O Virgin, for thou didst bear in thy womb Him Who is in nowise circumscribed, and hast ineffably given birth to Him, remaining a virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Rain down remission of sins upon me, O Lady who didst ineffably contain the Rain of heaven which came upon thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O only blessed and divinely joyous one who hast given birth to ineffable Joy for al mankind: take the grief away from my soul, I pray, and gladden my heart.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`He Who shone forth from thee in His surpassing goodness is all the desire and sweetness of life, O most immaculate one. Him do thou beseech, that He save me who now unceasingly glorifies thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`By Thy command Thou didst establish the earth upon nothing * and suspended it unsupported; * do Thou establish Thy Church on the unshakeable rock of Thy commandments, O Christ, * Who alone art good * and the Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`The works of the law have passed by as though they were a shadow; for Thou, O most pure one, hast given birth unto Christ Who in place of the law hath appointed for us the grace of purification and enlightenment, and hath lifted the curse, O all-immaculate Virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`God was born in the flesh from thee, O pure one; He Who before was invisible became visible. Wherefore, earnestly entreat Him, O maiden, that He deliver me who glorifies thee with splendor, from enemies visible and invisible.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Cruel waves of the passions assail me, the abyss of evil spirits besets me, and the tempest of sin troubles my heart. O Birthgiver of God, make me steadfast, for I hymn thee with splendor.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Having the divine Gabriel as our commander, with faith we cry out reverently together to the Theotokos and Mother who knewest not wedlock. By her we have been delivered from tribulations, sorrows and infirmities.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Habbakuk, prophetically apprehending * Thy divine self-emptying, O Christ, * cried out to Thee with trembling: * Thou hast come for the salvation of Thy people; * to save Thine anointed ones.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Virgin who within thyself wove a robe of incorruption with thy virginal blood for Him Who clothes the sky with clouds, clothe me who before was stripped naked through deception.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thy womb, O Virgin, became a holy and ineffable palace for God the King, in which He made His abode; whereby He hath made us temples.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`As thou art compassionate, have compassion on my most wretched soul, O all-immaculate Birthgiver of God, for it hath been cruelly darkened and fettered by the passions and sin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Thou didst shine forth the Scepter of the kingdom of incorruption from the root of Jesse, O pure one, and without knowing a man thou hast given birth to a Babe, the God of David, the Creator and Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Thou Who hast clothed Thyself in light as with a garment, * I rise early unto Thee and cry out to Thee: * Enlighten my darkened soul, O Christ, * in that Thou alone art compassionate!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Even after giving birth thou hast remained an incorrupt virgin, O most immaculate one; leading all the corrupt toward Life, and illumining them with incorruption.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`To the Pre-eternal One, Who shone forth timelessly from the Father, thou hast given birth as a newborn Babe, O most pure one. Him do thou entreat on behalf of the world, O Bride of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`O let me find thee, O Virgin, to be my helper, rescuing me from the sentence of the Judge at the hour of judgment, when I shall stand before the tribunal of Him Who was born from thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`glory`},{text:`O Virgin Bride of God, my beloved from out of Lebanon, wholly beautiful and immaculate art thou. By the Holy Spirit the incarnation of the Son of God was made known in thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Calm the raging sea of the passions, * O Master Christ, * with its soul-destroying tempest, * and lead me up from corruption * in that Thou art compassionate.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Without knowing a man, thou hast given birth to Emmanuel, Who hath taken pity on our lowliness, O Theotokos; wherefore, we ever glorify thee as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O most holy one, in a manner transcending understanding and past all telling, thou hast given birth to the Timeless One, the Creator Who delivereth from all corruption those who hymn thee, the Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having given birth to the Benefactor and Creator, O most holy and right-beloved Lady, bless thou mine afflicted soul.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`O all-pure one, we offer thee praise both new and old; for we have naught better for thy praise than “Rejoice!”, which we sing to thee with Gabriel.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The supremely exalted Lord of our fathers * quenched the flame, * and bedewed the youths * as they chanted in harmony: * O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Deliver me from evil despondency, from the darkness of the passions and everlasting condemnation, O most pure one, that I may glorify thee with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Mortify my passions, O thou who hast given birth to Life, and lift me up who lie in the grave of senselessness, O Bride of God, that I may glorify thee with love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`O most immaculate one, thou hast given birth to the incorporeal God clad in the flesh, Who doth deliver us who chant with fear: Blessed art Thou, O God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`glory`},{text:`Finding thy pure supplication to be priceless healing, O Virgin, chanting, we ask of thee goodly transformation of soul and health of body.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Unto Thee the Fashioner of all, * the children in the furnace chanted a hymn: * All ye works of the Lord, * supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O portal of the Light, open unto me the radiant gates of repentance, showing forth each straight path of righteousness leading into the entries of God’s will.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O Virgin Mother, thou hast given birth on earth to a newborn Child, the Son Who is co-beginningless with the Father, Who in His ineffable loving-kindness became like unto us who have become corrupt through sin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O most glorious Ever-Virgin whom God hath loved and chosen, thou hast been revealed to be wholly elect, wholly all-adorned; wherefore, we hymn thee throughout the ages, O pure one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`glory`},{text:`“Thou art wholly pure, full of divine glory, my dear one!” the Spirit of God said, proclaiming thee, O most pure one, whom we praise with hymns, chanting: Thou must needs rejoice, having given birth unto the God-man!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`O Isaiah, rejoice and be glad! * The Virgin hath conceived in her womb, * and hath borne a Son, Emmanuel, * Who is both God and man; * and Orient is His name; * Him we magnify, and the Virgin we call blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Disdain not the sighs of those who now hasten unto thee, O all-pure one, but look upon us who are in sorrows, and transform our lamentation into joy, and our compunction into gladness, for we praise thee in hymns.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thou art an immovable foundation, O pure one, having given birth to the Savior Who founded the earth upon the waters by His divine commands. Pray thou that He splendidly establishes thereon those who call thee blessed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thy birthgiving transcends understanding O Theotokos, for conception and a virginal birth took place within thee without the aid of a man; for it was God Who was born, and magnifying Him, we bless thee who gave birth to Him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Awesome art Thou, O Lord. Who then can withstand Thy threat, O Christ, only King, when Thou shalt render judgment? Wherefore, have pity and save me, O Savior, through the right acceptable supplications of her who gave birth to Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:3}],label:`both_now`}]}}},after_ode6:{rubric:`Lord, have mercy, (Thrice). Glory ..., Both now ..., Sessional Hymn, in Tone V:`,sessional:{text:`I lament for myself before the judgment, pondering mine evil and grievous deeds, and the abyss of transgressions which hath surrounded me from my youth and which drown my mind; yet by thy prayers, O pure one, grant me remission, and vouchsafe that I may receive salvation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Sunday-night Compline, sessional after Ode VI`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]}},closing_rubric:`Then, “It is truly meet ...,” and a prostration. Trisagion through Our Father ..., Troparion, and the rest as usual. Dismissal.`},mon:{canon:{title:`Canon of supplication to the most holy Theotokos`,heading_rubric:`Canon of supplication to the most holy Theotokos`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Christ, who with an upraised arm * bringeth wars to naught, * hath shaken horse and rider in the Red Sea; * but Israel hath He saved * as they chanted a song of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O good and most immaculate one, grant me contrition of soul, humility of heart, purity of mind, correction of life, remission of transgressions and fountains of tears.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Behold my tribulation and compunction, heal thou the stripes of mine ancient transgressions, and grant me time to repent and confess my sins.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Pondering the abyss of mine evils, O all-immaculate one, I weep for myself before my departure; wherefore, I beseech thee: Entreat thy Son, that He deliver me from torment.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`As thou hast time for repentance, O my soul, depart from all evil and cry out with tears to thy Creator: O my God, save me by the supplications of her who gave birth to Thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`both_now`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`By Thy command Thou didst establish the earth upon nothing * and suspended it unsupported; * do Thou establish Thy Church on the unshakeable rock of Thy commandments, O Christ, * Who alone art good * and the Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`The foremost of my passions have seized me, O most pure one, and have filled me with shame who have been created according to the image and likeness of God; yet deliver me from the harm thereof, for I hymn thee in compunction.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The enemy wickedly seeks to hunt me down, desiring to show me utterly consumed in everlasting flame, O most pure one; yet set at naught his wiles and counsels, that, rejoicing, I may glorify thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The enemies of the righteous have deceitfully set me in the uttermost pit of many offenses, yet as one now helpless and wholly wounded, I call upon thy supplication: O most immaculate Lady, save me!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`I have wasted my life in slothfulness, wretch that I am, and have now arrived at the gates of death; and, terrified of the assault of the enemy, I cry unto thee: deliver me from their temptations, that saved, I may glorify thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Habbakuk, prophetically apprehending * Thy divine self-emptying, O Christ, * cried out to Thee with trembling: * Thou hast come for the salvation of Thy people; * to save Thine anointed ones.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`I have been wounded by the darts of sin, and wounds now cover mine entire body; wherefore, I cry out to thee, O most pure one: by thy speedy prayers heal the wounds of my soul.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Have mercy upon thy servants, O pure one; for we have acquired thee as our mediatress before God, and we pray that we be delivered from all want and everlasting torment.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O good one, thou art my hope, shield and confirmation, my deliverance from evils, the enlightenment of my soul, my boast, bulwark and might.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Prodigally have I wasted the riches of good works which Christ gave me, in that He is good. Yet disdain me not, O most pure maiden, for I am perishing of hunger.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Thou Who hast clothed Thyself in light as with a garment, * I rise early unto Thee and cry out to Thee: * Enlighten my darkened soul, O Christ, * in that Thou alone art compassionate!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Behold the weakness of my lowly soul, O Lady, the infirmity of my flesh and the captivity of my mind, and save me who am bereft of hope.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`God to Whom thou hast given birth do thou ever entreat, that He save all of us who confess thee to be the Theotokos, and glorify thy birthgiving, O most pure one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Who doth not call thee blessed, O all-immaculate one? For thou didst ineffably give birth to the one Master, the Savior of the whole world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`O most pure one, send down upon me streams of tears, that, having purified myself of the defilements and blemishes of my sins, I may hymn the magnitude of thy goodness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Calm the raging sea of the passions, * O Master Christ, * with its soul-destroying tempest, * and lead me up from corruption * in that Thou art compassionate.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`I have been cast into the abyss of transgressions and iniquities, O all- immaculate one; yet stretch forth thy hand, and lead me up from the despair of Hades.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`I know the multitude of the offenses and thoughts which vex me; wherefore, hasten thou and deliver me, O most pure one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Take pity on thy servant, O Christ Master, by the supplications of her who in purity gave birth to Thee, when Thou shalt come to judge the world which Thou hast fashioned.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`O pure Lady, my soul hath been dragged down into the abyss of transgressions, to become food for the demons; wherefore, save me who am beyond hope.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The supremely exalted Lord of our fathers * quenched the flame, * and bedewed the youths * as they chanted in harmony: * O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`When I bring to mind the multitude of mine unseemly deeds and transgressions, O all-immaculate one, I am afraid and horrified. O Virgin, by thy prayers free me from them.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`The sleepless word and the unquenchable fire ever erode and devour my soul. Let me not become food for them, O most holy Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O all-immaculate Virgin, from the outmost darkness and dread torment deliver thy servants who cry out to thy Son: O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`glory`},{text:`I have defiled my flesh with shameful passions, and have darkened by mind with vile thoughts; yet take pity, O pure one, and save me, Thy useless servant.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Unto Thee the Fashioner of all, * the children in the furnace chanted a hymn: * All ye works of the Lord, * supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Unto thee, the Theotokos, do I bring the weakness of my lowly soul, the infirmity of my heart and the delusion of my mind; and I cry aloud, asking thine aid, O Virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Be Thou merciful to Thy servants, O Word, through the supplications of her who gave birth to Thee, and save those who chant: O all ye works of the Lord, hymn the Lord and supremely exalt Him throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`O thou who hast given birth to Him Who hath willed mercy, have mercy upon all who chant with faith: O all ye works of the Lord, hymn the Lord and supremely exalt Him throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`glory`},{text:`Deliver me from the outermost darkness and the worm which sleepeth not, O good Virgin, in that thou hast given birth to the Creator of the world; for all things whatsoever He desireth, He can accomplish by thy prayers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`O Isaiah, rejoice and be glad! * The Virgin hath conceived in her womb, * and hath borne a Son, Emmanuel, * Who is both God and man; * and Orient is His name; * Him we magnify, and the Virgin we call blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`God to Whom thou hast ineffably given birth, O pure Lady, do thou earnestly beseech, that He deliver us from misfortunes and sorrows, and from the dread judgment which is to come; and that He grant unto us the splendors of His saints.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`I have sinned more than all others, disobeying Thy life-creating commandments, O Christ, making myself like the irrational beasts; yet by the prayers of Thy Mother, O Word, may I not be taken unrepentant from this life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`In that thou hast given birth to the Word of God, the Abyss of mercy, O good one, have mercy upon the souls of all who flee beneath thy protection; for thee have we all acquired as an unashamed intercessor before God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Ask now for our purification and remission, deliverance from all needs, and correction of life which is pure and radiant, O Mother of God, that we may glorify thy great benificence.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]}}},after_ode6:{rubric:`Lord, have mercy, (Thrice). Glory ..., Both now ..., Sessional Hymn, in Tone V:`,sessional:{text:`The greatly painful passions of my soul and the infirmities of my flesh do thou quickly heal; still the wandering of my mind, O most immaculate Theotokos, and grant that in serenity of thought I may offer pure prayers unto the King, and beg remission offenses.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Monday-night Compline, sessional after Ode VI`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],spec_mel:`The co-beginningless Word`}},closing_rubric:`Then, “It is truly meet ...,” and a prostration. Trisagion through Our Father ..., Troparion, and the rest as usual. Dismissal.`},tue:{canon:{title:`Canon of supplication to the most holy Theotokos`,heading_rubric:`Canon of supplication to the most holy Theotokos`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Christ, who with an upraised arm * bringeth wars to naught, * hath shaken horse and rider in the Red Sea; * but Israel hath He saved * as they chanted a song of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Theotokos, accept the supplications of thy servants, offered unto thee from the depths of our hearts, and, bearing them to thy Son, grant us remission of transgressions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O Virgin Mother of God, who art truly the bestower of good things, who enrichest mortals, O portal of salvation leading them to life: Cease thou never to intercede for those who entreat thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Moved now by the entreaties of those who hymn thee, in that thou art mighty assistance toward salvation, O Lady, rescuing us from misfortune by thy supplications, preserve us whole, who honor thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Going quickly before us and interceding with fervor, O most holy Virgin, taking pity on us who are grievously beset by evil circumstances, deliver us and free us from grief.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`By Thy command Thou didst establish the earth upon nothing * and suspended it unsupported; * do Thou establish Thy Church on the unshakeable rock of Thy commandments, O Christ, * Who alone art good * and the Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Illumining the dark cloud of my heart with the divine light of thy vigilant supplication, O Mother of God, show me forth as a child of the day, made radiant by the virtues, O thou who guidest our souls with light.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Ever desiring to hymn thee as is meet, yet at a loss how to do so, we offer thee praise from our base lips: accept it readily, and hearken to the entreaties of us who pray to thee with faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Birthgiver of God, who showest barren souls to be right fruitful, and cleansest stony hearts by thy supplication, show thou my soul to produce the fruit of faith and an undefiled life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`How could He Who holdeth all the ends of the earth in His palm be contained by His Mother’s womb? How could He be fed with milk from her breasts, Who feedeth every living thing at His good pleasure? Incarnate, He Who is rich hath made Himself poor, emptying Himself.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Habbakuk, prophetically apprehending * Thy divine self-emptying, O Christ, * cried out to Thee with trembling: * Thou hast come for the salvation of Thy people; * to save Thine anointed ones.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Knowing thee alone, O most pure one, to be the mediatress before God, with praises and hymns we honor thee who dost liberate the guilty from their debts offenses.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`In making His abode within thee, O most immaculate Virgin, God showed thee to be a sanctified temple. Him do thou ever entreat, that He preserve thy servants unharmed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Hearken unto the entreaty of the lowly who place their hope in thee O Theotokos, hasten to deliver us, since thou hast a mother's boldness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`O Mother of God, thou art the sweet assuagement of those in sorrows, the help of those in need, the mediator of those in troubles, and the deliverance of those in every evil circumstance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Thou Who hast clothed Thyself in light as with a garment, * I rise early unto Thee and cry out to Thee: * Enlighten my darkened soul, O Christ, * in that Thou alone art compassionate!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Having truly given birth in circumscribed flesh to Him Who is infinite in nature and was begotten before all ages, entreat Him unceasingly on behalf of thy servants.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou dost quickly draw nigh to those in need, ever helping and directing toward salvation those who call upon thee amid temptations, O most pure one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Showing our compassionate God to be merciful by nature through thy supplications, O most immaculate one, grant a peaceful life and deliverance from transgressions to thy servants.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`O all-immaculate one who hast given birth to the burning Ember which Isaiah beheld, utterly consume the tinder of mine offenses, and illumine me, I pray.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Calm the raging sea of the passions, * O Master Christ, * with its soul-destroying tempest, * and lead me up from corruption * in that Thou art compassionate.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Raising us up who have been slain by the sinful passions, O Lady, enliven us by thy supplications, for thou hast given birth to the Destroyer of corruption.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Having thee as our sure hope, an invincible bulwark against the enemy, and a steadfast help, we do not fear the assaults made upon us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O pure one, do thou ever intercede for mortals in pain, and preserve thy servants unharmed by the evils which wither us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`O Bride of God, illumine my soul which hath been darkened by the cloud of thoughts which assail me through the attacks of the man-slaying demons.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The supremely exalted Lord of our fathers * quenched the flame, * and bedewed the youths * as they chanted in harmony: * O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Lady, accept the petitions of thy faithful servants, rescuing them from perils and saving from tribulations those who chant with faith: Blessed art Thou, O God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`O thou who hast given birth for us to God the Creator of good things, beseech Him with thy maternal supplications, O pure one, that He take pity on those who praise thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Having acquired thee as an invincible intercessor and an unshakable foundation, O Lady, arrayed in thine assistance, we vanquish the wily attacks of the archer, which he directeth at us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Look upon the lowliness of thy servants, O Lady, and from everlasting fire free me who unceasingly chant: O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`both_now`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Unto Thee the Fashioner of all, * the children in the furnace chanted a hymn: * All ye works of the Lord, * supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Weaving words and thoughts into praise for thee, O Virgin, we the faithful cry: Hymn the Lord, all ye works, and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Solomon described thee beforehand as the beauty wholly beloved of God, in that thou art closest to Him, O Virgin, delivering those in the world with thy maternal boldness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Having thee, after God, as our hope of salvation amid perils, we the faithful cry aloud: Hymn the Lord, all ye works, and supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`Accept this hymnody, O all-hymned Virgin, from the base lips of those who cry: Rejoice, O healing of sick bodies and salvation of despairing souls!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`both_now`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`O Isaiah, rejoice and be glad! * The Virgin hath conceived in her womb, * and hath borne a Son, Emmanuel, * Who is both God and man; * and Orient is His name; * Him we magnify, and the Virgin we call blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Unto thee do we pour forth supplication from our pain: Have mercy on us sinners, lest we be put to shame on the day of trial, for we call upon thee, the all- merciful Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Disdain not our kinship in dust, O pure Theotokos, but be thou our intercessor, protecting and strengthening us amid grief, and delivering all the infirm; for in thee do we trust, who art ready to save us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O God, hearken now to the supplication of Thy people, and deliver us from the harm of the enemy, for lo! we bring before Thee true purification: her who gave birth to Thee, whom we bless with love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Beneath the dominion of thy might do all of us mortals earnestly flee, asking thy mercies and merciful compassion; and, pouring them forth, sanctify us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]}}},after_ode6:{rubric:`Lord, have mercy, (Thrice). Glory ..., Both now ..., Sessional Hymn, in Tone V:`,sessional:{text:`Through the Cross of thy Son, O thou who art full of the grace of God, hath the deception of idolatry been utterly vanquished, and the might of the demons hath fallen; wherefore, we, the faithful, ever hymn and bless thee as is meet, confessing thee to be the true Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday-night Compline, sessional after Ode VI`}}},closing_rubric:`Then, “It is truly meet ...,” and a prostration. Trisagion through Our Father ..., Troparion, and the rest as usual. Dismissal.`},wed:{canon:{title:`Canon of supplication to the most holy Theotokos`,heading_rubric:`Canon of supplication to the most holy Theotokos`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Unto God the Savior * Who made His people pass dryshod through the sea, * but drowned Pharaoh with all his host, * unto Him alone let us sing: * For He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O radiant tabernacle of Christ the King, illumine my mind, which hath been darkened by the deceit of the enemy and blinded by the darkness of my transgressions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O Birthgiver of God, free my humbled soul from wicked thoughts, and make it a dwelling-place for God, that I may ever glorify thee as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`When I must needs depart from this transitory life at the command of God, O most pure one, show me to elude the hands of the demons, providing me angels as companions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Why hast thou wasted all thy life in great despondency, O my soul? Wherefore, hasten thou and cry out to the Mother of the Lord: Cleanse thou and save me, O Birthgiver of God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`both_now`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`By the power of Thy Cross, O Christ, * do Thou make steadfast mine understanding, * that I may hymn and glorify Thine arising on the third day.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Out of the pit of torments and sufferings do thou lead me up who hymn thee constantly, O all-blessed Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Rend asunder the rags of my boundless transgressions, and gird me about with the gladness of the virtues, O thou who art full of the grace of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Grant me tear-drops, O pure one, that I may dispel the perplexity of my heart and may hymn thee earnestly.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Cast down the arrogance of the incorporeal foe, O most immaculate one, and quickly free me from their tyranny.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`I have heard report of the mighty deed * of Thy Cross, O Lord, * how Paradise was opened thereby, and I cried: * Glory to Thy power, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Why hast thou likened thyself to the barren fig-tree, O my soul, in nowise afraid of being cut down and cast into everlasting flames? Hasten thou, therefore, and rouse thyself before it is too late.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`What tongue can describe the boundless sea of the evils I have committed and the abyss of my transgressions? Save me, who am in despair, O most immaculate Virgin!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`I weep for myself when I bring to mind my manifold transgressions and the fire which will never be quenched, and I entreat thee: Grant me time for repentance, O pure one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Let not the enemy seize my wretched soul like a savage lion, but by thy power break his soul-destroying fangs, O good one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Waking at dawn, * we cry unto Thee, O Lord: * Save us, for Thou art our God; * we know none other besides Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Look down and hearken to my voice, O Lady; and deliver me from everlasting condemnation, I pray.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`I have been wounded by the arrows of sin, and I cry to thee: Heal the wounds of my heart, O most pure one!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Have mercy on me, O only Compassionate One Who lovest mankind, through the supplications of her who gave birth to Thee; for Thou art my God and Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`I entreat thy goodness, be compassionate to me O thou who alone art all-hymned; and grant me mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`The abyss hath encompassed me, * the sea monster hath become my grave; * but I cried unto Thee, * the Lover of mankind, * and Thy right hand saved me, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Like a lion, the deceitful one seeketh after me to devour me, wickedly showing forth his gaping jaws, but from such do thou rescue me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Do Thou cleanse me O Lover of mankind, and by the pure prayers of her who gave birth to thee, deliver Thy world from every manner of suffering, and grant me everlasting glory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`A multitude of transgressions hath encompassed me, and I have fallen into the depths of despair. I pray thee O pure one, lead me up from the deepest depths of Hades, that I may glorify thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`My life hath been filled with transgressions and all manner of slothfulness; wherefore, before mine end, O pure one, turn me back to repentance and save me, O all-hymned one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`both_now`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The children were saved * in the burning furnace, * chanting: Blessed art Thou * O God of our fathers.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`By thy goodness, O Lady, grant me forgiveness of evils, voluntary or involuntary.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`My mind is weakened by the assaults of wicked thoughts of ungodliness. Help me, O good one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O Theotokos, with the remedy of thine entreaties heal now the wounds of the passions of my soul.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Grant me a contrite soul and humble mind, O good one, that I may glorify thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`The Son of God who before all ages * wast born of the Father * hath in these last times * become incarnate of the Virgin Mother, * O ye priests hymn, * and ye peoples supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Having lived my life in slothfulness, wretch that I am, and drawn nigh to the end of my life, I cry out to thee O Theotokos: Preserve my lowly soul from the snares of the adversary.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Grant unto me healing of bodily ailments, spiritual wounds, and deliverance from besetting passions by thy divine power, since thou alone art compassionate.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Engulfed by the tempest of life, and covered over by the waves of demonic temptations, do thou save me O pure maiden, leading me to a God- pleasing life of godly struggles.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`Like a herald entering a bridal chamber, Gabriel cried out, saying: Rejoice, O Virgin, thou most glorious palace of Christ, the King of all, wherein dwelling He hath deified all mortals!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Thee the true Mother of God, * who above all understanding * and beyond all description, * ineffably brought forth in time * the Eternal One, * with one mind do we the faithful magnify.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Thee, who hast ineffably given birth to God, have we acquired as an ally, an immovable rampart, the salvation of our souls, and a wellspring of miracles.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`On the day of judgment be Thou merciful to me, O Word of the true God, by the supplications of her who gave birth to Thee, and number me with those who are on Thy right hand.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Deliver me from everlasting fire, from the worm which sleepeth not and from all manner of torment, for I have placed my hope in thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`When my soul shall be separated from my wretched body, O Bride of God, deliver me from the tyranny of the invisible foe.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]}}},after_ode6:{rubric:`Lord, have mercy, (Thrice). Glory ..., Both now ..., Sessional Hymn, in Tone V:`,sessional:{text:`Rejoice, O firm rampart of divine victory! Rejoice, most militant felling of barbarians! Rejoice, O Theotokos, thou triumph of faithful Orthodox Christians, who truly set their hope on thee, delivering us from all misfortunes and ungodly enemies by thy supplications!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday-night Compline, sessional after Ode VI`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],spec_mel:`The co-beginningless Word`}},closing_rubric:`Then, “It is truly meet ...,” and a prostration. Trisagion through Our Father ..., Troparia, and the rest as usual. Dismissal.`},thu:{canon:{title:`Canon of supplication to the most holy Theotokos`,heading_rubric:`Canon of supplication to the most holy Theotokos`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Christ, who with an upraised arm * bringeth wars to naught, * hath shaken horse and rider in the Red Sea; * but Israel hath He saved * as they chanted a song of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`We know thee to be another, noetic garden of paradise, O Virgin Bride of God, beyond compare surpassing the Garden of Eden, O Mother of God; for thou hast budded forth incorruption for mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`In paradise Adam was hindered from touching the tree of life, having partaken of the fruit of knowledge; but the Fruit received from thee hath given him immortality.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Adam was the first man created from earth by the most pure hands of the Almighty; but thou, O Virgin Theotokos, hast given birth without seed to the new Adam, the Creator of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`The uttermost abyss of boundless transgressions hath engulfed me, and led me down into the depths of grievous despondency. O thou who hast given birth to the Abyss of loving-kindness, hasten thou and save me!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`By Thy command Thou didst establish the earth upon nothing * and suspended it unsupported; * do Thou establish Thy Church on the unshakeable rock of Thy commandments, O Christ, * Who alone art good * and the Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O immutable Word of God, Who didst make the earth the mother of living plants which did not exist on it in the beginning: Thou hast straightway come forth, seedlessly incarnate, from the woman who knew not a man, as from the earth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thou art the hope and help, the joy, protection and refuge of mortals, O Lady and Mother of life; wherefore, we pray: Send down thine aid upon all who hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Afflicted and stuck fast by grievous perils, O compassionate Accomplisher of all, Who art the God of all, we all set Thy thrice-holy tabernacle to pray before Thee, and we cry unto Thee: Loose Thou the bonds of Thy servants!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`The billows of sin cruelly batter me and drag me down into the abyss of transgressions; and the tempests of adverse thoughts batter my soul. O thou who hast given birth to the Helmsman, hasten thou to rescue thy servant.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Habbakuk, prophetically apprehending * Thy divine self-emptying, O Christ, * cried out to Thee with trembling: * Thou hast come for the salvation of Thy people; * to save Thine anointed ones.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`In submitting to the serpent, Eve begat grief for women; but having believed the tidings of God, O Virgin, thou didst cause Joy to blossom forth for the whole world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Eve was first formed from the rib of Adam of old; and now God is begotten of the Mother and Bride of God: He is born, incarnate without a father, from the Virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Eve rejoiceth, for the maiden who incorruptly conceived the Judge and gave birth to the Compassionate One, hath shown her first mother to be free from the ancient curse.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`My life hath been filled with transgressions, my mind is plagued with passions, and my soul is condemned; wherefore, in thy compassion, have mercy and save me, O Lady.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Thou Who hast clothed Thyself in light as with a garment, * I rise early unto Thee and cry out to Thee: * Enlighten my darkened soul, O Christ, * in that Thou alone art compassionate!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Having found thee to be a pillar and cloud of light, O Virgin Mother of the Bestower of light, we who walk in the wilderness of deception escape evils.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoice, O thou who hast given birth in the flesh to God Who before the ages was incorporeally begotten of the Father, and hath been well-pleased to appear to us openly.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The sun hath been surpassed by thy radiance, O Mary; for thou hast held in thine arms Him Who adorned the sky with luminaries, and didst feed Him at thy breast.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Condemn me not to the unquenchable fire, O Christ my Savior, by the supplications of the pure one who gave birth to Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Calm the raging sea of the passions, * O Master Christ, * with its soul-destroying tempest, * and lead me up from corruption * in that Thou art compassionate.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O pure Ever-virgin, without sustaining harm thou didst bear in thy womb the wondrous God Who of old saved the prophet Jonah in the sea monster.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Bearing the Lord God of hosts Who restraineth the storms of the sea, O most pure Virgin, thou didst still the briny billows of delusion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Having given birth to Christ, the Peace of all, O most pure one, by thy prayers to Him tame the raging storms of the passions which assail me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`On the day of grief, when the bonds holding soul and body together will be severed, intercede for me, and rescue me from the surrounding demons.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The supremely exalted Lord of our fathers * quenched the flame, * and bedewed the youths * as they chanted in harmony: * O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`God Who made a journey to meet with Abraham the forefather became thy Son, O blessed one; and He made his seed a blessing for the nations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thou art the ladder of Jacob, O undefiled one; for God depicted thee as the one Mother, for whose sake God gathered together his children.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The incarnate Son, Who is supremely exalted with the Father and the Spirit, having chosen thee, O pure one, loved thee exceedingly, that thou mightest become a dwelling-place for Him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Do thou ever entreat the God to Whom thou hast given birth, that He save me, wretch though I am, and accept me, the simple one who cries out with faith: Blessed art Thou, O God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Unto Thee the Fashioner of all, * the children in the furnace chanted a hymn: * All ye works of the Lord, * supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Thy birthgiving eludes examination, O Virgin, and is revealed to those who cry out with faith: All ye works of the Lord, hymn ye the Lord, and supremely exalt Him throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`In nowise having fallen from the glory of virginity, thou hast been enriched also with the honor of motherhood, O thou who knewest not wedlock. He Who worketh wonders hath made this clearly known, and we supremely exalt Him throughout the ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Behold the affliction of my lowly soul, O most pure one, and quickly deliver me from pain, that I may glorify thee throughout the ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Mercifully accept Thy Mother, who prayeth that Thou save Thy people, whom Thou hast acquired by Thy precious Blood, O good Word, that we may call Thee blessed throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`O Isaiah, rejoice and be glad! * The Virgin hath conceived in her womb, * and hath borne a Son, Emmanuel, * Who is both God and man; * and Orient is His name; * Him we magnify, and the Virgin we call blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Lady Theotokos, entreat the adored Trinity, to Whom alone thou hast given birth for us without suffering in the flesh, that He grant peace to those on earth, and that remission of sins be granted to those who hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Even though Emmanuel is understood to be a single Person, yet He hath two natures; for, lo! we proclaim two wills and activities in Him, and we confess thee, His Mother, to be the Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`I utter lamentation for myself, pondering the multitude of my sins, the uprisings of my passions, the despondency of my soul and the inconstancy of my mind. Grant salvation to me, wretch that I am,`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`Assailing me like brigands, and stripping me of my radiant and luminous vesture, mine enemies have inflicted many wounds upon me. O Lord, raise me up who am barely alive.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]}}},after_ode6:{rubric:`Lord, have mercy, (Thrice). Glory ..., Both now ..., Sessional Hymn, in Tone V:`,sessional:{text:`Beholding Thee willingly hanging upon the Cross between two thieves, O Christ, Thy Mother, her maternal womb rent with pain, exclaimed: “O my sinless Son, how have they unjustly crucified Thee on the Cross as a malefactor, Thee Who desireth to bring life to the race of mankind, in that Thou art supremely good?”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Thursday-night Compline, sessional after Ode VI`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]}},closing_rubric:`Then, “It is truly meet ...,” and a prostration. Trisagion through Our Father ..., Troparia, and the rest as usual. Dismissal.`},fri:{canon:{title:`Canon of supplication to the most holy Theotokos`,heading_rubric:`Canon of supplication to the most holy Theotokos`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Christ, who with an upraised arm * bringeth wars to naught, * hath shaken horse and rider in the Red Sea; * but Israel hath He saved * as they chanted a song of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`All the generations of mankind praise thee, O Virgin, as thou didst foretell in prophecy of old; wherefore, accept me who hymn thee, O Lady, and enlighten and make me wise.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thou hast broken the sting of death and the sin of the world, O Virgin Lady, having given birth to true Life. Quickly break also the sharp arrows of my passions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Having been revealed to be the only one arrayed in virgin’s vesture, thou didst rend asunder the fig-leaves which Adam wore; wherefore, clothe me in the garments of chastity by thy prayers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`Many daughters of Adam before thee acquired riches and divine glory, but thou hast surpassed them all beyond compare, O Lady; wherefore, enrich me now with heavenly and divine grace.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`By Thy command Thou didst establish the earth upon nothing * and suspended it unsupported; * do Thou establish Thy Church on the unshakeable rock of Thy commandments, O Christ, * Who alone art good * and the Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`The depths and heights of the unapproachable wisdom of God, Who was born from thy womb, have been recognized in thee, whereby deliver my heart from the depths of the serpent’s reasoning.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Christ, Who of old fashioned out of water the winged creatures and serpents, which before had not existed: Thou didst straightway fashion the strange vesture of Thy divine incarnation out of the blood of the pure Virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thou alone, O most pure one, art clearly the cleansing of our nature, for in thee the divine Fire made His abode without consuming thee, that He might purify it; wherefore, cleanse me of the defilement of the offenses of my passions, and illumine me by thy prayers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Knowing thee to be the cup of the Offshoot of the new vine, manifestly giving drink to the faithful for the remission offenses, O most pure one, I pray: Give drink to my heart with an outpouring of divine water.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Habbakuk, prophetically apprehending * Thy divine self-emptying, O Christ, * cried out to Thee with trembling: * Thou hast come for the salvation of Thy people; * to save Thine anointed ones.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Thou hast been revealed to be the unploughed furrow which produced the unsown divine Grain, whereby I, who hunger, am fed with divine gifts and grace.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Giving drink with the water of thy prayers to me who am truly sick unto death and am stuck fast in the fire of the passions of my soul, raise me up quickly.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`As thou art the animate city of God, gladdened by the flow of noetic rivers, make steadfast the house of my soul with the pillars of thy prayers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`Knowing thee to be the cloud raining down true righteousness, O most pure Lady, I pray that thou speedily deliver me thy servant from all who oppress me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Thou Who hast clothed Thyself in light as with a garment, * I rise early unto Thee and cry out to Thee: * Enlighten my darkened soul, O Christ, * in that Thou alone art compassionate!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Utterly suppress the turbulence and billows of sin and my passions, O Virgin Lady, having given birth to the Cause of dispassion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Shown from on high to be Christ’s cloth of the divine vesture of majesty, O pure one, with the raiment of the virtues clothe my naked soul.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Grant me cleansing offenses by thy supplications, O pure Virgin who hast given birth for us to Christ the Lord, our divine Purification.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`By thy prayers, O Virgin, do away with the sores, wounds and stripes of my sins, and grant power to thy servant.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Calm the raging sea of the passions, * O Master Christ, * with its soul-destroying tempest, * and lead me up from corruption * in that Thou art compassionate.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O thou who hast given birth to the Light Who created the luminaries of the sky, illumine now my soul and deliver me from the darkness of the passions, O all-radiant one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Entreat thy Son, Who of old sweetened the waters of Mara, O Theotokos, that He quickly deliver me from grievous suffering and bitterness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The torrents of the passions disturb my soul, O most pure one; yet dry them up by thy prayers, and destroy my wicked thoughts.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Delivering mankind, Christ hath issued forth out of Sion, from thy womb, O most immaculate Lady; and hath thereby delivered me from perils and tribulations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The supremely exalted Lord of our fathers * quenched the flame, * and bedewed the youths * as they chanted in harmony: * O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`The hordes of the demons fear and tremble before the invocation of thy name, O most pure one. Deliver me from them, save and preserve me, protecting me from all harm.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Inexpressible is thy glory, O Virgin; for thou hast given birth to the Lord of glory. Wherefore, grant unto me the glory of thy Son and my God, by thy prayers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Incline thine ear to the supplications of thy servant, O Lady, and speedily deliver me from tribulations and misfortunes, from all temptations, visible and invisible.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`With purity wash me who am wholly shameful and have sullied and defiled myself with the passions, and make me radiant through the sprinkling of thy prayers, O Virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Unto Thee the Fashioner of all, * the children in the furnace chanted a hymn: * All ye works of the Lord, * supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`The passion-plagued water of barrenness hath rendered the womb of my soul fruitless and dried it up. Rain down the divine Dew upon me, O light cloud, that I may bring forth fruits of repentance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`By thy prayers, O most pure one, calm, thou the water and storm of passionate thoughts, and guide me to the stream of dispassion, that I may glorify thee fervently throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O noetic portal, closed gate, which God alone hath passed through: Close and lock the gates of my passions, and open unto me the portals of hope.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Remove from me the burden of transgressions, O Virgin Mother, who alone ineffably hast given birth to the Lamb and Word of God, Who taketh away all the sin of the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`O Isaiah, rejoice and be glad! * The Virgin hath conceived in her womb, * and hath borne a Son, Emmanuel, * Who is both God and man; * and Orient is His name; * Him we magnify, and the Virgin we call blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Having as a man defiled my soul with many transgressions and sullied it with carnal passions, I now earnestly beseech thee and pray to thee: From all evil cleanse me, O pure one, by thy prayers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thou hast given birth to Him Who willeth mercy, the God of compassions and the Lover of mankind, Who alone is Good, Long-suffering and full of loving- kindness. By thy supplications, O pure one, show Him to be well-disposed toward me, and grant me release from offenses.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`By thy ceaseless maternal supplications, O Lady, to the virtues of good works do thou rouse thy servant, who am stuck fast in the slumber of despondency and asleep now in pleasures.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Blessing, I bless thee, O most pure one, and I magnify thee fervently. Wherefore, bless me who hymn thee; deliver me from all violence and grief, and by thy hands preserve me invincible.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]}}},after_ode6:{rubric:`Lord, have mercy, (Thrice). Glory ..., Both now ..., Sessional Hymn, in Tone V:`,sessional:{text:`Wherefore, growing despondent, hast thou forgotten thy God, Who hath mercy upon thee, O my passion-plagued soul? Despising His precepts, thou hast come in wickedness and prodigality to the end of thy life. But shun evil, crying out to the Theotokos: Have mercy on mine accursed soul!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Friday-night Compline, sessional after Ode VI`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]}},closing_rubric:`Then, “It is truly meet ...,” and a prostration. Trisagion through Our Father ..., Troparia, and the rest as usual. Dismissal.`},sat:{frame_rubric:`The priest saith: Blessed is our God..., and we respond: Amen. Glory to Thee, our God, glory to Thee. O heavenly King..., Trisagion through Our Father. Lord, have mercy (12 times). Glory ..., Both now ..., O come, let us worship ..., (Thrice). Psalm 50 (Have mercy on me, O God...); Psalm 69 (O God, be attentive unto helping me...); and Psalm 142 (O Lord, hear my prayer...). Then, Glory to God in the highest..., and the Symbol of Faith (I believe in one God...).`,canon:{title:`Canon of supplication to the most holy Theotokos, in Tone V`,heading_rubric:`Canon of supplication to the most holy Theotokos, in Tone V`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Christ, who with an upraised arm * bringeth wars to naught, * hath shaken horse and rider in the Red Sea; * but Israel hath He saved * as they chanted a song of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`We are all at a loss how to offer thee fitting hymnody, O Lady; for thy glory surpasseth all. Yet, O Bride of God, disdain not the entreaty offered to thee with fear and love.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`We all have recourse to the water of thine inexhaustible wellspring, O Virgin Theotokos, crying out: O most pure one, thou sole joy of our race, ask peace for thy Churches.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`God Who was well-pleased to receive flesh from thee hath appointed thee as a haven for all amid misfortunes, O pure one; wherefore, falling down before thee, we cry aloud: Grant thine aid unto thy servants!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`Let thy prayer, O most pure Virgin, be for thy servants the dispelling of the passions, the eradication of sins and the washing away of all manner of pain, O Birthgiver of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 1, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`By Thy command Thou didst establish the earth upon nothing * and suspended it unsupported; * do Thou establish Thy Church on the unshakeable rock of Thy commandments, O Christ, * Who alone art good * and the Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Thou art the hope of mortals, their help and joy, protection and refuge, O Lady, Mother of Life; wherefore, we pray thee: Send down thy help upon all who hymn thee, O most pure one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O compassionate Author, God and Savior of all, we who are infirm and are beset by grievous perils set Thy Mother before Thee as a most pure tabernacle, to supplicate Thee. Loose Thou the bonds of our transgressions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Bride of God, who alone hast given birth to the Creator, Fashioner and Lord of all while remaining a virgin, grant salvation from on high to thy servants who glorify thee as truly the Mother of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`Fill me with life-creating waters, O Lady who hast poured forth the divine Water upon the world; and with thy divine tranquility still thou the cruel torrents of mine iniquities and the tumult of my heart.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 3, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Habbakuk, prophetically apprehending * Thy divine self-emptying, O Christ, * cried out to Thee with trembling: * Thou hast come for the salvation of Thy people; * to save Thine anointed ones.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`In that thou art more exalted than all creation, O all-hymned Theotokos, God hath given thee to those on earth as a source of mediation before Him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Knowing thee to be the temple of God, O Virgin Mother, we who honor thee earnestly pray: Shut not the portals of thy mercy against thy servants, O Theotokos!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Knowing thee to be the true raiment of God all-adorned, O Mother who knewest not wedlock, we who honor thee all pray: Array us in the vesture of remission!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`The whole world was filled with joy at thy nativity, O most pure one; wherefore, the great Gabriel announced to thee: Rejoice, O Virgin Mother Mary!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 4, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Thou Who hast clothed Thyself in light as with a garment, * I rise early unto Thee and cry out to Thee: * Enlighten my darkened soul, O Christ, * in that Thou alone art compassionate!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Truly we are not chastened according to the measure of our offenses! O most pure Virgin Mother, turn away from us all the wrath of thy Son!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O pure one who hast given birth, without knowing wedlock, to God Who alone brought forth light out of darkness, earnestly beseech Him, that He send down divine light upon thy servants.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`With the incense of thy prayers, O pure Mother of the Creator, whom Solomon foretold as the divine Bride out of Lebanon, spread fragrance upon thy servants.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`Having given birth without seed to Christ, our Justification and Deliverance, O Theotokos, thou hast rendered the nature of our first parents free of the curse.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 5, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Calm the raging sea of the passions, * O Master Christ, * with its soul-destroying tempest, * and lead me up from corruption * in that Thou art compassionate.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Lady Theotokos who hast given birth to the Creator, ask remission for thy servants, and raise us up in might, that we may hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Be thou a help to us thy servants who entreat thee with faith, O pure Lady, in that thou art merciful, and raise us up in might, that we may hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`As thou hast the power to do what thou desirest, as is meet, O pure Lady, look upon thy servants with a merciful eye, and raise us up from corruption.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`Unceasingly pouring forth streams of compassion upon those who ask, O most immaculate and good one, rain down upon me also the light of thy Son’s commandments.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 6, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The supremely exalted Lord of our fathers * quenched the flame, * and bedewed the youths * as they chanted in harmony: * O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Christ, Thou unfathomable Wisdom of God, have pity upon Thy servants, for the sake of her who gave birth to Thee, for we unceasingly chant: Blessed art Thou, O God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Lord, we entreat Thy goodness: heal Thou our wounds, for the sake of her who gave birth to Thee, for we chant with fear: Blessed art Thou, O God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`With thy merciful eye, O Mother of God, look down and deliver thy servants from every evil circumstance, for we chant with faith: Blessed art Thou, O God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`Committing evil deeds, we have fallen away from thee, O Lady; yet have we straightway found thy help, O most pure one, when we have cried: Blessed art Thou, O God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 7, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`The Son of God who before all ages * wast born of the Father * hath in these last times * become incarnate of the Virgin Mother, * O ye priests hymn, * and ye peoples supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O our Lady, bestower of good things: grant the healing of the passions unto thy servants, O Virgin, that we may unceasingly hymn and supremely exalt thee throughout the ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O pure one who hast given birth indescribably to the Redeemer, thou didst ineffably give suck to Him while remaining a virgin. Him do thou entreat on behalf of those who hymn and glorify thee throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Forming ourselves into a most beautiful choir, we sing to thee, the radiant lamp of the Redeemer: O all ye works of the Lord, unceasingly hymn the Virgin Mary, and supremely exalt her throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`O pure ewe-lamb, Virgin maiden and Mother, cleanse me of the carnal passions, that I may be delivered from the snares of the deceiver, chanting hymns to thee, O divinely joyous one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 8, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`O Isaiah, rejoice and be glad! * The Virgin hath conceived in her womb, * and hath borne a Son, Emmanuel, * Who is both God and man; * and Orient is His name; * Him we magnify, and the Virgin we call blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Our hymnody is completed, O Christ Master, but our hope in Thee, our Creator, like Thy grace, knoweth no limitation. Wherefore, grant mighty power to Thy servants, both monastic and the laity, through the supplications of her who gave birth to Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`As thou art the true Mother of Life, O pure one, thou art the strength of the sick and infirm; wherefore, fleeing unto thee, O Lady, we have found the remission of all sorrows and have been saved by thy protection.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Beholding thy divine countenance in thine images, O Lady, we perceive thee clearly therein, in all ways hating the mindlessness of heretics on earth. And falling down before the icons, we receive healing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`O pure one, we sinners know thee to be an abyss of healings and a sea of grace; wherefore, we beseech thee: O most pure one, from all want rescue us who have recourse to thy protection.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline canon, Ode 9, item 4`},label:`both_now`}]}}},after_ode6:{rubric:`Lord, have mercy, (Thrice). Glory ..., Both now ..., Sessional Hymn, in Tone V:`,sessional:{text:`O all-holy Virgin, have mercy upon us who have recourse to thy tender compassion with faith, and who ask thy fervent aid; for thou art able to save us all, in that thou art the good Mother of God Most High, ever embracing Him with thy maternal supplications, O divinely joyous Virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-1.pdf`,locus:`Saturday-night Compline, sessional after Ode VI`}}},closing_rubric:`Then, “It is truly meet ...,” and the rest as usual. Dismissal.`}},matins_weekday:{mon:{sessionals:[{rubric:`After the 1st chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymns of repentance, in Tone V:`,spec_mel:null,items:[{text:`When the Judge taketh His seat and the angels stand before Him, when the trumpet sounds and the flame is kindled, what shalt thou do, O my soul, when thou art brought to judgment? For then thine evils will confront thee, and thy secret sins will be exposed. Wherefore, before the end cry out to the Judge: Cleanse me, O God, and save me!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, sessional set 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Let us all keep vigil and greet Christ with a multitude of oil and radiant lamps, that we may be deemed worthy to enter the bridal-chamber; for he who findeth himself outside the gates crieth unto God in vain: Have mercy on me!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, sessional set 1, item 2`},label:`plain`}],verses:[{text:`O Lord, rebuke me not in Thine anger, * nor chasten me in Thy wrath.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, sessional set 1 verse 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]}],closer:{text:`O Theotokos, in truth we confess thee * to be worthy of all praise; * truly higher than the heavens * and more holy than the cherubim. * Through thee we sinners gain salvation * and find protection in temptations! * cease not to intercede on our behalf, ** for thou art a strong support and refuge for our souls!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, sessional set 1 closer`},type:`theotokion`}},{rubric:`After the 2nd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymns, in Tone V:`,spec_mel:null,items:[{text:`O my soul, the things here on earth are transitory, but the things of the life to come are eternal. I envision the tribunal and the throne of the Judge, and I tremble at the thought of giving answer. Wherefore, turn thou with haste, for the judgment is inexorable.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, sessional set 2, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`I lie upon the bed of mine offenses, robbed of my hope of salvation; for the dreaming of my slothfulness winneth torment for my soul. O God Who wast born from the Virgin, raise me up to Thy hymnody, that I may glorify Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, sessional set 2, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Wondrous is God in His saints, * the God of Israel.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, sessional set 2, item 3`},label:`martyrs`},{text:`The memory of the passion-bearers shineth forth today, for it possesseth radiance from the heavens. The choirs of angels keep festival, and the race of mankind celebrates with them. Wherefore, they entreat the Lord, that our souls find mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, sessional set 2, item 4`},label:`plain`}],verses:[{text:`O Lord, rebuke me not in Thine anger, * nor chasten me in Thy wrath.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, sessional set 2 verse 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]}],closer:{text:`O Theotokos, thou who art of heaven with the angels * and of the earth with mankind, * we cry out to thee with a call of joy: * Rejoice, gate wider than the heavens! * Rejoice, thou who alone art the salvation of those born on earth! * Rejoice, O pure one, full of grace, * who hast given birth unto God incarnate.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, sessional set 2 closer`},type:`theotokion`}},{rubric:`After the 3rd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymns, in Tone V:`,spec_mel:`The co-beginningless Word`,items:[{text:`O Savior, summon me as Thou didst the prodigal, for I am weighed down with irrational passions and have wasted my life in prodigality; do Thou accept me, and extend to me thy fatherly embrace in the loving-kindness of Thy compassions; and by the prayers of the incorporeal ones grant unto me mine ancient dignity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, sessional set 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}],verses:[],closer:{text:`O fervent and invincible intercessor, * diligent and unashamed hope, * rampart, protection and haven * of those who have recourse to thee, * O pure Ever-virgin do thou, together with the angels, * entreat thy Son and God, ** that He grant peace, salvation and great mercy to the world.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, sessional set 3 closer`},type:`theotokion`}}],canons:[{title:`Canon of repentance, the acrostic whereof is “Have pity on me who have sinned greatly against Thee, O Word,” the composition of Joseph, in Tone V`,heading_rubric:`Canon of repentance, the acrostic whereof is “Have pity on me who have sinned greatly against Thee, O Word,” the composition of Joseph, in Tone V:`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Let us chant a hymn of victory * unto the Lord, Who wrought wondrous miracles * in the Red Sea, * for He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Christ, in that Thou art almighty, turn unto me and have compassion on me, for I have been led astray and deceived by the many falsehoods of the alien one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O Christ Who opened the ears of the deaf man, open Thou the deaf ears of my soul, I pray, that I may hear Thy words.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`As newly-revealed stars of Christ, the Sun of righteousness, O martyrs, dispel the darkness of our hearts.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Shown to be burning arrows set afire by the divine coals of the Holy Spirit, the spiritual athletes have broken all the arrows of the serpent.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 4`},label:`martyrs`},{text:`O portal of divine glory, open unto me the doors of repentance, and rescue my lowly soul from the gates of Hades, I pray.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`God is King over the nations. * God is seated on His holy throne. * And with understanding we chant unto Him * as King and God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O good Lord, Who dost not will that even one person perish: With Thy merciful hand have pity and save me who am perishing by Thy command, O all- Compassionate One.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`O Christ our Lord, Who knowest all the sins I have committed against Thee in knowledge and in ignorance, I approach and fall down before Thee: Accept me as Thou didst the prodigal.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`That ye might slay living sin and show forth the enemy as dead, O blessed martyrs, ye paid no heed to the death of your bodies.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Adorned with sufferings and clad in raiment dyed with your blood, O martyrs, ye stand, crowned, before the King of all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`O Virgin Mother who gave flesh unto God, accept the voices of those who ever cry out to thee, and deliver us from divers evil circumstances.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`The works of Thy dispensation, O Lord, * filled the prophet Habakkuk with wonder, * for Thou hast come to bring salvation to Thy people, * and to save all Thine anointed ones.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`The works I have done in this life are wicked and grievous. O Christ my God: deliver me from them, granting me sincere repentance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Every honorable commandment have I spurned; I have rejected the fear of Thee, O Christ, and I fear Thine inexorable tribunal. Condemn me not thereat, O Thou Who art full of loving-kindness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`All their limbs truly stretched out and secured with leather thongs, badly wounded with stripes and raked with iron claws, Thy spiritual athletes rejoiced with faith, O Word.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Using every means, the evil one was yet unable to move you from your divine stance, O spiritual athletes; wherefore, O valiant ones, ye have been revealed to be the divine confirmation of many who are shaken.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`The Lord became incarnate from thy pure blood, O all-hymned one, and by thy goodly mediations He grants repentance unto those who honor thee, in that He is compassionate, and alone the Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Christ God, Thou true Light, * out of the night my spirit riseth at dawn unto Thee. * Show forth Thy countenance upon me.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5 irmos`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]},items:[{text:`Awake, O my soul, awake from the heavy sleep of grievous sin, and enlighten thyself with the light of repentance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Let us diligently restore our souls and drink in showers of compunction, that we may produce the grain of repentance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Sharpened with the coals of love, O passion-bearers, ye were shown to be divinely forged swords, felling the hordes of the enemy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Not being enslaved by the enemy, ye instead enslaved him, O passion- bearers, and showed yourselves to be close friends of Christ.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`O Virgin who art blessed among women, grant thy mercies to thy people, for thou hast been revealed to be the Mother of the Merciful One.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Thou didst deliver the prophet from the whale: * Do Thou O Lord lead me up from the depths of sin * and save me.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`There is no sin in this life which I alone have not committed, wretch that I am. O only Sinless One, have pity on me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Propelled by the sail of zeal, let us all hasten to the harbor of salvation by repentance, that we may be saved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Creation is enlightened by the suffering of the preachers, apostles and martyrs. Enlighten us also by them, O Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Let us all honor the martyrs, the vessels containing divine radiance, the honored emanations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 4`},label:`martyrs`},{text:`O Virgin, intercessor for the faithful, entreat the Lord, that thy servants may be delivered from every sin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Blessed art Thou, O God, * who beholdest the depths * and sittest upon the throne of glory: * for Thou art supremely praised and glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Blessed art Thou, O God, and all-hymned and most glorious art Thou Who in thy tender compassion dost accept all who repent.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Heal Thou my many passions, O supremely hymned and most glorious tenderly compassionate Christ, for Thou knowest my weakness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The choir of passion-bearers was strengthened with divine power and vanquished the enemy, crying aloud: Thou art all- hymned and most glorious forever!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 3`},label:`martyrs`},{text:`O Word Who gavest the most wise passion-bearers the strength to endure most subtle tortures, by their prayers have pity on us all,`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Blessed art Thou, O God Who, making Thine abode within the Virgin’s womb, saved mankind; wherefore thou art all-hymned and most glorious throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`The Fashioner of all creation, * whom the angels fear: * let us praise, O ye people, * and supremely exalt throughout all ages!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Lord, enliven me who have become deadened by my trespasses, that I may glorify Thee throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Enlightening me with repentance, O Lord, deliver me from the darkness of sin, that I may glorify Thee throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O passion-bearing martyrs, ye trampled the flame of delusion underfoot, most gloriously receiving dew from heaven.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Like fertile soil, O holy ones, ye truly produced grain a hundredfold for Christ, the Judge of the contest.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`From thee did God shine forth, O all-hymned Virgin, with divine knowledge enlightening those who have been darkened.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`We, the race of mankind, * magnify thee, * who art blessed among women * and blessed by God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Lord, be merciful unto me for I have mindlessly committed innumerable sins, and grant me Thy kingdom, O Word.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`As of old Thou didst save the Ninevites who repented, O only Savior, by Thy mercy save us who hymn Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Giving your flesh over to all manner of wounds, ye preserved your souls unwounded, O passion-bearers of the Lord, and sharers in divine glory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Radiant daystars enlightening the souls of all on earth, ye showed yourselves to be passion-bearers of the Lord of all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 4`},label:`martyrs`},{text:`Like a fiery throne thou bearest Him Who holdeth all things in His hand, O Virgin, and at thy breast nourished Him Who feedeth all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]}},acrostic:`Have pity on me who have sinned greatly against Thee, O Word`,composer:`Joseph`},{title:`Another canon, of the incorporeal beings, the acrostic whereof is “The fifth hymn to the angels,” the composition of Theophanes, in Tone V`,heading_rubric:`Another canon, of the incorporeal beings, the acrostic whereof is “The fifth hymn to the angels,” the composition of Theophanes, in Tone V:`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Christ, who with an upraised arm * bringeth wars to naught, * hath shaken horse and rider in the Red Sea; * but Israel hath He saved * as they chanted a song of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O ye angels, initiates of the life-giving Godhead, shining with the light of His first- revealed rays, entreat the Master, that He illumine my soul with light.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`As ye all have boldness, standing before the throne on high, O supreme commanders, captains of the ranks of heaven, from misfortunes deliver those who piously hymn you.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The curse hath been annulled and grief hath ended; for the blessed and gracious one hath shone forth Christ, the Joy of the faithful, budding forth blessing like a flower for all the ends of the earth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 3`},label:`theotokion`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`By Thy command Thou didst establish the earth upon nothing * and suspended it unsupported; * do Thou establish Thy Church on the unshakeable rock of Thy commandments, O Christ, * Who alone art good * and the Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Thou Who by Thy word most wisely formed the choirs of the hosts on high, and Who showest forth Thine incalculable goodness: Through their intercessions make steadfast Thy Church, O only good One, and Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`Adorning the angels with ineffable radiance, and by them making Thy Church steadfast, O loving Christ, thereby enlighten my wretched soul, I pray Thee, O Master, remembering not my countless sins.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Without uniting with a man thou didst become the Mother of God Who illumines the incorporeal choirs, that they might unceasingly hymn the one Godhead in three hallowed Lordships, O most pure and all-hymned Virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Habbakuk, prophetically apprehending * Thy divine self-emptying, O Christ, * cried out to Thee with trembling: * Thou hast come for the salvation of Thy people; * to save Thine anointed ones.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Thou didst form the angelic luminaries and hast right generously enlightened them with deifying rays, for Thou art mighty in power, O Lover of mankind, and keepest Thy word.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`Let us set aside the worldly wisdom of our bodies, O ye faithful, emulating the life of the incorporeal ranks; and let us give wings to our mind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Be thou an intercessor, refuge and haven for me, averting the storm of the passions, O most immaculate one, for thou hast incomparably surpassed the angelic choirs in goodness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Thou Who hast clothed Thyself in light as with a garment, * I rise early unto Thee and cry out to Thee: * Enlighten my darkened soul, O Christ, * in that Thou alone art compassionate!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Traveling all the ends of the earth, ye bring the benefactions of the Master unto the faithful, and preserve them, O all-glorious archangels.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`Submitting to Thy word, O Word of God the Father, the glorious orders of the heavenly ranks are illumined with the light of Thine effulgence.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`All my desire do I set before thee, O thou who, in a manner past all telling, hast given birth to the Sweetness of desire for those who acknowledge thee to be the Theotokos, O pure one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`theotokion`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Calm the raging sea of the passions, * O Master Christ, * with its soul-destroying tempest, * and lead me up from corruption * in that Thou art compassionate.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O chosen assemblies of the angels, adorned with sanctity, ye shine with light- giving effulgence, manifestly perfected by deifying brilliance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`Richly all-adorned with thrice-radiant beams, O ye angels and archangels, in a godly manner illumine my wretched soul with your prayers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O most pure one, thou didst conceive the Creator and God of all, upon whom the angels, rejoicing, gaze with fear, standing reverently before Him.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The supremely exalted Lord of our fathers * quenched the flame, * and bedewed the youths * as they chanted in harmony: * O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Showing forth immeasurably powerful might, Christ appointed you, O supreme commanders, and taught you to chant: O God, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`O Thou Who with goodness adorned the countless multitudes of the incorporeal ranks, grant that the companies of mortals may hymn Thee, crying aloud: O God, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Make me now steadfast who am shaken by the passions, O Virgin for thou hast poured forth dispassion upon all the faithful, who chant with faith: O God, Blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`theotokion`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Unto Thee the Fashioner of all, * the children in the furnace chanted a hymn: * All ye works of the Lord, * supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`The councils of the angels now move me to chant with hymns and heartfelt desire; and with them I sing: Hymn the Lord, all ye works, and supremely exalt Him throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`O servants of the most holy and three-Sunned Radiance, pray ye that they may be saved who chant with faith: Hymn the Lord, ye works, and supremely exalt Him throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O Virgin Mother and maiden, portal of the Light: With thy light illumine those who chant with faith: Hymn the Lord, O ye works, and supremely exalt Him throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`theotokion`},{text:`refrain: “More honorable than the cherubim ...,” and make prostrations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 4`},label:`plain`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`O Isaiah, rejoice and be glad! * The Virgin hath conceived in her womb, * and hath borne a Son, Emmanuel, * Who is both God and man; * and Orient is His name; * Him we magnify, and the Virgin we call blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`As commander of the angelic ranks, O most radiant Michael, and thou, O Gabriel, as the true herald of the divine incarnation: Preserve all who hymn you, O glorious ones.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:3}],label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`O Thou who pourest out Thy treasures in rich gifts and Who appointed the angelic ranks: When Thou comest with them as Judge and King of all, save me who flee to Thy mercy, O Master.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`With faith the archangels, authorities and thrones, the cherubim, powers and seraphim, the radiant angels, principalities and dominions, noetically minister unto thy Son with trembling, O pure and all-blessed Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]}},acrostic:`The fifth hymn to the angels`,composer:`Theophanes`}],magnificat_rubric:`We then chant the hymn of the Theotokos (the Magnificat), with the`,post_canon_rubric:`Then, “It is truly meet to bless thee ...,” and a prostration. Small litany, Exapostilarion, and the usual psalms. Small Doxology (Read), Litany: Let us complete ..., On the Aposticha, these Stichera of repentance, in Tone V:`,aposticha:{rubric:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera of repentance, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`Turn away from the multitude of my transgressions O Lord, Who wast born of the Virgin, and cleanse me of all my sins. I beseech Thee to grant me the thought of turning back unto Thee, for Thou alone lovest mankind, and have mercy on me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, aposticha item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Woe is me, to whom am I like? I am like the barren fig tree, and I fear that I shall be cursed and cut down. But, do Thou O heavenly Husbandman, make my barren soul fruitful, O Christ God, and receive me as the Prodigal Son, and have mercy on me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, aposticha item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Blessed is the army of the King of heaven, for though the passion-bearers were mortals, yet they strove to attain the dignity of the angels; and spurning the pangs of their bodies, by their sufferings they were deemed worthy of the honor of the incorporeal ones. Wherefore, by their prayers, O Lord, send down upon us great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, aposticha item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}],verses:{ref:`shared.weekday_aposticha_verses.sets.standard_matins`}},aposticha_theotokion:{text:`O thou who art full of grace, * intercede by thy supplications, * and beg that a multitude of compassions be granted to our souls * and the cleansing of our many sins, ** we entreat thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Matins, aposticha Glory/Both-now closer`},type:`theotokion`},closing_rubric:`Then, “It is good to give thanks ...,” Trisagion ..., Our Father ..., Troparia.`},tue:{sessionals:[{rubric:`st After the 1 chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymns of repentance, in Tone V:`,spec_mel:null,items:[{text:`When the Judge shall take His seat and the angels stand before Him, when the trumpet shall sound and the flame kindled, what shalt thou do, O my soul, when thou art brought to judgment? For thine evils will then confront thee, and thy secret sins will be laid bare. Wherefore, before the end cry out to the Judge: Cleanse me, O God, and save me!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, sessional set 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Let us all keep vigil and greet Christ with a plentitude of oil and radiant lamps, that we may be deemed worthy to enter the bridal-chamber; for he who findeth himself outside the gates shall cry unto God in vain: Have mercy on me!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, sessional set 1, item 2`},label:`plain`}],verses:[{text:`O Lord, rebuke me not in Thine anger, * nor chasten me in Thy wrath.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, sessional set 1 verse 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]}],closer:{text:`The strange mystery of the Virgin * hath been revealed to the world as salvific: * for from her wast seedlessly born, * and revealed in the flesh without corruption. * The Joy of all, ** O Lord glory be to Thee!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, sessional set 1 closer`},type:`theotokion`}},{rubric:`After the 2nd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymns, in Tone V:`,spec_mel:null,items:[{text:`When thy deeds are laid bare, O my soul, and myriads of angels stand before the Judge, what answer shalt thou find for thy shame, if thou wilt not cry out, weeping, before the end: “I have sinned, O good Lord! Have mercy on me!”?`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, sessional set 2, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`I lie upon the bed of mine offenses, robbed of my hope of salvation; for the dreaming of my slothfulness winneth torment for my soul. O God Who wast born from the Virgin, raise me up to Thy hymnody, that I may glorify Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, sessional set 2, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thou hast given us an indestructible bulwark, O Christ God: the miracles of Thy holy martyrs. By their prayers make steadfast Thy faithful people, in that Thou art good and the Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, sessional set 2, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`}],verses:[{text:`O Lord, rebuke me not in Thine anger, * nor chasten me in Thy wrath.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, sessional set 2 verse 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]},{text:`Wondrous is God in His saints, * the God of Israel.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, sessional set 2 verse 2`}}],closer:{text:`Show forth thy ready protection, help and mercy * upon thy servants, O pure one; * dampen the waves of vain thoughts, * and raise up my fallen soul, O Theotokos, * for I know, O Virgin, I know, ** that thou canst do whatsoever thou dost will.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, sessional set 2 closer`},type:`theotokion`}},{rubric:`After the 3rd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymns, in Tone V:`,spec_mel:null,items:[{text:`The threefold waves of despair assail me who have fallen headlong into the depths of sin; but in that Thou art almighty, O Christ, Pilot of all, go Thou before me and in Thy tender compassion steer me to the calm harbor of dispassion, and save me by the prayers of the Forerunner, O Savior.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, sessional set 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Elizabeth was freed from barrenness, and the Virgin remained a virgin when she conceived in her womb at the sound of Gabriel’s voice. And the Forerunner John leapt up beforehand in his mother’s womb, perceiving in the womb of the Virgin the God and Master, Who became incarnate for our salvation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, sessional set 3, item 2`},label:`plain`}],verses:[],closer:{text:`O root that hath budded forth the divine flower, tabernacle and candlestick, golden vessel of manna, holy table bearing the bread of life: with John the Forerunner, intercede before Him, since He is thy son and God, that He may grant mercy and salvation to all who acknowledge thee to be the very Theotokos!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, sessional set 3 closer`},type:`theotokion`}}],canons:[{title:`Canon of repentance, the acrostic whereof is “O Christ, grant us cleansing of`,heading_rubric:`Canon of repentance, the acrostic whereof is “O Christ, grant us cleansing of`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`A land which the sun had never beheld, * and upon which it had never shined, * an abyss which the vault of heaven had not seen laid bare, * hath Israel traversed dry-shod, O Lord. * And Thou didst lead them to Thy mountain of sanctification, * as they sang and chanted * a hymn of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Grant me cleansing of the things I have done, O Savior, and absolve me before I depart from hence. Wash away my great filth, O Lord Who cleansed the lepers, and grant that I may stand blamelessly before Thee Who wilt come to judge the living and the dead.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`The discharge which lieth upon the eyes of my soul prevents me from gazing upon Thy beams, which Thou didst emit when Thou didst appear on earth, O unapproachable Sun. Wash it away, O Savior, and grant that I may contemplate the light of Thy grace, O compassionate Lord.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:3}],label:`plain`},{text:`Full of vigilance, O blessed spiritual athletes, keepers of the commandments of Christ, ye lulled to sleep all the evil of the enemy; wherefore, in your divine vigilance raise me up to repentance, I pray, for I am weighed down by the sleep of sin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Contending in your flesh against the adverse foe, O martyrs, ye vanquished him with the sword of the Cross and drowned him in the outpouring of your blood; and, singing and chanting a hymn of victory, ye have received from God crowns of victory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Deliver me from evil habits, O pure Virgin. Upon the rock of the commandments establish me who am shaken by the machinations of him who of old caused our first parents to fall. And grant that I may please Christ, singing well and chanting a hymn of victory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`Do Thou establish my heart, O Lord, * which is shaken by the billows of life, * and guide it to a calm haven, O God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`I promised Thee that I would repent, O God, yet still I commit sin. What will become of me? How shall I find myself when Thou shalt come to judge the earth?`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Let us offer supplication unto the Lord; let us sigh and shed the tears which wash away defilement, that we may find deliverance in the world to come.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Their minds wholly dead, the violators of the law wounded the victorious martyrs who love Life and confess Christ.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 3`},label:`martyrs`},{text:`The choirs of the martyrs have been numbered with the choirs of the noetic angels; becoming peers of the angels through the grace of the divine Spirit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 4`},label:`martyrs`},{text:`Open now to me the gates of repentance, the portal of the Light, O Virgin; and forbid the passions entry into my humbled soul.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`I have heard Thy report, O Lord, * and I was afraid. * I came to knowledge of Thy dispensation, * and I glorified Thee, O only Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Paying no heed to Thine enlightening words, O Lord, I have committed deeds of darkness, and I fear Thy dread tribunal in the life to come.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`If we give wings to the ship of our soul with the sail of the fear of God, we shall reach the havens of repentance, escaping the threefold waves of evils.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O martyrs, ye have been revealed to be divine mountains which let fall sweetness, and the divinely-planted garden having within it the Lord, the Tree of life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`With arrows of patience and perseverance ye shot down the demonic foe, and have received crowns of glory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 4`},label:`martyrs`},{text:`O most pure Lady, intercessor for sinners, divine correction of those who have fallen, thou art glorified as she who gave birth to God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Hasten Thou and have compassion on my wretched soul, * which doth battle at night * with the darkness of the passions. * Shine in me with the brightness of the day, * O noetic Sun, * and thereby make the night give way to light.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`There is no salvation for me in my works, for I have committed many sins on earth, wretch that I am, and I shall tremble before Thy dread judgment-seat when thou shalt judge those who have broken Thy commandments, O God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`How mindless have I been! How dark I have become by doing evil deeds! How I have failed to understand the fear of Thee, O Christ! I have fallen face down upon the ground and made myself like the irrational beasts; yet grant me conversion, O God of all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`The cloud of martyrs hath dispelled the clouds of bitter torments, shining forth the daylight of true understanding, destroying the gloom of polytheism, and reaching the unapproachable Light.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 3`},label:`martyrs`},{text:`Sanctify my mind by the supplications of Thy holy martyrs, I pray, O Christ, and show me to be full of enlightenment, and a partaker of everlasting glory, that, rendering glory, I may hymn Thee, O Savior.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`At the ineffable word thou hast given birth for us, O Virgin Mother, unto God Who through thy blessed mediations hath granted repentance unto all who have greatly sinned, O refuge and haven of the faithful.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`theotokion`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Even as Thou didst deliver the prophet from the beast, O Lord, * so do Thou lead me up from the depths * of unrestrained passions, I pray Thee, * that I may dare * to look upon Thy holy temple.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Now is the time to change our ways, yet I always lie prostrate, ever stuck in great senselessness. But releasing me from the darkness of my heart, O Word, have pity on me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Have pity on me who groan, as once Thou hadst pity on the publican, O compassionate Christ; and grant that I may weep fervent tears like the harlot, that I also may wash away the filth of my many transgressions`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O great martyrs of Christ, from the great flame in Gehenna, which awaiteth me there, rescue me who have sinned greatly, that I may ever greatly glorify your memory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Having struggled well, Thy passion-bearers were radiantly crowned by Thy life-creating right hand, O Lord and God. By their honored intercessions save all Thy people.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`O divinely joyous tabernacle of holiness, precious ark, lampstand of the divine Light, table of the Bread of life, animate palace of the Word: Show me to be a temple of the Spirit.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The prayer of the Children quenched the fire * and the furnace which bedewed them proclaimed the miracle, * for it neither burned nor consumed those, * who chanted hymns unto the God of our Fathers.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Forgive Thou mine iniquities, mine injustices and my countless offenses, O Christ, and in the greatness of Thy compassions, O God, deliver me from the torment which is to come.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Like the prodigal I have now squandered all the wealth I once received, and I am beset by starvation, deprived of divine food. Accept me, the penitent, O Savior, and save me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Your members mortified by many tortures, ye rendered dead the warring foe, O right wondrous martyrs of the Lord; wherefore, we the faithful piously hymn you.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`O martyrs, with patience and valor ye impaled hordes of the demons and all the multitude of tormentors, and have now been transported to true Life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Thou hast been revealed to be a haven of salvation for all, O pure one, stilling the tempest of the passions and leading to tranquility all who are humble on the earth, O pure Birthgiver of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`theotokion`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`O ye company of angels, * and assembly of mankind; * ye priests, Levites, and peoples: * praise, bless, and supremely exalt the King and Creator of all, * throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Behold, the sores of my soul have putrefied and grown fetid, O Christ, and I have suffered and been humbled thereby; but treat me, O Savior, with the medicines of repentance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`By deception the most wicked serpent defrauded me and filled me with evils; but, sighing, I cry: O Word, reject me not, who am condemned and brought low!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Ye turned not away from a higher standing, O all-famed ones, and ye cast down the enemies of the Cross who sought to undermine you, utterly vanquishing them, O most wise ones.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`O all-praised martyrs of the Lord, neither fire, nor the sword, nor wild beasts, nor starvation, nor the crushing wheel, nor any other torture was able to separate you from Christ the Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`O Mother of God, boast of angels and salvation of all, be thou a surety for me, that I may find and receive remission of the sins I have committed in the past, in knowledge and in ignorance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`For the mighty One hath done great things to thee, * in that He showed thee forth as a pure Virgin * even after giving birth, * since thou art she that hath seedlessly borne her own creator, * wherefore, O Theotokos, * we magnify thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`That I may magnify Thy long-suffering, I cry to Thee: O Jesus, be Thou yet patient with me, and hew me not down like the barren fig tree, but let me produce for Thee the fruits of repentance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`How awesome art Thou, O Thou Who alone art mighty and powerful! Who will withstand the dread threat of Thee when Thou Thyself shalt come to sit in judgment? When that shall take Thy place, preserve me uncondemned.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`By your divine pangs ye take away the pains of my body, O spiritual athletes of the Lord; wherefore, heal the most grievous passions of my soul, in that ye are most skilled physicians.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`The shrines of your relics shine forth more brightly than the rays of the sun with rays of divine grace, enlightening hearts and illumining the souls of those who praise you with faith, O passion-bearers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`O thou who art full of the grace of God, thou hast truly been revealed to be the radiant cloud which leadeth the new people to the promised land, and the gate which leadeth to life; wherefore, we magnify thee, O Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`theotokion`}]}}},{title:`Another canon, of the holy forerunner, the acrostic whereof is “O Baptist, accept`,heading_rubric:`Another canon, of the holy forerunner, the acrostic whereof is “O Baptist, accept`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Christ, who with an upraised arm * bringeth wars to naught, * hath shaken horse and rider in the Red Sea; * but Israel hath He saved * as they chanted a song of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`A pure and immaterial way of life didst thou show forth in a material body, O Forerunner; wherefore, we beseech thee: Make those who bless thee with faith emulators of thyself.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O Forerunner who immersed Christ, the Abyss of compassion, in the river’s streams, entreat Him to dry up the abyss of mine evils and to enlighten my mind, I pray.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Forerunner of the Savior, mediating causes of repentance for me, I pray thee: Ask and entreat Him Who is the Lover of mankind, that I be granted the compunction which washeth away the fetid mire of sin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Without pain thou hast ineffably given birth unto Him Whom the Father incorruptibly begat before all ages, O all-hymned Lady. Him do thou beseech, that He save from all harm those who have recourse unto thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`By Thy command Thou didst establish the earth upon nothing * and suspended it unsupported; * do Thou establish Thy Church on the unshakeable rock of Thy commandments, O Christ, * Who alone art good * and the Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Ever pouring forth healings upon those who approach thy temple with faith, O wondrous Forerunner, I pray thee: Cure the passions of my heart, which most wretchedly grows within me through negligence, O thou who art most noetically rich.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`I sigh and am ever wracked by lamentations when I think of Thine inexorable judgment, O only most-righteous Judge. By the supplications of Thy Forerunner, preserve me uncondemned there, O Lord my God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`As the mediator between the Old and the New Covenants through thy divine mediations, O glorious Forerunner, I cry to thee: By repentance renew me who am grown old through many sins, that I may honor thee in praise.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O holy Virgin Mother who alone art all-immaculate: Lift from us the blame of transgressions, enlighten our minds, purify our hearts, and deliver us all from everlasting condemnation, we pray.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Habbakuk, prophetically apprehending * Thy divine self-emptying, O Christ, * cried out to Thee with trembling: * Thou hast come for the salvation of Thy people; * to save Thine anointed ones.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`As a true warrior of Christ the King, thou hast made thine abode in the kingdom on high, O Baptist. Unceasingly entreat Him, that He have pity on those who honor thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Foreseeing the gratefulness of thy heart, the Lord sanctified thee from thy mother’s womb, O blessed one. Him do thou entreat, that He sanctify us all, we pray.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst announce the coming of Him Who died for our sake unto all the dead. Him do thou beseech, O Forerunner, that He give life to me who have died, and save me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Have mercy on me, O only most immaculate one, for thou hast ineffably given birth unto God Who is merciful in His surpassing goodness; and deliver me from everlasting torments.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Thou Who hast clothed Thyself in light as with a garment, * I rise early unto Thee and cry out to Thee: * Enlighten my darkened soul, O Christ, * in that Thou alone art compassionate!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`The womb of the barren one gave birth unto thee, O Forerunner, through thy right fruitful words showing forth as right fertile our hearts which are void of good works; wherefore, we call thee blessed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`In the desert places thou didst blossom like a right fragrant lily, O ever-blessed one; wherefore, we cry out to thee: Drive all the fetor of evil from my soul, O Forerunner.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst stand between the law and grace, O all-wise one; wherefore, I cry aloud: Have pity on me who am afflicted with wretchedness and am vanquished by the law of sin, O Forerunner.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`O most pure one, impassable portal of glory, open unto me the gates of repentance, winning for me divine entry and rest in the life to come.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Calm the raging sea of the passions, * O Master Christ, * with its soul-destroying tempest, * and lead me up from corruption * in that Thou art compassionate.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Resplendent with ineffable beams, O Forerunner of Christ, by thine effective supplications illumine the hearts of those who piously praise thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O Forerunner of Christ, with grace illumining me, who am held fast in the sleep of slothfulness, assiduously rouse me to do those things which God willeth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`From every tribulation caused by the adversary deliver us who have acquired thee as a divine intercessor and advocate before the Master, O blessed one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The tempest of sin assails me, O most pure Theotokos. Make haste to deliver me, guiding me to the haven of repentance, O all-immaculate one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`theotokion`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The supremely exalted Lord of our fathers * quenched the flame, * and bedewed the youths * as they chanted in harmony: * O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`With words we entreat thee who art the Forerunner of the Word: As thou didst loose the voice of thy father at thy birth, so loose thou the snares of our transgressions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O all-radiant sun who shinest the radiance of salvation upon me, deliver me from the darkness of the passions which vex my darkened heart.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`I have acquired an unfruitful soul and a barren heart, O divine offspring of the barren woman. O Baptist of Christ, pray thou without ceasing, that I may produce the fruits of repentance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Triadicon: Let us glorify the Son Who is equal to the Father, and the Holy Spirit, the indivisible Trinity, chanting in a godly manner: O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O all-immaculate one, thou hast given birth to Christ as a little Child, Who worketh the renewal of us who have grown old through the ancient transgression.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Unto Thee the Fashioner of all, * the children in the furnace chanted a hymn: * All ye works of the Lord, * supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Thou didst wash the assembly of the people in the streams of the Jordan, preaching repentance, O great Forerunner; wherefore, I cry out to thee: Dry up the stream of my passions, sending forth wellsprings of tears upon me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Be thou wholly atremble, O my soul, pondering the judgment-seat of the Almighty; and cry aloud: O Compassionate One, for the sake of Thy Forerunner have pity and save me, and deliver me from torments.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`I move mine unclean lips and defiled tongue in prayer to thee, O holy Forerunner: Hasten thou quickly, and help me, who am unceasingly shaken by all the assaults of the deceiver.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Triadicon: O consubstantial Trinity - Father, Son and Spirit - rain down upon us remission offenses, that, having received perfect salvation, we may supremely exalt Thee throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O divinely joyous one, by thine exalted birthgiving thou hast raised us up from the pit into which we have fallen; wherefore, with grateful voices, O maiden, we hymn thee with faith throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`theotokion`},{text:`refrain: “More honorable than the cherubim ...,” and make prostrations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 6`},label:`plain`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`O Isaiah, rejoice and be glad! * The Virgin hath conceived in her womb, * and hath borne a Son, Emmanuel, * Who is both God and man; * and Orient is His name; * Him we magnify, and the Virgin we call blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Lo! the majesty of thy temple is acknowledged to be heaven on earth, O Forerunner of Christ, and with divine rays thou enlightenest those who approach it and who now bless thee therein every day.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`As the true friend of the Master, O all-blessed Baptist, strengthen me to love Him without wavering, and with an upright character, and to spurn the corrupting passions which lead me into the pit of perdition.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast not a reed shaken by contrary winds, O most wise one, but rather our divine confirmation and the unshakable fortification of the Church, which do thou preserve unshaken by thy supplications, causing every temptation to cease.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The coming of the Creator is at hand! Why, therefore, dost thou not weep over thyself, O my wretched soul - living in indifference. But arise, and cry out to the Lord: Have pity on me, O Savior, through the supplications of the Fore- runner, in that Thou lovest mankind!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thou hast been shown to be the radiant chariot of the Sun Who shone forth from thy womb and broke the cruel darkness of delusion, O all- immaculate and pure one. Wherefore, with faith we bless thee as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]}}}],magnificat_rubric:`We then chant the hymn of the Theotokos (the Magnificat), with the`,post_canon_rubric:`Then, “It is truly meet to bless thee ...,” and a prostration. Small litany, Exapostilarion, and the usual psalms. Small Doxology (Read), Litany: Let us complete ..., On the Aposticha, these Stichera of repentance, in Tone V:`,aposticha:{rubric:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera of repentance, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`Turn away from the multitude of my transgressions O Lord, Who wast born of the Virgin, and cleanse me of all my sins. I beseech Thee to grant me the thought of turning back unto Thee, for Thou alone lovest mankind, and have mercy upon me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, aposticha item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Woe is me, to whom am I like? I am like the barren fig tree, and I fear that I shall be cursed and cut down. But, do Thou O heavenly Husbandman, make my barren soul fruitful, O Christ God, and receive me as the Prodigal Son, and have mercy upon me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, aposticha item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy passion-bearers, O Lord, emulators of the angelic ranks, endured tortures as though bodiless, and in oneness of mind possessed the hope of enjoyment of the good things promised them. By their prayers, O Christ God, grant peace to Thy world and great mercy to our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, aposticha item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`martyrs`}],verses:{ref:`shared.weekday_aposticha_verses.sets.standard_matins`}},aposticha_theotokion:{text:`O thou who art full of grace, * intercede by thy supplications, * and beg that a multitude of compassions be granted to our souls * and the cleansing of our many sins, ** we entreat thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Matins, aposticha Glory/Both-now closer`},type:`theotokion`},closing_rubric:`Then, “It is good to give thanks ...,” Trisagion ..., Our Father ..., Troparia.`},wed:{sessionals:[{rubric:`After the 1st chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymns of the holy and precious Cross, in Tone V:`,spec_mel:null,items:[{text:`The place of the skull became paradise, for no sooner was the tree of the Cross planted than straightway Thou, the grapes of Life, sprang forth, O Savior, unto our gladness. Glory be to Thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, sessional set 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O ye faithful, let us hymn our Savior and Redeemer Who was willingly crucified, as He Himself knew and was well-pleased; and let us glorify Him: For He hath nailed our sins to the Cross, delivering the race of mankind from delusion, and hath granted us the kingdom.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, sessional set 1, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}],verses:[{text:`Exalt ye the Lord our God, * and worship the footstool of His feet, for He is holy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, sessional set 1 verse 1`}}],closer:{text:`When the Mother who bore Thee without the pangs of childbirth * beheld Thee lifted up upon the Cross, * weeping, she lamented crying aloud: * ‘Woe is me, O my sweetest Son! * I am wounded in depths of my soul, * seeing Thee now nailed upon the Cross ** as a malefactor, between two thieves.’`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, sessional set 1 closer`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`}},{rubric:`After the 2nd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymns, in Tone V:`,spec_mel:null,items:[{text:`O Savior Who willingly endured crucifixion and freed us from corruption, we, the faithful, hymn and worship Thee, for Thou hast enlightened us with the power of the Cross; and with fear we glorify Thee as the Lord and Bestower of life, O Compassionate Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, sessional set 2, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The tree of Thy Cross hath been shown to be salvation for the world, for Thou wast willingly nailed to it, delivering mortals from the curse. O Lord, Joy of all, glory be to Thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, sessional set 2, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Zealous for the cup of Thy sufferings, O Lord, the passion- bearers forsook the beauties of life and became communicants with the angels. Through their entreaties, O Christ, grant peace and great mercy to our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, sessional set 2, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`martyrs`}],verses:[{text:`God is our King before the ages; * He hath wrought salvation in the midst of the earth.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, sessional set 2 verse 1`}}],closer:{text:`Through the Cross of thy Son, * O thou who art full of the grace of God, * hath the deception of idolatry been utterly vanquished, * and the might of the demons hath fallen; * wherefore, we, the faithful, ever hymn and bless thee as is meet, ** confessing thee to be the true Theotokos.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, sessional set 2 closer`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`}},{rubric:`After the 3rd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymns, in Tone V:`,spec_mel:`The co-beginningless Word`,items:[{text:`The prophecies of the prophets have already been fulfilled; Thine ancient counsel hath reached its end; for of Thine own will, O Christ, King of all, Thou didst abase Thy self to assume the flesh, and for our sake didst deign to ascend the Cross and endure death. Wherefore, we glorify Thy condescension which passeth understanding, O Word.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, sessional set 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`When the ranks of the angels beheld Thee nailed to the Cross and having fallen asleep, O Jesus, King of all, they were stricken with awe; and straightway the hordes of the demons fled, and the gates of Hades were broken, the tyranny of death was cast down, and those dead in the grave arose.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, sessional set 3, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}],verses:[],closer:{text:`Beholding Thee suspended on the Cross between two thieves of Thine own will, O Christ, Thy Mother, her womb rent asunder maternally, said: “O my sinless Son, how is it that Thou art unjustly nailed to the Cross like a malefactor, desiring to give life to the human race, in that Thou art compassionate?”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, sessional set 3 closer`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`}}],canons:[{title:`Canon of the precious and life-creating Cross, the acrostic whereof is`,heading_rubric:`Canon of the precious and life-creating Cross, the acrostic whereof is`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Christ, who with an upraised arm * bringeth wars to naught, * hath shaken horse and rider in the Red Sea; * but Israel hath He saved * as they chanted a song of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`“Raising up the world, O Christ Thou wast lifted up upon the Tree,” the`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`composition of Joseph, in Tone V:`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Of old, the law-breaking assembly of the Jews lifted up upon the Tree Him Who is inconceivably understood to be incarnate, and Who appeared to the world in the flesh as He desired.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`When the Jews lifted Thee up, suspending Thee, the fruitful vine, upon the tree of the Cross, O Christ, Thou didst exude the wine of gladness which taketh away all the drunkenness of evils, O Word.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Your patience doth not fall under the laws of praise, O martyrs; for ye endured pain past all human nature, and, rejoicing, have made your abode in a rest which is devoid of pain.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Navigating the waves of tortures by the steering of the Word, O all-praised spiritual athletes of Christ, ye reached the harbors of heaven, delighting now in divine tranquility.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 6`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`When thou didst behold the Lord Who had been born of thy womb uplifted unjustly upon the Tree, O Virgin, thou didst shed tears and hymn His truly ineffable condescension.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 7`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`By Thy command Thou didst establish the earth upon nothing * and suspended it unsupported; * do Thou establish Thy Church on the unshakeable rock of Thy commandments, O Christ, * Who alone art good * and the Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`When Thou wast crucified, paradise was opened again and the thief was the first of all to enter therein, rejoicing; and when Thou didst die, O my Jesus, the enemy deceiver was slain, and slain Adam was given life. Glory to Thy surpassing loving-kindness!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Crucified upon the Tree in Thy goodness, O Jesus, Thou didst cause the flame of sin to wither away; bound, Thou hast released mankind from delusion; and stripped naked, Thou hast clothed us in the vesture of glory. Glory be to Thy surpassing compassion!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O Christ Who ever revealeth the martyrs to be shining stars dispelling the darkness of ungodliness: By their supplications drive away the night of mine evils, and enlighten my darkened heart.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`O right glorious martyrs who suffered lawfully, by faith and the law ye were crowned with wreaths, and wisely turning away from the counsels of the iniquitous, ye have received divine sustenance and a dwelling-place in paradise.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`The angelic choirs hymn thee who art indisputably more exalted than them, O all-hymned one; for thou hast given birth in the flesh to God, Who by the Tree annulled the curse of the tree and hath poured forth blessing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Habbakuk, prophetically apprehending * Thy divine self-emptying, O Christ, * cried out to Thee with trembling: * Thou hast come for the salvation of Thy people; * to save Thine anointed ones.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Working never-ending deliverance for men’s souls when willingly hanging of upon the Tree, O Christ, Thou didst commit Thy most holy soul into the hands of the Father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The unjust judge condemned Thee, the righteous Judge, to die suspended upon the Tree, that Thou mightest justify us who unjustly submitted to the enemy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The good things of all time were ye deemed worthy to behold, O martyrs, when ye were openly subjected to many tribulations and afflictions, and countless torments on earth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Ye passed through the winter of trials, and reached the springtime of heavenly reward, O honored martyrs, and ye have been numbered with the angelic choirs.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`The sword of divine sufferings pierced thy soul, O blessed one, when thou didst behold thy Son crucified and surrendering His soul into the hands of the Father.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Thou Who hast clothed Thyself in light as with a garment, * I rise early unto Thee and cry out to Thee: * Enlighten my darkened soul, O Christ, * in that Thou alone art compassionate!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Thou didst stand condemned, O Christ, Thou righteous Judge, condemning the enmity of the flesh; and beaten with a reed, Thou hast signed for me a complete release.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`When it beheld Thee suspended on the Tree in the flesh, O Christ, the sun turned its light into darkness, the earth quaked, and the rocks split asunder.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Ye sanctified the ends of the earth, O all-praised martyrs, suffering as fulfillers of the law of God; and ye have inherited sanctity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Let the all-beauteous and divinely radiant martyrs be honored, who are clothed in divine glory and have laid bare the malice of the enemy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 4`},label:`martyrs`},{text:`We bless thee the all-immaculate Mother of God for whose sake the primal curse hath become infertile, and redemption and blessings have been given.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 5`},label:`plain`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Calm the raging sea of the passions, * O Master Christ, * with its soul-destroying tempest, * and lead me up from corruption * in that Thou art compassionate.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Thou wast lifted up upon the Tree, O Long-suffering One, putting down all the uprisings of the enemy, and in Thy surpassing goodness saving me who have fallen.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`No sooner did the souls of the righteous sense Thee surrendering Thy soul upon the Tree of old, O Word and Master, than they were released from everlasting bonds.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Like hard diamonds ye endured all the burning of torments with patience, and, humbled, ye cast down the enemy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 3`},label:`martyrs`},{text:`As emulators of the sufferings of Christ, ye endured every torture, O passion-bearers of the Lord; wherefore, ye have been deemed worthy of the beauties of heaven.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Wondrous is thine Offspring, Who worketh great miracles and is glorious in His saints, O Lady Theotokos, who alone art all-wondrous.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The supremely exalted Lord of our fathers * quenched the flame, * and bedewed the youths * as they chanted in harmony: * O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`The iniquitous assembly crowned Thee with thorns, O immortal King, who cuttest off the thorns of delusion at the root. Blessed art Thou, O God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`That Thou mightest clothe me in the vesture of incorruption, O Word, Thou didst willingly allow Thyself to be stripped naked; and though dispassionate by nature, Thou didst deign to be spat upon, crucified and subjected to suffering.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Having conformed to the sufferings of Him Who hath dominion over all things, O saints, ye truly became children and heirs to the unshakable kingdom.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Ye did not offer worship to irrational trees, worshipping instead as King and Master Him Who stretched out his hands upon the Tree.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 4`},label:`martyrs`},{text:`Strange is thy birthgiving, O all-immaculate one; for thou hast given birth unto Him Who by the Tree caused the flame of delusion to wither away, enlightening the world.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Unto Thee the Fashioner of all, * the children in the furnace chanted a hymn: * All ye works of the Lord, * supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Most High God, Thou wast lifted up upon the Cross and given gall to eat, O Sweetness of life; and Thou wast pierced by a spear, slaying the serpent who laid Adam low in paradise.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Bound of Thine own will, O Word, Thou freest me from the bonds of sin, binding the apostate foe with eternal bonds, O Savior. Wherefore, I glorify Thy sufferings throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`As secondary lights ye were shown to partake of the immaterial Light, O martyrs, removing the gloom of deception, and divinely illumining the hearts of all the faithful.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Ye became children of the free Jerusalem on high, O martyrs, enlightening the Church of the firstborn and supremely exalting Christ throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Thou didst stand at the Cross, seeing Him to Whom thou hadst given birth nailed thereto, O maiden and Lady; wherefore, thou didst cry out: “Show me not to be childless, O Thou Who art beginningless, the Son and Word of the beginningless Father!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`theotokion`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`O Isaiah, rejoice and be glad! * The Virgin hath conceived in her womb, * and hath borne a Son, Emmanuel, * Who is both God and man; * and Orient is His name; * Him we magnify, and the Virgin we call blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Thou wast lifted up upon the Tree like a lamb, O Christ our Master, breaking the jaws of the noetic wolf, snatching Thy reason-endowed sheep from his jaws, and bringing them to the Father, O Master.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`As King of kings Thou wast crowned with a crown of thorns, O Christ, abolishing the rule of the evil one, and cutting the thorns of delusion off at the root; wherefore, we glorify Thee with faith, O good One.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Your firm and steadfast opposition shone forth like the sun and dispelled all the gloom of the enemy, O right glorious ones, ye invincible martyrs, enlighteners of all the faithful, unshakable towers of piety.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`O all-praised martyrs of the Savior, ye were revealed to be a divinely assembled regiment, a heavenly army, a chosen assembly, a holy encampment, who destroy the cities of the evil one with divine grace.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Thou hast given birth to the Gardener, the Planter of piety Who soweth true understanding on the earth and destroyeth the curse which grew from the garden. And magnifying Him, we call thee, the Virgin, blessed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 5`},label:`theotokion`}]}}},{title:`Another canon of the most holy Theotokos, the acrostic whereof is “This`,heading_rubric:`Another canon of the most holy Theotokos, the acrostic whereof is “This`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Portal of divine glory, who hast opened the gates of paradise, open unto me the doors of repentance, I pray, and enlighten my mind, that I may hymn thee, O divinely joyous one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thou didst restrain the onrushing of death, O all-immaculate one who hast given birth unto Him Who hath dominion over life and death. Him do thou entreat, that He restrain my soul and save me, O thou who puttest transgressions to death.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`The Word Who with the Father is equally without beginning chose thee alone, the beauty of Jacob, from among the generations of mankind, and became incarnate from thy blood. O Lady, save me by thy mediations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Like the fleece thou didst absorb the rain of heaven which descended upon thee, O all-pure one; wherefore, dry up the teeming of my passions, I pray thee, O Virgin Mother.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O pure one, with the remedy inherent in thee wholly heal me, for I have been wounded by the darts of sin. Free me from the pangs which beset me, O thou who by thy birthgiving hast freed the race of mankind from pain.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`O Lady, by thine aid cast down the invisible enemies who assail my lowly heart in vain and seek to slay me, that they may remain impotent and full of shame.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O Lady who hast poured forth upon the world the divine Water, fill me with life-creating waters, dry up the grievous torrents of mine iniquities, and with thy divine serenity still thou the waves of my heart.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The tabernacle of the law hath passed away, for thou hast given birth to Christ, the Bestower of the law, Who layeth down for us the grace of purification and enlightenment, annulling the curse, O most pure and immaculate Virgin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`I have no saving works; wherefore, with hope I flee under thy protection, O all-immaculate Virgin, By thy supplications save me who am desperate.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O pure receptacle of the Light, honored chariot of the Sun: Illumine my heart, which hath been darkened by the gloom of evils, and save me, I pray, O Lady.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`O maiden who of thy virginal blood didst weave a robe for Him Who covereth the sky with clouds: With a robe of incorruption clothe me who have been stripped naked by delusion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The Creator took thee like a lily from the vales of life, and through thee He breathed forth a spiritual fragrance upon the world, O most holy Virgin Bride of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`That I may obtain thine aid O Virgin, I turn to thee before the dread hour when I shall stand before the judgment-seat of Him Who was born from thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O pure one, convert me, who am vanquished by the law of sin, am oft beguiled by the deceptions of the deceiver, and am weighed down by the fetters of my transgressions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O all-immaculate one, who hast given birth to the burning Coal which Isaiah beheld, consume the dross of mine offenses, and enlighten me, I pray.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O Virgin who lent Christ flesh from thy blood, wholly wash away my carnal passions, and show me the way of dispassion.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`May I not be consumed in the depths of despair O Lady, and overwhelmed by the waves of sin, but by thy prayers may I be saved O only pure one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O most pure one, the candle-stand of the law prefigured thee who gave birth to the Light, illuming all creation, wherefore we cry aloud to thee: Do thou enlighten me who am darkened.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O all-pure and compassionate Lady, who gave birth to our blessed Benefactor and Fashioner, do thou bless my wicked soul.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou hast given birth for us to the Bestower of life, the Author of salvation, Who truly granteth everlasting deliverance unto those who proclaim thee the Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 4`},label:`plain`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`I hymn thee, O all-hymned and all-holy Virgin, for without seed thou hast given birth unto the all-hymned God Who deifieth those who chant: O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Mortify my passions, O thou who hast given birth to Life, and raise me up who lie in the grave of insensibility, that I may glorify thee with love, O Bride of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Mercifully regard the supplications of thy servants, O Lady, delivering from misfortunes and saving from tribulations those who chant with faith: O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`O pure one, thou hast given birth unto Him Who is immeasurably powerful, yet Who bore our infirmity. Him do thou beseech, that He heal my soul which is grievously sick.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Virgin who art all-beauteous and divinely radiant, with the vision of beautiful things do thou enlighten me, that I may cry aloud: Hymn the Lord and supremely exalt Him throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O portal of the Light, open unto me the splendid gates of repentance, showing me every straight path of righteousness which grants entry to the will of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`To the holy Word Who sanctifieth the faithful didst thou ineffably give birth, O pure one. Him do thou entreat, O all-holy one, that He now sanctify my lowly soul which hath been defiled by evil.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`The Lord of all, the Torrent of light and Wellspring of immortality, issued forth from thee, O holy Lady; wherefore, I cry to thee, O pure one: With the showers of thy prayers dry up the streams of mine evils.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`refrain: “More honorable than the cherubim ...,” and make prostrations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 5`},label:`plain`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O pure one, thou hast given birth to the Savior, the unshakable Foundation, Who by His command founded the earth upon the waters. Him do thou entreat, that He make us steadfast who in a pure manner call thee blessed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O pure one, cause me to walk, unerringly and without being led astray, the path of the humility of the precepts of God, driving far from me the turmoil of the demons and the assaults of the passions, and granting me tranquility.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The enemy, seeing me stuck fast in the slumber of indifference, mightily attacks me, hoping to carry me off by pleasurable dreams; but do thou thyself preserve me by thy tireless supplication, O pure Virgin Mother.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`As one self-condemned I ponder the multitude of my sins and the dread tribunal of the Judge, at which I must needs be tried. But as she who gave birth unto God the Judge, O Theotokos, preserve me uncondemned at that time.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}]}}}],magnificat_rubric:`We then chant the hymn of the Theotokos (the Magnificat), with the`,post_canon_rubric:`Then, “It is truly meet to bless thee ...,” and a prostration. Small litany, Exapostilarion, and the usual psalms. Small Doxology (Read), Litany: Let us complete ..., On the Aposticha, these Stichera of the precious Cross, in Tone V:`,aposticha:{rubric:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera of the precious Cross, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`No sooner was the tree of Thy Cross planted, O Christ, than the deception of idols was driven away and grace blossomed forth; for the tyranny of condemnation was no more, but the triumph of our salvation was made manifest. For the Cross is our boast, the Cross is our confirmation, the Cross is our joy!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, aposticha item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`For our sake Thou wast led as a sheep to sacrifice and as an innocent lamb to voluntary slaughter, O Christ Immanuel, as one reckoned among the iniquitous. Come, O ye nations of the homeland, and hymn and worship the endless Life Who was lifted up upon the Cross!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, aposticha item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Struggling on earth, the holy martyrs endured the cold and gave themselves over to the fire. And as the waters received them their cry was: “We went through fire and water, and Thou didst bring us out into refreshment!” By their supplications, O Christ God, have mercy upon us!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, aposticha item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`}],verses:{ref:`shared.weekday_aposticha_verses.sets.standard_matins`}},aposticha_theotokion:{text:`Of old, the Virgin Mother, the all-blessed maiden, beholding the Lamb, her Son, lifted up upon the Cross, cried out, weeping: ''Woe is me, O my Son! How is it that Thou diest Who art in essence God immortal?”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Matins, aposticha Glory/Both-now closer`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`},closing_rubric:`Then, “It is good to give thanks ...,” Trisagion ..., Our Father ..., Troparia.`},thu:{sessionals:[{rubric:`st After the 1 chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymns of the holy apostles, in Tone V:`,spec_mel:null,items:[{text:`With spiritual songs and hymns let all of us on earth praise the most wise apostles as eyewitnesses and servants of the Word; for they earnestly entreat Christ on behalf of us who hymn their sacred memory and bow down before their relics.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, sessional set 1, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Together let us praise the apostles as eye-witnesses of the Word, divine preachers, spiritual fishers of the nations, for they have clearly brought us to an understanding of Christ; and having delivered the race of mankind from delusion, they have granted us the kingdom.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, sessional set 1, item 2`},label:`plain`}],verses:[{text:`Their sound hath gone forth into all the earth, * and their words unto the ends of the world.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, sessional set 1 verse 1`}}],closer:{text:`I am condemned by the court of my conscience, and considering my plea before I am brought to trial, I tremble, wretch that I am, remembering the multitude of mine evils. Yet unto thee, who art mine invincible intercessor and protection, do I cry out with compunction: Deliver me from that shame, and save me by thy prayers!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, sessional set 1 closer`},type:`theotokion`}},{rubric:`After the 2nd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymns, in Tone V:`,spec_mel:null,items:[{text:`Together let us praise the apostles, for they preached the Orthodox doctrine of the Lord unto all, dispelling the gloom of heresies and shining forth in the world the light of the Spirit through the teaching of grace; and they pray that we be saved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, sessional set 2, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Together let us praise the apostles ...,`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, sessional set 2, item 2 (incipit repeat, §2.7)`},label:`plain`,incipit_ref:`tone5.matins_weekday.thu.sessionals[1].items[0]`},{text:`The hosts of heaven exceedingly marveled at the corrections of the holy martyrs; how, fighting the good fight in their mortal bodies, they invisibly vanquished the incorporeal foe with the power of the Cross; and they pray unto the Lord, that our souls find mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, sessional set 2, item 3`},label:`martyrs`}],verses:[{text:`The heavens declare the glory of God, * and the firmament proclaimeth the work of His hands.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, sessional set 2 verse 1`}},{text:`Wondrous is God in His saints, * the God of Israel.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, sessional set 2 verse 2`}}],closer:{text:`Finding thee to be a haven, a bulwark, a refuge, our hope, protection and fervent help, we, the faithful, hasten to thee and cry out earnestly, exclaiming with faith: Have mercy upon those who place their trust in thee, O Theotokos, and deliver us from transgressions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, sessional set 2 closer`},type:`theotokion`}},{rubric:`After the 3rd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymns, in Tone V:`,spec_mel:null,items:[{text:`O disciples of the Savior, divine apostles, who sowed the word of salvation unto the ends of all the earth, and illumined those sitting in darkness and shadow: By your supplications, O all-praised ones, enlighten my soul, which hath been darkened by the darkness of the passions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, sessional set 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Preaching the ineffable mystery of Thine incarnation, O Lord, illiterate men put philosophers to shame; fishermen shut the mouths of rhetors. And they became most wise teachers of the nations, illumining the ends of the earth with the light of divine understanding. Through them grant us great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, sessional set 3, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}],verses:[],closer:{text:`We who have thee as our unashamed hope, O Virgin who art our protection, free us from divers perils, evil circumstances and grievous tribulations, and with His apostles beseech thy Son, that He save all who hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, sessional set 3 closer`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],type:`theotokion`}}],canons:[{title:`Canon of the holy apostles, the composition of Theophanes, Bishop of Nicea, in`,heading_rubric:`Canon of the holy apostles, the composition of Theophanes, Bishop of Nicea, in`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Christ, who with an upraised arm * bringeth wars to naught, * hath shaken horse and rider in the Red Sea; * but Israel hath He saved * as they chanted a song of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Enriched by the effulgence of Him Who first bestowed the gift of light, and Who deigned to converse with men in the flesh, O glorious and divine apostles, release my soul from all darkness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`Having been drawn, the divine Bow loosed you like arrows upon the whole world, O apostles, breaking all the arrows of the wicked and crafty one, and healing the wounds of the faithful.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Possessed of the very wisdom of the Teacher, O apostles, ye made wise all the ends of the earth; wherefore, make me wise, that I may fend off every wicked scheme of the enemy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O most pure one, who alone art blessed and full of divine joy, having filled the race of mankind with joy by thy blessings, with the divine apostles entreat Christ, that we find mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`By Thy command Thou didst establish the earth upon nothing * and suspended it unsupported; * do Thou establish Thy Church on the unshakeable rock of Thy commandments, O Christ, * Who alone art good * and the Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`He Who is exceeding great in goodness, and beggared Himself by assuming flesh, enriched you with all manner of gifts, O glorious apostles, who became poor for His sake and have enriched the ends of the earth with divine and honorable understandings.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`I have sustained the venomous bite of the serpent, and my heart hath been wounded; wherefore, I cry out to Thee, O Christ, Who wast wounded for my sake: By the prayers of Thine apostles heal and save me, I pray!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Having drawn me forth from the depths of the evil adversary, from the threefold waves of wicked thoughts, and from deadly passions, with the net of your prayers, O all-blessed ones, bring me, saved, unto the God of all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O thou who received the Rain of heaven, with the apostles entreat Him to cause the torrents of my passions to cease their flow, drying up my sin, and to save me who glorify thee in a pure manner.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Habbakuk, prophetically apprehending * Thy divine self-emptying, O Christ, * cried out to Thee with trembling: * Thou hast come for the salvation of Thy people; * to save Thine anointed ones.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`As the Door, Jesus, our God and Lord, opened to the apostles the understanding of Him, and through their teachings opened the door to all the nations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`O Son of God, by fellowship Thou didst reveal the apostles to be sons of the heavenly Father. Through their entreaty make us all children of the light.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O apostles who will most gloriously be seated on twelve thrones with the Judge and King, deliver me from the awesome and dread trial.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O ark of divine sanctity, hallow my soul and enlighten my mind, ever praying to Christ with the apostles, that He save me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`O Thou Who hast clothed Thyself in light as with a garment, * I rise early unto Thee and cry out to Thee: * Enlighten my darkened soul, O Christ, * in that Thou alone art compassionate!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`In the upper room, the rhetors of the Spirit, the honored apostles, beheld the Holy Spirit Who came upon them in the form of fire, receiving Him in an awesome manner.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 1`},label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`O apostles, ye who have crushed ungodliness, with the dew of healing heal my mind, which hath been crushed by transgressions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O apostles, Christ sent you forth like choice arrows, breaking the arrows of wickedness; wherefore, heal me who have been wounded by the arrows of the enemy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`“Condemn me not, neither turn Thy face away from me, O greatly Merciful One!”, for the council of the apostles and she who gave birth to Thee entreat Thee in a pure manner.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Calm the raging sea of the passions, * O Master Christ, * with its soul-destroying tempest, * and lead me up from corruption * in that Thou art compassionate.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`With the salt of the teaching of Thy sacred disciples Thou didst put an end to the corruption of evil for the souls of the nations, O Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`Thou knowest the depths of mine evils, O Master Christ. Grant me Thy hand, and by the supplications of Thy sacred apostles save me, O Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`O most righteous Judge, on the dread day of judgment deliver me, who tremble, from condemnation, by the supplications of Thy right glorious apostles.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`From the multitude of mine iniquities grant salvation unto me who am desperate, by the supplications of Thy disciples and Thy Mother.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 4`},label:`theotokion`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The supremely exalted Lord of our fathers * quenched the flame, * and bedewed the youths * as they chanted in harmony: * O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`The supremely exalted Lord of our fathers exceedingly exalted you, O disciples of Christ who beheld God, casting down all the power of the enemy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`With streams of compunction and your supplications, O apostles, wash away the defilement of my heart, teaching me to cry: O God, blessed art Thou!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`With the fire of the divine Spirit ye burned up the tinder of all vanity; wherefore, deliver me from burning Gehenna, O disciples of God the Word.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O Virgin who set aright the fall of Adam, by your prayers and those of the divine apostles, raise me up who have fallen into the precipice of evil.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Unto Thee the Fashioner of all, * the children in the furnace chanted a hymn: * All ye works of the Lord, * supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Word, Thou didst send forth Thine apostles as noetic clouds which let fall upon us the rain of most wise and divine teachings, giving us drink throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`O beholders of God, pillars of the Church all-adorned, surrounding it with the teachings of the Faith: with divine skill make steadfast the defiled house of my soul.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Groan thou, O my soul, and offer unto the Lord torrents of tears from the depths of thy heart, crying aloud: O only Compassionate One, save and purify me through the right acceptable prayers of the all-glorious apostles.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`O most pure Virgin, chosen Sion, city of the King: make me a citizen of the city on high, entreating Thy timeless Son with the divine disciples.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`O Isaiah, rejoice and be glad! * The Virgin hath conceived in her womb, * and hath borne a Son, Emmanuel, * Who is both God and man; * and Orient is His name; * Him we magnify, and the Virgin we call blessed.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`By the splendors of divine virtues ye were noetically revealed to be starry skies, having Christ, the Sun, in your midst; and ye have renewed the ends of the earth, O most wise ones; wherefore, we call you blessed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,repeat:2},{text:`Bearing the wounds of Christ upon your divine bodies like an all-magnificent armor, O most wise ones, by your mediations before the Lord heal my soul, which hath been wounded by the darts of the demons.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`In that Thou raised up Lazarus, O Christ, Lord and Word, by Thy disciples save me who lie in the uttermost abyss of sin, having weighed down my soul with the sleep of grievous slothfulness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Direct the steps of my soul straight to the paths of Thine unerring commandments, O Word of God, having the most pure Virgin who gave birth to Thee praying to Thee with Thy most wise apostles, O greatly Merciful One.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`theotokion`}]}},composer:`Theophanes`},{title:`Another canon, of the holy hierarch Nicholas, the acrostic whereof is “I offer a fifth hymn unto thee, O Nicholas,” the composition of Joseph, in Tone V`,heading_rubric:`Another canon, of the holy hierarch Nicholas, the acrostic whereof is “I offer a fifth hymn unto thee, O Nicholas,” the composition of Joseph, in Tone V:`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Uniting thyself unto God by faith and love, O father, thou didst fulfill His all- holy desires, and thereby didst become holy in all things, O wise and holy hierarch Nicholas.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Having thee as an intercessor before the Compassionate One, we who are beset by perils and griefs flee unto thee. Grant thou a saving hand, delivering us from all difficulties.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Christ anointed thee for the people of Myra as a holy hierarch who filleth us with the sweet fragrance of miracles; wherefore, we beseech thee, O Nicholas, to deliver us from the foul stench of sin.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Of old, the choir of the prophets foretold thee to be the divine mountain and impassable portal, O Virgin. Wherefore O maiden, we pray thee: Open unto us the divine gates of repentance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`theotokion`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`With the opposition of thy divine labors, O venerable one, thou didst break the arrows of the evil one. And by thy supplications, O most wise one, preserve thou, unharmed by his malice and violence, those who hymn thee, O great Nicholas.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:3}],label:`plain`},{text:`Having shown forth an angelic life on earth, thou now ever standest with the angels before the throne of the Trinity, O sacred one, asking remission of our offenses and temptations, O father and chief hierarch Nicholas.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`By thy luminous supplications drive away all darkness from my mind, O Nicholas; still the tempest of my passions, O father, and steer me to the harbor of dispassion, I pray, that I may glorify thee in praise.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Standing at the right hand of Christ as a Queen truly arrayed in golden vesture, O all-immaculate and divinely joyous maiden, by thy prayers win for us the kingdom of heaven.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Thou didst exchange fleeting things for things yet to come, O Nicholas. By thy prayers cause us also to share therein, delivering us from every temptation of life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`As first hierarch of the people of Myra, O holy Nicholas, perfume with myrrh all the senses of my heart, and by thy prayers ever drive from it the fetid passions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Foil all the enemy’s wiles, visible and invisible, O Nicholas, and send to never- ending perdition our foes, who ever wage war upon us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O holy Theotokos, save me who am constantly drowning in carnal pleasures and lie, ever groaning, upon my bed of despair.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Thou didst break asunder the graven idols and show the counsels of the heretics to be impotent, O holy Nicholas, and didst deliver those sentenced to death.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Having risen early unto the Lord from childhood, O venerable one, thou wast wholly enlightened by the heavenly radiance; wherefore pray thou that cloudiness be driven from my soul.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`We beseech thee, O father Nicholas: At the dread hour be thou among all who call upon thee, and grant us our petitions which are conducive to salvation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`He Who is inaccessible to the mind of man, as one mortal took thee as His possession, delivering all from besetting tribulations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 4`},label:`theotokion`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`By thy supplications render the Master merciful unto all who honor thee, O Nicholas, that He may grant us remission of our sins.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Deliver from infirmities and the temptations of life, from perils and tribulations, those who have acquired thee as an advocate before the Lord, O Nicholas.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Christ the Master hath shown thee to be an excellent physician; wherefore, heal thou the infirmities of those who approach thee in piety, O Nicholas.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast a mother who knew no husband, O pure Mother of God; wherefore, I pray thee with faith: Dispel the despondency of my soul.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Having relied wholly on God, O divinely wise Nicholas, wholly save me who am ever wretchedly tripped by the passions of life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O divinely radiant lamp, illumine my mind which is ever darkened by the gloom of the passions, and grant that I may walk nobly in this life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Every wicked mouth which is opened against me do thou shut by thy prayers, O Nicholas, delivering me from enemies, visible and invisible.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`From thee, O all-radiant cloud, did Christ our God, the never- setting Sun, shine forth upon us, illumining those in the darkness of ignorance, O Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`theotokion`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Nicholas, who wast a great hierarch in Myra, perfume the senses of my soul with myrrh, that I may escape the stench of the passions and receive the grace of the Comforter.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`With streams pouring forth from thy holy tongue, O most wise one, thou didst stop the streams of the blasphemy of Arius; wherefore, we cry out to thee: By thy supplications dry up the streams of my passions, O all-blessed Nicholas!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`By thy supplications deliver us from our offenses, from the oppression of the demons, foreign captivity, and the most evil and wicked harm caused by men, that we may praise thee, our deliverer.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Triadicon: Unceasingly glorifying with faith the monarchy of the Trinity, we cry out: O Father, Word and all-holy Spirit, we hymn Thee throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Having clad Himself in flesh taken from thee for our sake, O Virgin, God showed thee, the pure and all-immaculate one, to be the divine intercessor for the whole race of mankind; wherefore, we, the faithful, hymn thee aloud.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`},{text:`refrain: “More honorable than the cherubim ...,” and make prostrations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 6`},label:`plain`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`As a divine and holy hierarch thou didst keep all the commandments of Christ; wherefore, thou wast the godly preserver of the faithful. O father Nicholas, preserve them from all perils and afflictions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`As a good shepherd thou didst feed thy city, which was starving in hunger, so now feed my soul with the bread of understanding, O father Nicholas, for I have acquired thee as a good helper.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O venerable pastor, with faith we entreat thee, the great sun which ever riseth above the Church of Christ: With radiant beams of light drive away the deep gloom of sins from our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The dread day of the coming of Christ draweth nigh, as it is written. Rouse thyself, O my soul, and cast off slothfulness, and cry aloud to Christ: Save me, O Lord, by the prayers of Thy servant Nicholas!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`O most pure one, the prophet foresaw thee as the radiant lampstand bearing Christ, the noetic Lamp, by Whom those who lie in darkness and the passions have been enlightened, wherefore we call thee blessed, O Ever- virgin Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`theotokion`}]}},acrostic:`I offer a fifth hymn unto thee, O Nicholas`,composer:`Joseph`}],magnificat_rubric:`We then chant the hymn of the Theotokos (the Magnificat), with the`,post_canon_rubric:`Then, “It is truly meet to bless thee ...,” and a prostration. Small litany, Exapostilarion, and the usual psalms. Small Doxology (Read), Litany: Let us complete ..., On the Aposticha, these Stichera of the holy apostles, in Tone V:`,aposticha:{rubric:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera of the holy apostles, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`As eye-witnesses to the mysteries of the Savior, O disciples, ye preached the Invisible One Who hath no beginning, saying: In the beginning was the Word. Ye were not created before the angels, nor were ye taught of men, but by the wisdom of the Most High. Wherefore, as ye have boldness, pray ye on behalf of our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, aposticha item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Together let us praise the apostles of the Lord with hymns, for, having arrayed themselves in the armor of the Cross, they abolished the delusion of the demons and were shown to be crowned victors. By the supplications of them and all the saints, O God, have mercy upon us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, aposticha item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoicing in the midst of their torments, the saints cried out: “These things are goods with which we trade with the Lord: for, instead of the wounds we bear on our bodies, radiant vesture shall blossom forth for us unto our resurrection; instead of dishonor, we shall receive crowns; instead of fetters in prison, we shall receive paradise; and instead of condemnation with malefactors, we shall have life with the angels!” By their supplications, O Lord, save Thou our souls!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, aposticha item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`}],verses:{ref:`shared.weekday_aposticha_verses.sets.thursday_matins_as_printed`}},aposticha_theotokion:{text:`We bless thee, O Virgin Theotokos, * for from thee hath shone forth Christ, the Sun of righteousness, ** Who hath great mercy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Matins, aposticha Glory/Both-now closer`},type:`theotokion`},closing_rubric:`Then, “It is good to give thanks ...,” Trisagion ..., Our Father ..., Troparia.`},fri:{sessionals:[{rubric:`After the 1st chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymns of the holy and precious Cross, in Tone V:`,spec_mel:null,items:[{text:`The place of the skull became paradise, for no sooner was the tree of the Cross planted than straightway Thou, the Grapes of life, sprang forth, O Savior, unto our gladness. Glory be to Thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, sessional set 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O ye faithful, let us hymn our Savior and Redeemer, Who was willingly crucified, as He Himself knew and was well-pleased to do; and let us glorify Him, for He hath nailed the sins of all to the Cross, delivering the race of mankind from delusion, and hath granted us the kingdom.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, sessional set 1, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}],verses:[{text:`Exalt ye the Lord our God, * and worship the footstool of His feet, for He is holy.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, sessional set 1 verse 1`}}],closer:{text:`Beholding Thee hanging willingly on the Cross between the thieves, O Christ, Thy Mother said maternally, her womb rent with pain: “O my sinless Son, how is it that Thou art unjustly nailed to the Cross as a malefactor, Who desirest to give life to the race of mankind, in that Thou art compassionate?”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, sessional set 1 closer`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`}},{rubric:`After the 2nd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymns, in Tone V:`,spec_mel:null,items:[{text:`O Savior Who of Thine own will endured crucifixion and freed us from corruption, we, the faithful, hymn and worship Thee, for Thou hast enlightened us with the power of the Cross; and with fear we glorify Thee as Lord and the Bestower of life, O Compassionate Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, sessional set 2, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`The tree of Thy Cross hath been shown to be salvation for the world, for Thou wast willingly affixed to it, delivering mortals from the curse. O Lord, Joy of all, glory be to Thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, sessional set 2, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Today the memory of the passion-bearers shineth forth with radiance from the heavens; the choir of the angels keepeth festival, and the race of mankind celebrateth with them. Wherefore, they pray unto the Lord, that our souls find mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, sessional set 2, item 3`},label:`martyrs`}],verses:[{text:`God is our King before the ages; * He hath wrought salvation in the midst of the earth.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, sessional set 2 verse 1`}},{text:`Wondrous is God in His saints, * the God of Israel.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, sessional set 2 verse 2`}}],closer:{text:`Through the Cross of thy Son, O thou who art full of the grace of God, hath the deception of idolatry been utterly vanquished, and the might of the demons hath fallen; wherefore, we, the faithful, ever hymn and bless thee as is meet, confessing thee to be the true Theotokos.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, sessional set 2 closer`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`}},{rubric:`After the 3rd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymns, in Tone V:`,spec_mel:`The co-beginningless Word`,items:[{text:`When the ranks of the angels beheld Thee nailed to the Cross and having fallen asleep, O Jesus, King of all, they were stricken with awe; and straightway the hordes of the demons fled, and the gates of Hades were broken, the tyranny of death was cast down, and those dead in the grave arose.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, sessional set 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Adam received bitterness from the tree, falling headlong into corruption through the envy of the serpent; but when Thou wast nailed thereto O Jesus, life was planted, and because of the tree of the Cross we have once again made our abode in the heavens, the serpent hath been set at naught, corruption hath been slain, and we all offer Thee glory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, sessional set 3, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}],verses:[],closer:{text:`When the Mother who bore Thee without the pangs of childbirth beheld Thee lifted up upon the Cross, weeping, she lamented crying aloud: ‘‘Woe is me, O my sweetest Son! I am wounded in depths of my soul, seeing Thee now nailed upon the Cross as a malefactor, between two thieves.’’`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, sessional set 3 closer`},type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`}}],canons:[{title:`Canon of the precious and life-creating Cross, the acrostic whereof is “By Thy Passion Thou dost save me from the passions, O my Christ,” the composition of Joseph, in Tone V`,heading_rubric:`Canon of the precious and life-creating Cross, the acrostic whereof is “By Thy Passion Thou dost save me from the passions, O my Christ,” the composition of Joseph, in Tone V:`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Unto God the Savior * Who made His people pass dryshod through the sea, * but drowned Pharaoh with all his host, * unto Him alone let us sing: * For He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`It was Thine own desire to didst endure the passion-slaying Passion, O Christ, and thereby slay him who of old brought death upon us in paradise; wherefore, we glorify Thy goodness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast lifted up upon the Cross, and the enemy fell headlong; and we, who are fallen, have been raised up and been made inhabitants of paradise, O Christ, glorifying the might of Thy kingdom.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Well armed with the shield of the Cross, ye arrayed yourselves for every battle with the demon, O most wise great-martyrs; and having vanquished him, ye have received glory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Like honored sheep ye offered yourselves unto the Lamb Who was slain for our sake, O spiritual athletes, manifestly abolishing the sacrifices of the ungodly; wherefore, we call you blessed, O all-praised ones.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`For us, O pure Virgin, thou hast given birth to a little Babe, the Ancient of days, Who by His divine sufferings hath renewed human nature, which had grown old, O all-immaculate one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`theotokion`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`By the power of Thy Cross, O Christ, * do Thou make steadfast mine understanding, * that I may hymn and glorify Thine arising on the third day.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Nailed to the Tree, O Savior, Thou dost cause the fruit of corruption to wither away, and from Thy side poured forth upon us streams of incorruption, O Master.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast slaughtered on the Tree like a lamb, O Master, marking the linings of our souls with Thy divine blood; wherefore, we glorify Thee with fear.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Bound with bonds, wounded in many and various ways, and cast to the wild beasts, O spiritual athletes, ye remained unshaken.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`As grapes of the Vine of life ye poured forth the wine of martyrdom which gladdens the hearts of the faithful, O martyrs of our God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Dying upon the Cross, thy Son and Lord was shown to be the Mediator of life for us, O pure one, glorifying those who hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`I have heard report of the mighty deed * of Thy Cross, O Lord, * how Paradise was opened thereby, and I cried: * Glory to Thy power, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`When Thou didst set upon the Cross, O Christ, Sun of righteousness, Thou didst shine forth never-waning light upon us who hymn Thine awesome dispensation, O Word.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`When once thou didst stand before the judgment-seat, O Christ our Judge, Thou didst condemn the unjust foe; and Thou wast crucified between the unrighteous thieves, justifying us.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Crowned with victory, the spiritual athletes of the Lord put the invisible enemy to shame, and cried aloud: Glory be to Thy power, O Lord!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Assembling with faith, let us honor the passion-bearers of Christ, the never-fading flowers of the noetic paradise, the most precious vessels.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 4`},label:`martyrs`},{text:`When thou didst behold on the Cross Christ to Whom thou hast given birth, O pure one, thou didst marvel at His ineffable long-suffering; wherefore, with Him we glorify thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Waking at dawn, * we cry unto Thee, O Lord: * Save us, for Thou art our God; * we know none other besides Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`When the rocks felt Thee lifted up upon the Tree, O Christ, they split asunder, and the foundations of the earth were shaken.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The sun set aside its radiance when Thou wast lifted up upon the Tree, O long-suffering Sun of righteousness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The saints shine forth with the radiance of miracles, by the Spirit dispelling the darkness of sicknesses.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 3`},label:`martyrs`},{text:`Your bodies were dismembered with the sword, O martyrs, but the spirit of divine love was never severed from you.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Seeing the Savior lifted up upon the Cross, O all-immaculate Virgin Mother, thou didst lift up thy voice in lamentation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`The abyss hath encompassed me, * the sea monster hath become my grave; * but I cried unto Thee, * the Lover of mankind, * and Thy right hand saved me, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`When the Cross was planted in the ground, the fall of the demons came about, faith received the beginning of its confirmation, and evil hath been driven from our midst.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The sun was extinguished when Thou didst light Thy flesh like a lamp upon the Tree, O Lord; and the coin was found which had been lost through the dark passions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`When Thou wast lifted up upon the Tree, Thou didst have the choir of martyrs following in Thy steps, emulating Thy Passion as the mediator of dispassion, O Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`With the streams of your blood ye dried up the torrents of delusion, O crowned martyrs, and ye extinguished the alien fire of the demons with divine dew.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`A sword pierced thy heart, O all-immaculate Virgin, when thou didst behold the Creator crucified, His divine side pierced by a spear.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The children were saved * in the burning furnace, * chanting: Blessed art Thou * O God of our fathers.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`That we might be delivered from pleasurable sin, Thou didst taste gall, O Christ, Thou sweetness of life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`When Thou wast wounded on the Tree, O Christ, Thou didst heal the wounds Adam had suffered for many years.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`With eagerness of will ye set yourselves apart for suffering, O passion-bearers, and were shown to be victors.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Having honored God by enduring painful dishonor, O spiritual athletes, ye received honor on high.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`After giving birth thou hast remained as thou wast before birthgiving, O pure one; for God was born, that He might deify mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`The Son of God who before all ages * wast born of the Father * hath in these last times * become incarnate of the Virgin Mother, * O ye priests hymn, * and ye peoples supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Savior, Who healed the curse of the tree by the Tree and hast poured forth blessing upon mankind, we hymn and glorify Thee throughout the ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`By Thy Cross Thou didst bring down the serpent who exalted himself, and when Thou wast laid low Thou didst raise up him who had grievously fallen. Thee, O Savior, do we hymn and supremely exalt throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`With faith let us hymn the passion-bearers in the heavens: the destroyers of delusion, the champions of the divine Faith, the pillars of the Church, the truly hard diamonds, the warriors of Christ.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 3`},label:`martyrs`},{text:`The glorious passion-bearers shone forth like the sun, through grace driving away the clouds of sicknesses; and by faith in the Trinity they dispelled the gloom of ungodliness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 4`},label:`martyrs`},{text:`Gabriel was sent as an escort for the bride, O Virgin, and he cried out to thee, saying: O most splendid palace of Christ, the King of all, when He shall make His abode within thee, He shall deify all mankind!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`theotokion`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Thee the true Mother of God, * who above all understanding * and beyond all description, * ineffably brought forth in time * the Eternal One, * with one mind do we the faithful magnify.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`The might and dominion of the enemy were taken away, O only mighty Lord, when Thou wast lifted up upon the Cross and didst bloody Thy fingers thereon.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O my Christ, the iniquitous ones who crucified Thee impaled Thy hands and feet and reckoned the number of Thy bones; and they gave thee vinegar with gall to drink.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Before the tyrants ye preached God Who became man with radiant mouths, O passion-bearers, and have inherited glory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Beating you, the enemies who wounded you with stripes and divers tortures became sick, O divine martyrs, all-honored physicians of illnesses.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`Jesus the Light shone forth upon us from thee, O pure one, and enlightened all creation by His crucifixion, dispelling the darkness of the demons.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`theotokion`}]}},acrostic:`By Thy Passion Thou dost save me from the passions, O my Christ`,composer:`Joseph`},{title:`Another canon of the most holy Theotokos, in Tone V`,heading_rubric:`Another canon of the most holy Theotokos, in Tone V:`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`I know thee, O all-immaculate Mary, Virgin and Mother, to be a wellspring of compassion and a fervent intercessor; and I cry out to thee: Have mercy and compassion upon my humbled soul.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Making His abode within thy womb, and taking human essence upon Himself, in that He is good, O pure one, the Son of God hath delivered all from the corruption of the serpent.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Be mine enlightenment and hope of salvation, O all-immaculate Birthgiver of God, loosing the bonds of my transgressions, and delivering me from the torments and condemnation which are to come.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Free my lowly soul from wicked thoughts, O Birthgiver of God, and make it a dwelling-place of God, that I may always glorify thee as is meet.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`By thy compassionate goodness, O Birthgiver of God, lead me up who have fallen into the destructive pit of grievous offenses.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Arriving at the eventide of life, I am held fast by perplexity, O all-hymned one, and I cry out to thee: Show thyself to be my helper!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O pure and holy Theotokos, grant me remission of sins, and ask for me salvation and everlasting joy.'`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Grant me tear-drops, O pure one, that I may drive doubt from my heart and earnestly hymn thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Who can entreat the Judge concerning my wicked deeds and my transgressions if not thee, O pure one, thou only helper of the sinful?`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`By thy power, O most pure one, raise me up who have fallen through many transgressions and enslaved my soul through sins, and free me from slavery by thy prayer.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`As thou hast given birth to the Creator and King of all, O all-immaculate and pure Theotokos, deliver me from every vile offense.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`I weep over myself when I bring to mind my many transgressions and the unquenchable fire; and I pray: Grant me time to repent, O most pure one.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Lady, apply the bandages of thy tender compassion to the bruises which through sin have come to cover my whole body.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Of old thou didst halt the advance of corruption by thy divine birthgiving, O most immaculate one, and thou hast now staunched the progress of my sins.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Have mercy and compassion upon my soul, O Lady, and deliver it from condemnation and eternal torment.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Look down and hearken unto my voice, O Lady, and deliver me from everlasting torment, I pray.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`The deep of transgressions hath surrounded me, and the abyss of sin hath firmly gripped me, and bringeth me to pernicious despair. But save me now, O holy Lady!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Raise me up who lie upon the bed offenses, O most holy Lady, and grant me the effulgence of salvation through repentance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Through the supplications of her who in purity gave birth to Thee, cleanse me, O Lover of mankind; and deliver Thy world from all tribulation, and vouchsafe us everlasting glory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`I ever promise to cease mine evil deeds, yet I always lie, and grieve my Master. O most pure Lady, grant me correction.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O pure Birthgiver of God, disdain me not who with faith ever flee beneath thy protection.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`O Birthgiver of God who ever driest up the pasture of my passions, grant that I may shed abundant drops of tears.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`By thy supplications release me who am bound with the chains of my sins, O most immaculate one, for thou hast given birth to our all-hymned God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Unto thee do I flee with faith, O pure one, and to thee do I cry: Deliver me from everlasting fire, O Virgin!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`At a loss, I have no fear of the threat of Gehenna in either heart or mind, and I ever commit sins; but do thou, O Virgin, free me from vexation, and deliver me from the fire.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`I am often dragged out and sold like a captive by the pleasures of my flesh, and I ever anger God. O Theotokos, thou only help of the helpless, do thou thyself have mercy upon me!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thy prayer is sure and certain, O all-immaculate one, for whatsoever things thou desirest thou givest, entreating thy Son and God. Wherefore, I pray thee: Have mercy and save my lowly soul!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`I am cruelly tested by bodily sickness, rising passions and wounds of soul. O thou who hast given birth to the only Benefactor, by thy supplications restore my health.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`refrain: “More honorable than the cherubim ...,” and make prostrations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 5`},label:`plain`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`Same as the foregoing.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Grant me tears of repentance before the end of my life arrives, O most pure one, that I may weep over my grievous and unjust deeds.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Why dost thou offend thy Master, O my soul, committing unrighteous deeds? Why dost thou not arise? Wherefore, before the end hasten thou to repent.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Deliver me from evil transgressions and tribulations. Grant me mercy, O all- pure Virgin, and a divine share in incorruptible life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thee have we acquired as the intercessor who hast ineffably given birth unto God, the insurmountable rampart and salvation of our souls, and a wellspring of miracles.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 4`},label:`plain`}]}}}],magnificat_rubric:`We then chant the hymn of the Theotokos (the Magnificat), with the`,post_canon_rubric:`Then, “It is truly meet to bless thee ...,” and a prostration. Small litany, Exapostilarion, and the usual psalms. Small Doxology (Read), Litany: Let us complete ..., On the Aposticha, these Stichera of the precious Cross, in Tone V:`,aposticha:{rubric:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera of the precious Cross, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`No sooner was the tree of Thy Cross planted, O Christ, than the deception of idols was driven away and grace blossomed forth; for the tyranny of condemnation was found no more, but the triumph of our salvation was made manifest. For the Cross is our boast, the Cross is our confirmation, the Cross is our joy!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, aposticha item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`For our sake Thou wast led as a sheep to sacrifice and as an innocent lamb to voluntary slaughter, O Christ Immanuel; and Thou wast reckoned among the iniquitous. Come, O ye nations of the homeland, and hymn and worship the endless Life Who was lifted up upon the Cross!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, aposticha item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Blessed is the army of the King of heaven, for even though the passion-bearers were mortal, yet they strived to attain the dignity of the angels; and having spurned their bodies, for the sake of their passions they have been deemed worthy of honors. By their supplications, O Lord, save Thou our souls!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, aposticha item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`}],verses:{ref:`shared.weekday_aposticha_verses.sets.standard_matins`}},aposticha_theotokion:{text:`Standing at the foot of the Cross, O Jesus, she who gave birth to Thee lamented, weeping and cried aloud: “I cannot bear these things, seeing Thee to Whom I gave birth nailed to the Tree! I escaped the pangs of childbirth, since I never knew a husband, so how now am I wracked with pain and wounded in heart? For now the words spoken by Symeon have been fulfilled: ‘A sword shall pierce thy heart, O immaculate one!’ Yet now arise, O my soul, and save those who hymn Thee!”`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Matins, aposticha Glory/Both-now closer`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:3}],type:`stavrotheotokion`,sourceLabel:`Stavrotheotokion`},closing_rubric:`Then, “It is good to give thanks ...,” Trisagion ..., Our Father ..., Troparia.`},sat:{sessionals:[{rubric:`st After the 1 chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymns of the holy martyrs, in Tone V:`,spec_mel:null,items:[{text:`Today the memorial of the passion-bearers shineth forth with radiance from the heavens; the choir of the angels keepeth festival, and the human race celebrateth with them. Wherefore, they pray unto the Lord, that our souls find mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, sessional set 1, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Through the miracles of Thy holy martyrs, O Christ God, Thou hast given us an indestructible rampart. By their supplications make steadfast Thy faithful peoples, in that Thou art good and the Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, sessional set 1, item 2`},label:`plain`}],verses:[{text:`Wondrous is God in His saints, * the God of Israel.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, sessional set 1 verse 1`}}],closer:{text:`Rejoice, impassible portal of the Lord! * Rejoice, rampart and protection of those who have recourse unto thee! * Rejoice, haven untouched by storms, * and who knowing not wedlock, * didst bear in the flesh thy Creator and God. * Cease not to intercede for those ** who praise and worship thine Offspring.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, sessional set 1 closer`},type:`theotokion`}},{rubric:`After the 2nd chanting of the Psalter, the Sessional Hymns, in Tone V:`,spec_mel:null,items:[{text:`Thy martyrs, O Lord, longing to drink from the cup of Thy sufferings; forsook the beauties of life, and shared in the life of the angels. By their intercessions, O Christ, grant peace and great mercy to our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, sessional set 2, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The hosts of heaven marveled exceedingly at the corrections of the holy martyrs; how, fighting the good fight in their mortal bodies, they invisibly vanquished the incorporeal foe by the power of the Cross; and they pray unto the Lord, that our souls find mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, sessional set 2, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`With the righteous grant rest, O our Savior, unto Thy servants, and settle them in Thy courts, as it hath been written, overlooking, in that Thou art good, all their transgressions, voluntary and involuntary, committed either knowingly and unknowingly, O Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, sessional set 2, item 3`},label:`for_the_reposed`}],verses:[{text:`Wondrous is God in His saints, * the God of Israel.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, sessional set 2 verse 1`}},{text:`Blessed are they whom Thou hast chosen and taken to Thyself, O Lord. * Their memorial is unto generation and generation.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, sessional set 2 verse 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}]}],closer:{text:`O Christ God, Who hath shone forth upon the world from the Virgin and shown us forth as children of the light: have mercy upon us!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, sessional set 2 closer`},type:`theotokion`}}],canons:[{title:`Canon of the holy martyrs, hierarchs, the venerable and the departed, the acrostic whereof is “I offer these hymns to Thy servants, O Christ,” the composition of Joseph, in Tone V`,heading_rubric:`Canon of the holy martyrs, hierarchs, the venerable and the departed, the acrostic whereof is “I offer these hymns to Thy servants, O Christ,” the composition of Joseph, in Tone V:`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`A land which the sun had never beheld, * and upon which it had never shined, * an abyss which the vault of heaven had not seen laid bare, * hath Israel traversed dry-shod, O Lord. * And Thou didst lead them to Thy mountain of sanctification, * as they sang and chanted * a hymn of victory.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Surrendering your bodies to arrogant judges, ye endured unbearable wounds, O valiant spiritual athletes, expecting to receive honors from on high; and Christ led you into the eternal mansions of those who rejoice and chant the hymn of victory.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The venerable and the righteous, and the holy hierarchs, fulfilling the right glorious precepts of God, pastured the people and guided them to the waters of understanding; and they have worthily received torrents of sweetness, pouring forth rivers of healing through grace.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Through the prayers of the most glorious prophets, of the most wise hierarchs, and of the sacred women who with manly mind endured mightily and trampled underfoot the enemy by fasting, guide me, O Lord - Who appeared on earth by divine grace, to the havens of Life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thee do we beseech, the God Who is easy to reconcile: Grant rest in the bosom of Abraham unto Thy servants whom Thou hast taken to Thyself from the turmoil of life, and grant unto them eternal light, overlooking their offenses, in that Thou art good.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 4`},label:[`glory`,`for_the_reposed`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., For the reposed:`},{text:`“Rejoice!”, I cry to thee who hast given birth to Joy, O all-hymned one. Enlighten our minds and souls, and guide all in the steps of understanding, and entreat thy Son and God, that He grant cleansing of transgressions unto all, O only Bride of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 1, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:[`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion:`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`Do Thou establish my heart, O Lord, * which is shaken by the billows of life, * and guide it to a calm haven, O God.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Ye spared not your bodies when they were beaten with staves and dismembered by the sword, O all-praised warrior martyrs, who were strengthened by the hope of everlasting- good things.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Ye enlightened the vesture of the hierarchy, shepherding the flock of Christ in the fields of life through the virtues.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Mortifying the flesh through asceticism, the venerable ones shared in divine life. By their sacred prayers, O Christ, deliver us from misfortunes.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Unto those who have fallen asleep grant heavenly rest, O Lover of mankind, remitting the debts they incurred upon earth, in that Thou art good.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:[`glory`,`for_the_reposed`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., For the reposed:`},{text:`As they beheld thee, who art blessed among women, the company of women suffered and were taken to thy Son, O Virgin Mother.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 3, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:[`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion:`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`I have heard Thy report, O Lord, * and I was afraid. * I came to knowledge of Thy dispensation, * and I glorified Thee, O only Lover of mankind.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`By Thy power, O Lord, the passion-bearers trampled underfoot the power of the enemy, and became the might and great confirmation of the faithful.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`All the venerable now rejoice with great joy, and the divine priests are clothed in righteousness as in a garment.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Let us all hymn the divinely eloquent prophets of God, and let us honor the company of women who ran well the good race.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Guiding to the harbor of Thy kingdom those whom Thou hast taken from the tumult and tempest of this present life, O Master, grant them rest.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:[`glory`,`for_the_reposed`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., For the reposed:`},{text:`Through thee, O Virgin, the Timeless One hath now come under time. Him do thou entreat, that He free my soul from the transgressions I have committed in time.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 4, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:[`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion:`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Hasten Thou and have compassion on my wretched soul, * which doth battle at night * with the darkness of the passions. * Shine in me with the brightness of the day, * O noetic Sun, * and thereby make the night give way to light.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`The bones of the martyrs pour forth healing upon the infirm, for, unbroken by malice, they restore our broken state and grind to dust all the bones of ungodliness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`Observing Thy laws, the holy hierarchs shepherded the people and guided them to the life which is to come, O Compassionate One; and the venerable ones slew the tyranny of the passions with a perfect mind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Let the prophets be honored, and with them all who were righteous by faith; and let the divine women who lived in holiness and shone forth on earth through their torments be praised as servants of Christ.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`Thy faithful servants, whom Thou hast taken from earth, do Thou number in the mansions of heaven, overlooking their transgressions, O Christ Who in Thine exceeding goodness wast incarnate for the sake of us mortals.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:[`glory`,`for_the_reposed`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., For the reposed:`},{text:`We hymn thee, O Virgin , through whom God appeared to those who earth, becoming a man; and we cry aloud: Rejoice, O right fertile ground which produced the mystic Grain which feedeth every creature!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 5, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:[`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion:`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`Even as Thou didst deliver the prophet from the beast, O Lord, * so do Thou lead me up from the depths * of unrestrained passions, I pray Thee, * that I may dare * to look upon Thy holy temple.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Surrendering their bodies into the hands of the torturers to be wounded, the divine martyrs rejoiced in soul; for they truly beheld divine and everlasting joy and divine rewards.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Christ, Thou art the glory of the most wise holy hierarchs and the venerable. Through their supplications have pity on Thy people, whom Thou hast acquired by Thy blood, in that Thou lovest mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Illumined in mind by Thee, O Lord, the prophets clearly revealed things far distant as though they were close; and by Thy power women have destroyed the dominion of the enemy through suffering and fasting.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Numbering Thy faithful servants, who have departed from us, among the choirs of the elect, O good Lord, grant them rest, overlooking all their offenses in Thy loving-kindness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:[`glory`,`for_the_reposed`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., For the reposed:`},{text:`O Lord Who created Eve in the beginning, and entered the Virgin’s womb: Having clothed Thyself in the form of a servant Thou workest our restoration, O Master of all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 6, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:[`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion:`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The prayer of the Children quenched the fire * and the furnace which bedewed them proclaimed the miracle, * for it neither burned nor consumed those, * who chanted hymns unto the God of our Fathers.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Set aflame with the fire of cruel torments, O glorious martyrs, ye showed most fervent love for the Lord, which cooled you with the understanding of piety.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Having adorned yourselves with the wisdom of the Spirit, and lived splendid lives, ye performed the sacred acts of the grace of the Gospel; wherefore we praise you as ministers of God.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`O venerable ones, who mortified the flesh with many pangs, ye have been deemed worthy of the life to come, praying that we who have been slain by the assaults of the passions may receive it.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`With faith let the blessed choir of the prophets of God and the assembly of sacred women, who struggled in asceticism and by suffering cast down the enemy, be praised.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 4`},label:`plain`},{text:`O Word Who hast given a share in the life of all unto the dead, who have now left behind the turmoil of life: do Thou guide them to Thy divine haven, overlooking their offenses, O good One.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:[`glory`,`for_the_reposed`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., For the reposed:`},{text:`Let us, who with upright mind understand thee to be the Theotokos, be delivered by thy mediation from darkness and the invisible foes who wage war upon us, O Lady.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 7, item 6`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:[`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion:`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`O ye company of angels, * and assembly of mankind; * ye priests, Levites, and peoples: * praise, bless, and supremely exalt the King and Creator of all, * throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Navigating the deep of torments with the rudder of the Word, O spiritual athletes, ye drowned all the hordes of the deceiver in the outpouring of your blood, and live throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`As most wise sacred ministers, by the waters of Orthodoxy ye nurtured in a sacred manner the flock entrusted to you; and ye truly delight in the sweet torrents of beauty.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`Having done the works of light, O venerable ones, ye were revealed to the faithful as lamps, and have passed over to the divine Effulgence. Pray ye to the Master, that He free us from darkness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Be glad, O company of women who through wounds received the fullness of all honors! Rejoice forever, O choir of the prophets, and ye righteous who were pleasing unto Christ!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Grant, O Master, that Thy servants who have departed this life may without hindrance pass by the sword which is now withdrawn, causing them to dwell in paradise, in that Thou alone art merciful.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:[`glory`,`for_the_reposed`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., For the reposed:`},{text:`Let us hymn the joyous Virgin Mary as the gate leading to the divine entry, the easily mounted ladder of God, the unerring guide for those who seek salvation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 8, item 6`},label:[`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion:`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`For the mighty One hath done great things to thee, * in that He showed thee forth as a pure Virgin * even after giving birth, * since thou art she that hath seedlessly borne her own creator, * wherefore, O Theotokos, * we magnify thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Let the sacred ministers and pastors, the choir of the holy prophets, the countless multitude of the righteous and the assembly of the martyrs be blessed with sacred hymns, for they pray that our souls be saved.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 1`},label:`plain`},{text:`The wondrous council of the venerable, having struggled most wisely in asceticism, hath now been rendered wondrous by many displays of miracles. By their prayers, O wondrous Lord, show forth the wonder of Thy mercy upon all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`With faith and love let the countless multitude of women who suffered and fasted, and who abide with the angelic choirs, be blessed with the hieromartyrs who finished well the race.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`The multitudes of all the saints entreat Thee, O Word: In the magnitude of Thy mercy grant rest to the multitudes who with faith have passed from the earth, overlooking the offenses they committed during their life.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:[`glory`,`for_the_reposed`],sourceLabel:`Glory ..., For the reposed:`},{text:`In sickness of mind I committed many sins, O Virgin, and torment awaiteth me in the future. Deliver me from such, for I come to thee with an unwavering heart, and I call upon thy divine protection.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 1, Ode 9, item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:[`both_now`,`theotokion`],sourceLabel:`Both now ..., Theotokion:`}]}},acrostic:`I offer these hymns to Thy servants, O Christ`,composer:`Joseph`},{title:`Another canon, of the departed, chanted when no Menaion is available, the acrostic whereof is “The fifth canon of Theophanes for the reposed,” in Tone V`,heading_rubric:`Another canon, of the departed, chanted when no Menaion is available, the acrostic whereof is “The fifth canon of Theophanes for the reposed,” in Tone V:`,odes:{1:{irmos:{text:`Unto God the Savior * Who made His people pass dryshod through the sea, * but drowned Pharaoh with all his host, * unto Him alone let us sing: * For He hath been glorified.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1 irmos`}},items:[{text:`With divine love the passion-bearers of Christ trampled the pride of the tyrants underfoot; and with faith they ask prayerful remission and rest for the departed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 1`},label:`plain`,refrain:`Wondrous is God in His saints, the God of Israel.`},{text:`Cause the departed to dwell in Thy holy habitations and courts, O Christ Master, Who shed Thine exceedingly precious blood to redeem our debt.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1},{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic), in refrain`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,refrain:`Grant rest, O Lord, to the souls of Thy departed servants.`},{text:`The Wisdom of God, the Compassionate One Who beareth the express impress of the Father: Unto those whom Thou hast taken to Thyself grant rest, imparting everlasting blessedness unto them.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`O all-immaculate one, thou hast been shown to be the splendid tabernacle, the golden ark containing the divine Word Who assumed flesh for our sake, and destroyed the power of death.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 1, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},3:{irmos:{text:`Do Thou establish us O God our Savior, * by the might of Thy power, * and raise the horn of Thy Church, * that with right faith singeth praises unto Thee`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Struggling manfully, the spiritual athletes withstood the assaults of the tyrants; and they pray to Christ on behalf of those who have fallen asleep.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 1`},label:`plain`,refrain:`Wondrous is God in His saints, the God of Israel.`},{text:`Receiving in Thy splendid mansions those who were nurtured on Thy laws and have reposed, grant them rest, O good One.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1},{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic), in refrain`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,refrain:`Grant rest, O Lord, to the souls of Thy departed servants.`},{text:`O only merciful God, vouchsafe the splendors of the saints unto those whom Thou hast taken, overlooking their offenses.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`O pure one, we hymn thy birthgiving, whereby we have been delivered from the primal condemnation and curse and have been freed from death.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 3, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},4:{irmos:{text:`I have heard, O Lord, * of Thine arising from the tomb, * and have glorified * Thine invincible power.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Piously confessing Thee to be equally eternal with the Father, O Christ, the martyrs were slain; and they cry out to Thee: Deliver Thy servants, whom Thou hast taken to Thyself, O Christ!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`,refrain:`Wondrous is God in His saints, the God of Israel.`},{text:`As the only mortal free among the dead, O Christ, giving life everlasting to mortals grant rest to Thy departed servants.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1},{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic), in refrain`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,refrain:`Grant rest, O Lord, to the souls of Thy departed servants.`},{text:`O Christ Who camest to save the lost, grant a dwelling-place in paradise unto those departed in faith, O Thou Who dost justify man by grace.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`glory`},{text:`The power of the Most High overshadowed thee, O maiden, and made of thee a paradise of life, having the Lord and Mediator as a tree in thy midst.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 4, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},5:{irmos:{text:`Waking at dawn, * we cry unto Thee, O Lord: * Save us, for Thou art our God; * we know none other besides Thee.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Accepting the entreaties of the martyrs, O Lord, among the elect number the souls whom Thou hast received.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,refrain:`Wondrous is God in His saints, the God of Israel.`},{text:`Thou didst foretell that those who believe on Thee will not see death, O Master; wherefore, grant rest to the departed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1},{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic), in refrain`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,refrain:`Grant rest, O Lord, to the souls of Thy departed servants.`},{text:`Grant that Thy servants receive the beauty of Thy house, O Lord, and a share in delight.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`O Word Who art equally eternal with the Father and wast incarnate from the Virgin: Thou hast slain death by death..`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 5, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},6:{irmos:{text:`The abyss hath encompassed me, * the sea monster hath become my grave; * but I cried unto Thee, * the Lover of mankind, * and Thy right hand saved me, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6 irmos`}},items:[{text:`The army of Thy martyrs, likening themselves to the hosts on high, beseech Thee, O Christ: Unto those who have departed grant the bliss which cometh from Thee, O Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`,refrain:`Wondrous is God in His saints, the God of Israel.`},{text:`In that Thou lovest mankind, O Christ, number Thy servants, whom Thou hast taken to Thyself, in places of coolness, in places of the splendor of the saints, in places of ease.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1},{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic), in refrain`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,refrain:`Grant rest, O Lord, to the souls of Thy departed servants.`},{text:`Cleanse Thy servants, and grant them forgiveness offenses, O Lover of mankind; and grant unto them life incorruptible and a blessed inheritance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Who can recount in words the wonder of thy seedless conception, O all-immaculate one; for thou hast given birth unto God. Who came to us in His loving-kindness.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 6, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},7:{irmos:{text:`The children were saved * in the burning furnace, * chanting: Blessed art Thou * O God of our fathers.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7 irmos`}},items:[{text:`O Savior, grant that those who have departed may now partake of the unapproachable light, through the supplications of Thy passion-bearers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,refrain:`Wondrous is God in His saints, the God of Israel.`},{text:`O compassionate Christ, number among the Church of the firstborn those who have departed in faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1},{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic), in refrain`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,refrain:`Grant rest, O Lord, to the souls of Thy departed servants.`},{text:`O Savior, grant rest unto Thy servants who have departed unto Thee, adorning them with the raiment of incorruption.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Having conceived Life without seed, O all-immaculate one, thou didst staunch the flow of the essence of death.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 7, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},8:{irmos:{text:`The Son of God who before all ages * wast begotten of the Father * hath in these last times * become incarnate of the Virgin Mother, * O ye priests hymn, * and ye peoples supremely exalt Him throughout all ages.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8 irmos`}},items:[{text:`We hymn Thee, O Savior, Who dost accept the struggles of the holy martyrs, for their sake granting peace unto those who have departed in the Faith; let us supremely exalt Him throughout all ages!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,refrain:`Wondrous is God in His saints, the God of Israel.`},{text:`As Thou art compassionate, O Savior, grant that those who have departed from us may be illumined by the radiance of Thy heavenly glory, and hymn and exalt Thee supremely throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1},{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic), in refrain`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,refrain:`Grant rest, O Lord, to the souls of Thy departed servants.`},{text:`Reckon with the choirs of the saints those whom Thou hast taken to Thyself, O Savior, and number them with Lazarus in the bosom of Abraham, for they hymn and supremely exalt Thee throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Thou wast adorned with the beauty of purity, O Virgin Mother, becoming the habitation of the magnificence of the virtues; wherefore, we hymn and supremely exalt thee, the pure one, throughout all ages.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`},{text:`refrain: “More honorable than the cherubim ...,” and make prostrations.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 8, item 5`},label:`plain`}]},9:{irmos:{text:`O Thou who art God's Mother transcending mind and word, * who ineffably in time * hast given birth unto the Timeless One, * Thee do we the faithful magnify with one accord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9 irmos`}},items:[{text:`Having received rewards for their sacred sufferings, the martyrs now beseech Thee to grant remission unto those who have departed in faith, O Savior.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,refrain:`Wondrous is God in His saints, the God of Israel.`},{text:`Thou didst endure death, O only immortal Savior, granting resurrection and the radiance of immortality unto the dead, in that Thou art compassionate.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1},{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic), in refrain`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`,refrain:`Grant rest, O Lord, to the souls of Thy departed servants.`},{text:`Thou didst set us aright who have fallen into death, and didst teach us to hope for everlasting life, which do Thou grant unto Thy servants.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 3`},label:`glory`},{text:`The shadows of the Law have passed away at thy birthgiving, O Theotokos; truth hath shone forth, and grace hath been bestowed; wherefore, we magnify thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, canon 2, Ode 9, item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]}},condition:`which we chant when there is no Menaion`,acrostic:`The fifth canon of Theophanes for the reposed`}],magnificat_rubric:`We then chant the hymn of the Theotokos (the Magnificat), with the`,post_canon_rubric:`Then, “It is truly meet to bless thee ...,” and a prostration. Small litany, Exapostilarion, and the usual psalms. On the Praises, these Stichera of the holy martyrs, in Tone V:`,praises:{rubric:`On the Praises, these Stichera of the holy martyrs, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`Blessed is the army of the heavenly King: for though the passion-bearers were born of this earth, spurning the pangs of their bodies they hastened to attain to the dignity of the angels; and through their sufferings were deemed worthy of the honour of the incorporeal hosts. By their prayers, O Lord, send down upon us great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, Praises item 1`},label:`martyrs`},{text:`Thy passion-bearers, O Lord, emulating the life of the angelic ranks; endured tortures as though incorporeal, in oneness of mind possessing the hope of the blessings promised them. By their intercessions, O Christ God, grant peace to Thy world, and great mercy to our souls.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, Praises item 2`},label:`plain`},{text:`The holy martyrs struggled here on earth, enduring cold and given over to fire and water. And as the waters received them, they cried aloud: “We went through fire and water, and Thou didst bring us out into refreshment!” By their prayers, O Christ God, have mercy upon us!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, Praises item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Rejoicing in the midst of their torments, the saints cried aloud: “These things are goods with which we may trade with the Lord: for, instead of the wounds we bear on our bodies, radiant vesture shall blossom forth for us upon our resurrection; instead of dishonor, we shall receive crowns; instead of fetters in prison, we shall receive paradise; and instead of condemnation with malefactors, we shall have life with the angels!” By their supplications, O Lord, save Thou our souls!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, Praises item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thou hast fashioned me, O Lord, and set Thine hand upon me; and Thou hast commanded me, saying; ‘To the earth shalt thou return once more.’ Guide me on Thy right path, forgive me my transgressions, and absolve and save me, I pray Thee, O Lover of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, Praises item 5`},label:`for_the_reposed`}],verses:[{text:`Praise Him for His mighty acts, * praise Him according to the multitude of His greatness.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, Praises verse 1`}},{text:`Praise Him with the sound of trumpet, * praise Him with the psaltery and harp.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, Praises verse 2`}},{text:`Praise Him with timbrel and dance, * praise Him with strings and flute.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, Praises verse 3`}},{text:`Praise Him with tuneful cymbals, praise Him with cymbals of jubilation. * Let every breath praise the Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, Praises verse 4`}}],theotokion:{text:`Alas, O wretched soul! What answer wilt thou have to give to the Judge at that hour when the thrones are set for judgment and the Judge descendeth from the heavens, with myriads of angels? When He is seated upon the judgment seat to try His unprofitable servants like me, what shalt thou bring forth then? Truly naught, having defiled thy mind and body, wherefore, fall down before the Virgin, and cry without ceasing, that she grant thee abundant forgiveness of sins!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, Praises Glory/Both-now Theotokion`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Glory ..., Both now ..., Theotokion:`},doxology_rubric:`Small Doxology (Read), Litany: Let us complete ...,`},aposticha:{rubric:`On the Aposticha, these Stichera of the departed, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`With the light of Thy countenance, O Christ, enlighten those who have departed, as Thou art compassionate, and lead them to a place of verdure, beside the waters of Thy pure divine repose. In the longed for bosom of our forefather Abraham, where Thy light shineth in purity, and the springs of love ever pour forth, where the assemblies of all the righteous rejoice and exult in Thy goodness. Number Thy servants with them, and grant them great mercy. ‘`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, aposticha of the departed, item 1`},label:`plain`,spec_mel:`Rejoice`},{text:`O Compassionate One, be Thou well-pleased to grant those who have passed from transitory things unto Thee, the Master of all and our God, all-harmonious voices to hymn and glorify Thy might; and grant that they may be enlightened by Thy beauty, and in a most pure manner partake of sweet and beauteous communion with Thee, where the angels rejoice around Thy throne and the choirs of the saints joyously stand round about. Grant rest with them and great mercy unto Thy servants.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, aposticha of the departed, item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Unto those who have fallen asleep in faith, grant rest with the choir of the prophets, with the ranks of the apostles and the martyrs, and with all those who from time immemorial, have been justified by Thy redeeming Passion and Thy Blood, by which Thou hast ransomed captive mankind. In Thy love forgive them all their offences, for Thou alone hast lived a sinless life upon the earth, Thou alone art holy, Thou alone art free among the dead. Therefore grant unto Thy servants rest and great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, aposticha of the departed, item 3`},label:`plain`}],verses:[{text:`Blessed are they whom Thou hast chosen * and taken to Thyself, O Lord.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins aposticha of the departed, verse 1 — pointed, "they", final period (§5 per-tone; the 4-7 pattern)`}},{text:`Their souls * shall dwell among good things.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins aposticha of the departed, verse 2 — tone 5 prints TWO verses where 2-7/3-7 carry three (§5 structural per-tone set)`}}]},aposticha_theotokion:{text:`Having conceived Christ the King and Bestower of life, we who were enslaved by the law of sin, O Lady, have been set free, O only Virgin Mother. Through Him we are freely justified by grace. Entreat Him now to write into the book of life, the names of those who acknowledge thee to be the Birthgiver of God; that saved by Thy mediation, we may receive from Thy Son redemption, worshipping Him Who granteth the world great mercy.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Matins, aposticha Glory/Both-now closer`},type:`theotokion`,sourceLabel:`Theotokion`},closing_rubric:`Then, “It is good to give thanks ...,” Trisagion ..., Our Father ..., Troparia.`}},liturgy_weekday:{mon:{beatitudes:{rubric:`On the Beatitudes, these Troparia, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`Believing Thee to be God, the thief on the cross confessed Thee, O Christ, in purity from the depths of his heart, crying out: Remember me, O Lord, in Thy kingdom!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`I have met with soul-corrupting thieves on the path of life, and they have wounded me. But now I flee to thy loving-kindness, O Christ. Heal and save me, I pray.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`The choirs of heaven hymn Thee, the God of all. By their sacred mediation overlook my many evils, O Master, and save me, I pray.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Having joined the angelic choirs, and been filled with never- waning light, O spiritual athletes of Christ, dispel ye the fetid passions of my heart.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`O ye mortals, unto God Who is hymned by the angels in the highest let us chant the thrice-holy hymn: Holy art Thou, O beginningless Father, Son and Spirit!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`glory`},{text:`O pure one who received the Joy of the angels in thy womb, fill with joy my soul, which hath been downcast by mine evil deeds, and guide it to the light.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-2.pdf`,locus:`Monday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 6`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},prokeimenon:{ref:`shared.daily_liturgy_propers.mon.prokeimenon`},alleluia:{ref:`shared.daily_liturgy_propers.mon.alleluia`},communion:{ref:`shared.daily_liturgy_propers.mon.communion`}},tue:{beatitudes:{rubric:`On the Beatitudes, these Troparia, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`Believing Thee to be God, the thief on the cross confessed Thee, O Christ, crying out in purity from the depths of his heart: Remember me, O Lord, in Thy kingdom!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`As Thou didst justify the harlot who wept from the depths of her soul, O Christ, so do Thou rescue me from all torment, for I am in despair, O good Master, I entreat Thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Together let us bless John, who went before Christ and prepared His goodly ways, that through his divine supplications we may be delivered from transgressions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 3`},label:`plain`},{text:`O holy martyrs, who drained the cup of Christ with a fervent soul: With the downpour of your divine prayers deliver us from turbid sins and ailments.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`O unapproachable God, almighty Trinity and Unity: By the supplications of Thy Forerunner save me, delivering me from darkness and the flame which awaiteth me.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`Ever defiled by wicked acts, I beseech thee, the undefiled Mother of the Master: Cleanse me of all defilement, O Lady!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-3.pdf`,locus:`Tuesday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 6`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},prokeimenon:{ref:`shared.daily_liturgy_propers.tue.prokeimenon`},alleluia:{ref:`shared.daily_liturgy_propers.tue.alleluia`},communion:{ref:`shared.daily_liturgy_propers.tue.communion`}},wed:{beatitudes:{rubric:`On the Beatitudes, these Troparia, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`Believing Thee to be God, the thief on the cross confessed Thee, O Christ, crying out in purity from the depths of his heart: Remember me, O Lord, in Thy kingdom!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Pierced in the side, Thou didst pour forth torrents of remission, O Christ; and, Thy hands nailed to the Cross, Thou didst discomfit all the passionate mind of mankind.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Ascending the Cross, Thou didst fill the whole multitude of the demons with trembling, didst cast down the pernicious might of the tyrant, O Christ our Master, and didst save humanity.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`As emulators of the sufferings of Christ, O blessed passion- bearers of the Lord, ye underwent every torture; wherefore, ye have been vouchsafed the beauties of heaven.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`On the Cross Thou didst endure voluntary suffering, O Christ Who art inseparable from the Father and the divine Spirit, taking away all our corrupting passions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`She who stood before the Cross and beheld her Son wounded, was wounded in soul and hymned His truly great dispensation.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-4.pdf`,locus:`Wednesday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 6`},label:`both_now`}]},prokeimenon:{ref:`shared.daily_liturgy_propers.wed.prokeimenon`},alleluia:{ref:`shared.daily_liturgy_propers.wed.alleluia`},communion:{ref:`shared.daily_liturgy_propers.wed.communion`}},thu:{beatitudes:{rubric:`On the Beatitudes, these Troparia, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`Believing Thee to be God, the thief on the cross confessed Thee, O Christ, crying out in purity from the depths of his heart: Remember me, O Lord, in Thy kingdom!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Like radiant clouds ye traversed the earth, O divine disciples, letting fall the water of life; and ye give drink in abundance to hearts withering away through transgressions.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`As mystic rays of the Sun Who shone forth from the pure Virgin, O divine disciples of Christ our God, ye have enlightened those who sit in the darkness of ignorance.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`That Thou mightest recover the coin buried in the abyss of transgressions, O Christ, and bring it to the Father, through the divine Spirit Thou didst ordain the apostles as preachers.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Enduring the burning of cruel tortures, O most wise ones, ye burned up the falsehood of the idols and have passed over to divine consolation, O saints.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`O supremely divine Trinity, single Godhead - beginningless Father, Son Who art equally without beginning, and Holy Spirit - Preserve Thy Church through the supplications of all who preach Thee!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 6`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`O divinely joyous one, adornment of the apostles: With rays of repentance enlighten me who am darkened by the pleasures of life, that I may magnify thee.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 7`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`both_now`}]},prokeimenon:{tone:8,text:{text:`Their sound hath gone forth into all the earth, * and their words unto the ends of the world.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Liturgy prokeimenon (text byte-matches shared; stored per-tone beside its divergent verse)`}},verse:{text:`The heavens declare the glory of God, * and the firmament proclaimeth the work of His hands.`,tier:2,src:{file:`5-5.pdf`,locus:`Thursday Liturgy prokeimenon verse — prints a * pointing mark absent from the 2-5/shared print (§5 divergence; 4-5 printed the same mark)`}}},alleluia:{ref:`shared.daily_liturgy_propers.thu.alleluia`},communion:{ref:`shared.daily_liturgy_propers.thu.communion`},alleluia_note:`5-5 prints the digit-zero artifact ("0 Lord") at the same verse as 2-5/3-5/4-5 — four tones running; normalized per §9.10 (scan review delivered); post-normalization the print byte-matches shared, so the ref stands.`},fri:{beatitudes:{rubric:`On the Beatitudes, these Troparia, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`Believing Thee to be God, the thief on the cross confessed Thee, O Christ, crying out in purity from the depths of his heart: Remember me, O Lord, in Thy kingdom!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Dying on the Cross, O compassionate Bestower of life, Thou gavest life unto Adam, upon whom death had come through eating, and Thou didst show him to be a dweller in paradise, O good One.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Thou wast nailed to the Cross, O Christ, Thou true vine, and hast poured forth the fluid of salvation, giving drink through grace unto the hearts of all the faithful.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`When ye were beaten and dismembered, O wise ones, ye emulated the sacrifice of the Master; wherefore, ye are ever called blessed, O martyrs of Christ.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`martyrs`},{text:`With faith we worship Thee, the one God in three Hypostases, the indivisible and supremely divine Essence; and we cry out to Thee: Glory be to Thee, O Trinity and Unity, our God!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`She who beheld our Life dead of His own will upon the tree of the Cross, beat her breast, weeping; wherefore, we all ever bless her with divine voices.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-6.pdf`,locus:`Friday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 6`},label:`both_now`}]},prokeimenon:{ref:`shared.daily_liturgy_propers.fri.prokeimenon`},alleluia:{ref:`shared.daily_liturgy_propers.fri.alleluia`},communion:{ref:`shared.daily_liturgy_propers.fri.communion`}},sat:{beatitudes:{rubric:`On the Beatitudes, these Troparia, in Tone V:`,items:[{text:`Believing Thee to be God, the thief on the cross confessed Thee, O Christ, crying out in purity from the depths of his heart: Remember me, O Lord, in Thy kingdom!`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 1`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`Dying, O martyrs, ye destroyed the enemy, the author of evil, and, crowned with divine victories, ye mounted on high, where ye stand before God, the King of all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 2`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Illumined by the light of the priesthood, O holy hierarchs, ye were glorified; and the multitude of the venerable have received life everlasting. Wherefore, they are blessed.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 3`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`plain`},{text:`Those whom Thou hast taken to Thyself, O Master, do Thou cause to dwell with the choirs of the elect in a place of ease, O Christ the Word, overlooking the offenses they committed on earth.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 4`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`plain`},{text:`O adored Trinity, be Thou entreated by the struggles of the holy hierarchs and honored martyrs; and grant salvation and great mercy unto the souls of those who departed in faith.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 5`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:1}],label:`glory`},{text:`O divinely joyous one, thou didst contain Him Whom naught can contain. Having given birth to Him in a manner transcending nature and all telling, beseech Him, O Lady, to be merciful unto all.`,tier:1,src:{file:`5-7.pdf`,locus:`Saturday Liturgy, Beatitudes item 6`},homoglyph_log:[{from:`U+041E О (Cyrillic)`,to:`O`,count:2}],label:`both_now`}]},prokeimenon:{ref:`shared.daily_liturgy_propers.sat.prokeimenon`},alleluia:{ref:`shared.daily_liturgy_propers.sat.alleluia`},communion:{ref:`shared.daily_liturgy_propers.sat.communion`}}}};export{e as default};